# Правила работы ИИ-агентов: polytropos-alpha

Этот документ обязателен для любого ИИ-агента, который изменяет репозиторий. Он распространяется на корень и все вложенные каталоги. **`AGENTS.md` в корне — единственный источник инструкций агентам проекта.** Дублирующие файлы правил не создавать.

## Назначение и границы проекта

- Разрабатываем **VeriNeural**: архитектурно-нейтральную импортируемую Rust-библиотеку, в которой пользователь определяет математические операции и контракты, собирает вложенные модули и архитектуры, а единый Semantic Neural IR служит источником для NVIDIA GPU-кода, Lean 4-моделей и проверяемых артефактов.
- VeriNeural **не является готовой LLM**. Не создавать обязательные Transformer/Attention/MHA/GQA, KV Cache, MoE, tokenizer, serving/API, обучение, распределённую инфраструктуру или деплой. Исследовательские архитектуры принадлежат потребителям библиотеки, а не её ядру.
- **`docs/verineural/SPEC.md`** описывает конечные требования; **`docs/verineural/ROADMAP.md`** задаёт этапы и критерии приёмки. Фактически реализованные интерфейсы проверять по исходному коду и Taskfile. Не выдавать целевую спецификацию за уже работающую функцию.
- **Этот `AGENTS.md` содержит только постоянные правила для агентов, а не журнал разработки.** Запрещено добавлять сюда хронологию этапов, коммитов, результаты тестов, benchmark, SHA-256 манифесты, отчёты о проверках и текущие временные статусы. Изменять файл лишь при изменении самих правил.

## Конечная цель проекта: сильная рекуррентная LLM с дисковой латентной памятью

Это **постоянная архитектурная цель polytropos-alpha**, а не обещание достигнутого качества. Нельзя подменять её созданием энциклопедии внутри весов или преждевременной разработкой интеграций.

- **Первый приоритет — интеллектуально сильное ядро.** Создать компактную, крайне эффективную **рекуррентную LLM**, которая самостоятельно решает сложные математические, химические и другие задачи, требующие многошаговых рассуждений, обобщения и переноса навыков. Качество решения новых задач, способность строить и проверять выводы важнее механического запоминания фактов. Исследовательский ориентир по полезным интеллектуальным способностям — **Qwen3.8 27B**; сопоставимость не заявлять без отдельных воспроизводимых тестов.
- **Размер весов ядра — целевые 3–4 GB.** Это верхний целевой диапазон *хранимых параметров модели*, без дисковой латентной памяти. Основная аппаратная граница — **одна NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5060 с 8 GB VRAM**, на которой должно быть возможно **обучение**, а не только inference. Размер весов не равен полному расходу VRAM: отдельно учитывать пик активаций, градиентов, состояний оптимизатора, временных буферов и CUDA. Никаких фиктивных заявлений о выполнимости обучения без замеров.
- **Крайне высокая обучаемость.** Приоритетны sample efficiency, стабильность сложных рассуждений, скорость обучения, пропускная способность и время до заданного качества при реальном аппаратном бюджете. Сравнения проводить на одинаковых задачах и бюджетах данных/вычислений, а не только по скорости одного CUDA kernel.
- **Минимум универсального знания внутри ядра.** Ядро должно сохранять базовые понятия, математические/логические навыки, способы решения задач, обобщающие связи и способность адресовать нужные сведения. Большой объём частных фактов, деталей и специализированных знаний должен быть **вынесен во внешнюю латентную память**, а не обязательно закодирован в весах.
- **Обучаемое разделение знаний, а не ручная разметка.** **Во время обучения сама модель должна определять**, какие сведения критично оставить в весах, а какие сохранить или обновить во внешней памяти. Целевой ориентир — **около 20% базовых/связующих знаний в ядре и 80% расширяемых знаний во внешней памяти**. Это доли *полезного содержания/функций памяти*, а **не** строгая доля параметров, байтов, обучающих токенов или заранее доказанный коэффициент. Нужны измеримые критерии удержания навыков, качества извлечения, ошибок переноса и потери информации.
- **Связность важнее простого разбиения 20/80.** Оставшиеся в ядре общие знания должны быть достаточными для понимания задачи, выбора нужной области памяти, извлечения релевантных подробностей, объединения нескольких фрагментов и вывода ответа. Нельзя получить «умную» модель простым удалением 80% данных без механизма обучения извлечению и интеграции.
- **Внешняя латентная память — на диске, не в VRAM.** Хранить расширяемые иерархические представления и факты в дисковом хранилище без требования целиком загружать, копировать или постоянно кешировать эту базу на GPU. **В VRAM находится активная модель и необходимое для её вычислений ограниченное рабочее состояние**, но не вся внешняя база знаний. При запросе поднимать с диска **только адресованные регионы** в ограниченные CPU/передаточные буферы и предоставлять модели лишь необходимое содержимое/представление в рамках её входа и вычислений. Не маскировать массовую загрузку внешней базы «памятью модели».
- **Масштабируемая и обучаемая дисковая память.** Её ёмкость **не должна ограничиваться объёмом VRAM или размером весов**; она должна расширяться по мере накопления знаний и допускать эффективные добавление, обновление, организацию и поиск. «Неограниченная» здесь означает отсутствие *архитектурного фиксированного лимита*, но реальная ёмкость, I/O, скорость поиска и место на диске конечны и измеряются отдельно.
- **Иерархическая адресация и выбор глубины.** Кластеризовать знания по областям и уровням детализации. Рекуррентное ядро само выбирает регион, ветвь и нужную глубину, при необходимости уточняя запрос: например, «базы данных» (уровень 0) → «PostgreSQL» (1) → «SQL» → «как работает SELECT» (уровень *x*). Не загружать все кластеры в контекст и не закреплять постоянную глубину поиска.
- **Текущий этап без внешних адаптеров.** Не планировать и не реализовывать пока сетевые коннекторы, web-поиск, Wiki API и другие внешние сервисные адаптеры. Источник знаний на данном этапе — **собственная локальная дисковая латентная память**, с которой ядро учится работать непосредственно. К интеграциям возвращаться только после сильного базового reasoning и подтверждённого обучаемого распределения знаний.
- **Вращающиеся матрицы** исследуются как способ уменьшения памяти параметров ориентировочно **в 10–100 раз** с максимально возможным сохранением качества, устойчивости и скорости обучения. Это гипотеза, а не достигнутый результат: проверять число весов, размер checkpoint, цену вычислений и деградацию на серьёзных задачах.
- **Приёмка по этапам:** (1) способность ядра решать сложные задачи без внешней памяти; (2) обучаемое решение «оставить внутри / выгрузить на диск» и сохранение качества рассуждений; (3) адресное и иерархическое извлечение из дисковой памяти с измеренными задержками/ошибками; (4) обучение на RTX 5060 8 GB и проверка предела 3–4 GB весов; (5) сравнение с крупной эталонной моделью. Проверять отдельно качество **без памяти и с памятью**, а также вклад памяти, не приписывая внешние факты внутренним параметрам.

**Граница ответственности сохраняется:** `crates/verineural/` предоставляет архитектурно-нейтральные примитивы, состояние, контракты, Semantic IR, GPU lowering и Lean-верификацию. Конкретные рекуррентные блоки LLM, алгоритм обучаемой маршрутизации знаний, дисковая латентная память и обучение принадлежат **`labs/` как потребителям публичного API**. Если не хватает общего примитива, сначала расширять универсальную библиотеку, не встраивая в неё готовую предметную LLM.

## Rust workspace, Nix и Task

1. **Rust только через Cargo workspaces.** Корневой `Cargo.toml` задаёт workspace. Переиспользуемые библиотечные/инструментальные компоненты добавлять в `crates/`; конкретные исследовательские consumer-архитектуры допускаются в `labs/<architecture-name>-<version>/` и при появлении Rust package включаются в тот же workspace. Не переносить lab-specific нейросеть в `crates/verineural/`. Зависимости должны быть явными; не создавать циклов.
2. **В корне обязателен `flake.nix`.** Все необходимые инструменты разработки и генерации артефактов (Rust, LLVM/NVPTX, Lean 4, CUDA toolkit, Task и другие при расширении проекта) должны быть описаны в Nix. При добавлении обязательной зависимости актуализировать `flake.nix`. Драйвер NVIDIA остаётся системной предпосылкой, а не зависимостью, автоматически устанавливаемой в devShell.
3. **Команды определять и документировать в корневом `Taskfile.yml` (go-task).** Для сборки, форматирования, проверки, тестов, генерации кода и сертификатов использовать `task <имя>`; не вводить параллельный набор Makefile, shell-скриптов и разрозненных инструкций. `task check` обязан сначала выполнять `task prepare` (Rust autoformat), затем `cargo check`; при успешной проверке он может автоматически коммитить и отправлять **только новые изменения форматирования отслеживаемых Rust-файлов** в `dev`, если до запуска не было изменений `.rs` или staged-файлов и `HEAD` совпадает с `origin/dev`. Существующие пользовательские правки не отправлять автоматически.
4. **По умолчанию ИИ-агент НЕ запускает большинство команд**: `task build`, `task check`, `task test`, `task clippy`, `task doc`, тяжёлые `nix develop`/`nix flake check` и GPU-прогоны. Пользователь самостоятельно тестирует и собирает проект локально. Выполнять такие команды только по его **явному запросу**. Допустимы лёгкое чтение файлов и локальные статические проверки структуры; о непроверенном состоянии сообщать прямо.
5. Не устанавливать инструменты глобально, не обходить Nix непрозрачными установщиками, не изменять пользовательское окружение.
6. `Cargo.lock` и `flake.lock` при их появлении сохранять для воспроизводимости; не игнорировать. Не утверждать, что окружение зафиксировано, пока lock-файл отсутствует.

## Обязательное использование VeriNeural в лабораториях

- **При разработке нейросети или исследовательской архитектуры в `labs/` обязательно использовать публичный API библиотеки VeriNeural** для определения вычислительных примитивов, контрактов, модулей, связей, Semantic Neural IR, генерации NVIDIA GPU-кода и Lean-моделей/доказательств в пределах поддерживаемого профиля. Лаборатория должна быть потребителем библиотеки, а не параллельной реализацией её вычислительного и верификационного стека.
- **Если для лабораторной архитектуры не хватает возможностей VeriNeural, сначала расширить библиотеку универсальными, архитектурно-нейтральными строительными блоками в `crates/verineural/`**, а не реализацией требуемого конечного компонента. Разрабатывать минимально необходимые переиспользуемые примитивы, операции над тензорами и состоянием, интерфейсы композиции и контракты; при необходимости доводить их через Semantic Neural IR до поддерживаемых GPU/Lean backend-путей, тестов и явно ограниченных доказательств. Затем **собирать специализированный компонент из этих примитивов внутри `labs/`**. Не обходить ограничения библиотеки отдельными лабораторными CUDA kernels, генераторами Lean, скрытыми операциями или собственным несовместимым IR.
- **Граница абстракции обязательна:** VeriNeural предоставляет элементарные и составляемые механизмы, пригодные для разных архитектур, но **не содержит готовых предметно-специфичных компонентов**, даже если они нужны текущей лаборатории. Например, **KV-кэш реализуется только в лаборатории**; библиотека при необходимости расширяется общими примитивами хранения и обновления состояния, индексного чтения/записи, работы с формами и зависимостями, из которых потребитель может построить KV-кэш, другие виды памяти или совершенно иной алгоритм. Нельзя добавлять в ядро типы, API или семантику, жёстко завязанные на ключи/значения Attention, KV-кэш либо другую частную модель.
- В `labs/` оставлять специфичные для эксперимента определения архитектуры, специализированные составные компоненты, их композицию, конфигурацию, данные, сценарии запуска, независимые тестовые оракулы и исследовательские результаты. **Не переносить готовую конкретную нейросеть или её прикладные блоки в ядро VeriNeural**: расширять только универсальный набор операций и контрактов, достаточный, чтобы потребитель сам собрал нужный сложный компонент.
- При отсутствии доказанного lowering или математической гарантии расширять поддерживаемый профиль с отдельной проверкой либо **явно завершать неподдерживаемый этап ошибкой**. Не выдавать лабораторный обходной путь, численное совпадение или Lean-доказательство идеальной модели за сертификацию NVIDIA FP32/SASS.

## Git: разработка только в `dev`

- **Единственная рабочая ветка — `dev`.** Все изменения исходников, тестов и документации коммитить непосредственно в неё. **Не создавать** `agent/*`, `feature/*`, временные или отдельные ветки под исправления и этапы. Не спамить ветками.
- **Не коммитить напрямую в `main`.** `main` — ветка стабильной интеграции. Перенос изменений из `dev` в `main` возможен **только по явному запросу пользователя** и только fast-forward с проверкой предка; никакого автоматического продвижения.
- Перед записью в `dev` проверять её актуальный HEAD и ancestry нового коммита. При расхождении сначала синхронизироваться без merge-коммитов; не переписывать историю. При GitHub API обновлять `refs/heads/dev` исключительно с `force=false`, `expected_sha` и повторной проверкой HEAD.
- **Никаких pull request**, draft PR, PR merge, squash merge, rebase merge, merge-коммитов, force push и принудительных перемещений refs. Не удалять чужие или существующие ветки без явного разрешения пользователя.
- После изменения кратко сообщать SHA коммита в `dev`, сущность изменений и реальный статус проверок, не записывая эти сведения в `AGENTS.md`.

## Запрет на самовольную инфраструктуру

**Без предварительного явного разрешения пользователя ЗАПРЕЩЕНО добавлять или изменять:**
- CI/CD, GitHub Actions (`.github/workflows/`), другие пайплайны;
- автоматические pre-commit hooks, git hooks, ботов, cron/scheduled tasks;
- контейнеризацию, удалённые среды, деплой, release automation, новые внешние сервисы;
- вспомогательную инфраструктуру проверки, мониторинга и публикации ради самой инфраструктуры.

Не подменять этот запрет аргументом «так принято в индустрии». Если инфраструктура действительно понадобится, сначала объяснить её цель и попросить разрешение.

## Принципы разработки (обязательны)

- **KISS**: самая простая реализация, которая даёт требуемую функциональность. Никаких фреймворков и слоёв абстракции «на вырост».
- **DRY**: один источник правды для контрактов, семантики и конфигурации; не дублировать одну и ту же математическую логику между backend'ами.
- **Pragmatic Engineering**: оптимизировать полезный результат, понятность и время реализации; конкретный работающий вертикальный срез ценнее теоретически идеального, но незавершённого дизайна.
- **Risk-based Verification**: усилия на доказательства направлять туда, где ошибка наиболее опасна: формы, границы индексов, память, численная семантика, корректность трансформаций и отчёт о гарантии.
- **Modular Verification**: небольшие проверяемые примитивы, локальные контракты, повторно используемые леммы и композиция доказательств. Не начинать с монолитного доказательства всей нейросети; затем реализовать численно осведомлённую композицию контрактов.

## Темп работы и масштаб изменений

- Проект **любительский**. Планировать **крупные содержательные этапы** с чётким работающим артефактом и критерием завершения. Не дробить одну фичу на десятки мелких коммитов/«рефакторингов ради рефакторинга» и не расходовать три дня на косметику.
- Предпочитать end-to-end вертикальные срезы: пользовательский Rust API → IR → GPU либо Lean → явный отчёт. Не создавать неподключённые заготовки.
- При выборе между широтой поддержки и глубиной гарантий сужать поддерживаемое подмножество, а не преувеличивать корректность.
- Новые зависимости, функции и модули добавлять по мере фактической необходимости. Не опережать этапы дорожной карты без конкретного запроса.

## Обязательная модель CUDA-исполнения: CUDA Graph + Kernel Fusion

- **Строго запрещены CUDA Legacy Streams**: `CU_STREAM_LEGACY`, NULL/default stream (`stream = 0`) в CUDA runtime/Driver API, а также неявный fallback на legacy/per-thread default streams. Не передавать `nullptr` / `ptr::null_mut()` вместо потока при запуске kernels, копировании или синхронизации.
- **Все вычислительные kernels исполнять через CUDA Graph**, построенный из зависимостей Semantic Neural IR: захват на явно созданном `CU_STREAM_NON_BLOCKING` либо явное построение kernel-узлов графа. Сборка графа, его инстанцирование и `cuGraphLaunch` должны использовать реальные CUDA Graph API. Запуск отдельного kernel через `cuLaunchKernel` вне построения CUDA Graph запрещён.
- **Kernel Fusion является основным механизмом GPU-оптимизации**: объединять совместимые операции, не нарушая потребителей IR, зависимостей, контрактов, порядка вычислений и FP32-политики. Нельзя навязывать fusion любому произвольному подграфу без проверки предпосылок.
- Передача данных и синхронизация выполняются на **явном non-blocking stream**, без legacy/default-stream-семантики. Для async transfer использовать корректно живущую до завершения операции закреплённую host-memory (pinned memory).
- Если требуемые CUDA Graph API / `CU_STREAM_NON_BLOCKING` недоступны, **fail-closed**, без старого пути прямых запусков и без запуска на legacy stream. Зависимости CUDA Graph должны определяться IR и профилем исполнения, а не готовой архитектурой Transformer.
- Lean-доказательство математической fusion-леммы не означает доказательства CUDA Graph, FP32, PTX, JIT или исполнения аппаратурой. Статус этих гарантий всегда отражается отдельно.

## Формальная верификация и честность отчётов

- Источник математических требований — явный Rust-контракт или семантика доверенного примитива; генератор не придумывает корректность новой математики.
- В certified-режиме запрещены `sorry`, `admit`, непроверенные аксиомы и неподтверждённые допущения. Недоказанная цель означает провал нужного уровня сертификации.
- Точно различать: **формально доказано в Lean**, **численно проверено запуском**, **принято как доверенное предположение (TCB)**, **не поддерживается/не доказано**.
- Нельзя утверждать, что доказано исполнение машинного кода, если не доказана связь GPU IR → LLVM IR → PTX → SASS/железо; явно описывать доверенную границу.
- Strict FP32 требует явной обработки rounding, FMA, FTZ/денормалов, NaN/Infinity, signed zero и порядка редукции. Fast-math не включать неявно.
- Экспериментальные GPU-оптимизации отделять от доказанно эквивалентных преобразований. Лемма Lean об идеальной `Int`-семантике не доказывает эквивалентность LLVM/PTX/FP32 и не разрешает выдавать фьюжн за сертифицированную численную оптимизацию.
- Изменения оптимизирующих проходов в certified-режиме допустимы только с правилом сохранения семантики или сертифицированной оценкой ошибки.
- Нейросетевые свойства обучения, сходимости и качества не следует автоматически из корректности forward pass.
- **Теорема о локальном блоке не равна теореме о всей архитектуре.** Глобальное свойство требует формальной постановки, проверенных условий применения локальных лемм и отдельной композиционной проверки. Формирование Lean-файла и численная валидация GPU не доказывают произвольный алгоритм, IEEE-754 или машинный код.

## Порядок работы агента

1. Читать корневой `AGENTS.md`, `docs/verineural/SPEC.md` и `docs/verineural/ROADMAP.md` перед изменениями VeriNeural.
2. Сначала проверять текущую структуру и этап. Делать только нужный для задачи вертикальный срез; не трогать архитектуру раньше времени.
3. Обновлять документацию и Taskfile только при реальном изменении API/команд.
4. По завершении кратко перечислять изменённые файлы, реализованные и **нереализованные** возможности и факт запуска/незапуска тестов.
5. Не добавлять CI или инфраструктуру, не запускать массовые проверки без прямой санкции пользователя.

FILE	Cargo.toml
[workspace]
members = [
    "crates/verineural",
    "labs/coupled-field-0.1.0",
    "labs/xor-0.1.0",
    "labs/consumer-acceptance-0.1.0",
    "labs/rotating-matrices-0.1.0",
    "labs/torus16-mix-0.1.0",
]
resolver = "3"

[workspace.package]
version = "0.1.0"
edition = "2024"
rust-version = "1.85"

FILE	README.md
# polytropos-alpha

Исследовательский Rust-проект для разработки **интеллектуально сильной, компактной рекуррентной LLM**. Сначала ядро должно научиться самостоятельно решать сложные **математические, химические и логические задачи**. Затем во время обучения оно должно научиться решать, какие базовые знания и навыки оставить в параметрах, а какие сохранять во **внешней иерархической латентной памяти на диске**.

**Целевые ограничения (пока не достигнуты):** уровень полезных интеллектуальных возможностей выбранного ориентира Qwen3.8 27B, **3–4 GB весов ядра**, реальное обучение на **одной RTX 5060 с 8 GB VRAM**, высокая скорость и эффективность обучения. Вращающиеся матрицы исследуются как способ сжатия параметров в **10–100 раз** при контролируемой потере качества. Целевые характеристики должны быть подтверждены экспериментами.

**Принцип разделения знаний:** ориентир **20% базовых и связующих знаний в ядре / 80% расширяемых сведений во внешней памяти**. Это не жёсткое соотношение байтов или параметров: ядро учится сохранять способности рассуждать и извлекать нужные знания. Дисковая память может расти независимо от VRAM, должна поддерживать эффективное обучение/обновление и **не загружаться в GPU целиком**. Модель запрашивает только нужные иерархические регионы и выбирает глубину погружения, например «базы данных → PostgreSQL → SQL → SELECT». В VRAM помещаются веса, обязательные вычислительные состояния и лишь ограниченное представление запрошенных данных. **Сетевые и Wiki-адаптеры пока исключены из текущего этапа.**

## Два уровня проекта

**VeriNeural** (`crates/verineural/`) — независимый от архитектуры конструктор вычислений. Пользователь определяет Rust-примитивы, операции и контракты, объединяет их в Semantic Neural IR и получает:

- LLVM NVPTX/PTX и исполнение через **CUDA Graph** на явном non-blocking stream;
- Lean 4-модели и проверку поддерживаемых математических свойств;
- артефакты перевода, проверки ограничений памяти, композиции и доверенных предположений.

VeriNeural **не поставляет готовые LLM, Transformer/Attention, KV cache или обучающий стек конкретной модели**. Они принадлежат потребительским архитектурам в `labs/` и должны собираться из публичного API. Дисковая латентная память и её обучаемая маршрутизация также относятся к конкретной LLM, а не к готовым компонентам библиотеки. Lean-доказательства математической модели не являются доказательствами CUDA JIT/SASS или успешности обучения.

## Структура

| Каталог | Назначение |
| --- | --- |
| `crates/verineural/` | Компонуемые Rust API, Semantic IR, autodiff, компиляция GPU, Lean, проверки |
| `lean/VeriNeural/` | Исходники проверяемых Lean-теорем |
| `labs/torus16-mix-0.1.0/` | Исследование рекуррентной языковой модели EMA4/Torus16/Role-Delta; экспериментальная v0.2 |
| `labs/rotating-matrices-0.1.0/` | Исследование вращающихся матриц, маршрутизации, сохранённые результаты |
| `labs/xor-0.1.0/`, `labs/coupled-field-0.1.0/` | Отдельные проверяемые потребители библиотеки |
| `labs/consumer-acceptance-0.1.0/` | Приёмочные сценарии публичного API |
| `docs/verineural/` | Полная спецификация, дорожная карта, границы доказательств |

Основные документы: [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) (обязательные правила и конечные критерии), [SPEC.md](docs/verineural/SPEC.md) (целевая библиотека), [ROADMAP.md](docs/verineural/ROADMAP.md) (реализованное и планы), [AUTO_BUILD.md](docs/verineural/AUTO_BUILD.md) (сертифицируемая сборка), [Torus16 v0.2 transition](labs/torus16-mix-0.1.0/V0.2_TRANSITION.md) и [журнал экспериментов](labs/torus16-mix-0.1.0/EXPERIMENT_RESULTS.md).

## Среда и основные команды

Инструменты Rust, LLVM NVPTX, CUDA toolkit, Lean 4 и Task определены в `flake.nix`. NVIDIA Driver/GPU требуются на хосте для аппаратных проверок.

```sh
nix develop
task prepare           # cargo fmt и проверка форматирования
task check             # Rust workspace (см. правило auto-format в AGENTS.md)
task test              # CPU/обычные Rust-тесты
task clippy
```

`repospool` доступен в закреплённом Nix devShell. Команда `task prepare` сначала выполняет `repospool generate .`, создавая локальный `.repospool` со снимком **закоммиченного `HEAD`** (незакоммиченные изменения не входят), затем форматирует Rust. Все основные лабораторные команды Taskfile проходят эту подготовку; `task build`, `task clippy` и `task doc` также обновляют снимок без запуска автоформатирования. Если RepoSpool завершится ошибкой, последующая лабораторная команда не запустится. Снимок является генерируемым файлом, который CI публикует в `dev`; ручной запуск: `task repospool-generate`.

Специализированные команды из единого [Taskfile.yml](Taskfile.yml):

```sh
task proof-stage3
task verify-certified-build
task lab-xor && task verify-lab-xor
task lab-stage9 && task verify-lab-stage9
task verify-gpu-temporal-bptt
task verify-gpu-batch-transfers
task test-lab-torus16-ema4-checkpoint
```

Задачи `lab-xor` и `lab-stage9` **создают проверяемые файлы в своих лабораториях** (DOT/PNG, Lean, LLVM/PTX, manifests, output bits). Эти файлы считаются **генерируемыми выходами**, в Git не хранятся. Оффлайн `verify-lab-xor` / `verify-lab-stage9` запускают **после** генерации актуального набора. Исходники и обязательства доказательств сохраняются в Rust и Lean.

Для Torus16 сначала изучить [README лаборатории](labs/torus16-mix-0.1.0/README.md) и [план перехода v0.2](labs/torus16-mix-0.1.0/V0.2_TRANSITION.md). **Полный BPTT16 GPU JIT намеренно заблокирован по умолчанию:** большой граф с 63 707 CUDA kernels зависал на загрузке драйверного модуля без нагрузки GPU. `task benchmark-torus16-v02-bptt16` исторически называется benchmark, но сейчас выполняет только безопасный **CPU preflight** без LLVM/CUDA JIT и обучения. Не считать его показателем качества модели.

## Лёгкий CI (без GPU)

GitHub Actions при push в `dev` и `main` генерирует и проверяет `.repospool`,
загружает резервный snapshot в Actions Artifacts на 7 дней, затем запускает
только `cargo test --locked -p verineural --lib --tests`. Тесты с `#[ignore]`
(требующие GPU/Lean/LLVM/Graphviz) не запускаются. **Лабораторные crates
и их задачи через CI не запускаются.** Полная GPU/Lean-приёмка остаётся локальной.

После успешных тестов workflow **коммитит `.repospool` в `dev`** отдельным
fast-forward коммитом от `github-actions[bot]` без force-push; `main` остаётся
только для чтения и тестов. Снимок содержит исходное состояние предыдущего
коммита: сам `.repospool` исключён из индекса RepoSpool, а его запись в Git
создаёт новый SHA, поэтому он не может ссылаться на собственный Git-коммит.
Следующие `task repospool-generate` / `task prepare` учитывают этот случай и
не изменяют содержимое снимка на уже опубликованном artifact-only HEAD.
Публикация выполняется только при успешной генерации, верификации и CPU-тестах;
при конкурентном push обычный fast-forward `git push` отклонит устаревший снимок.

## Компактный контекст RepoSpool

[.repospoolignore](.repospoolignore) сохраняет только стартовый архитектурный
срез (~20% прежнего объёма). Исключение не удаляет файлы из Git и не отменяет
их обязательность: перед изменениями VeriNeural нужно отдельно читать полные
[AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md), [SPEC.md](docs/verineural/SPEC.md) и
[ROADMAP.md](docs/verineural/ROADMAP.md). Для конкретного backend читать
`crates/verineural/src/gpu.rs`, `cuda.rs`, `numeric.rs`, `proof.rs`,
`translation.rs`, а для сборки `Taskfile.yml`; для экспериментов обращаться
к соответствующим `labs/*/README.md`, данным и тестам. RepoSpool не заменяет
полную проверку реализации, доказательств и результатов.

## Правила результатов и верификации

- **Не путать** математические Lean-теоремы, структурный PTX audit, численную CUDA-проверку и неподтверждённую корректность аппаратного исполнения.
- Сообщать размер весов **отдельно** от объёма дисковой латентной памяти; измерять пик VRAM (включая состояния оптимизатора), задержки адресного чтения с диска, время компиляции/JIT, training throughput и время до качества.
- В лабораториях отделять train, validation и test; не выбирать архитектуру по зарезервированному test, сравнивать одинаковый объём обучения и учитывать различия числа optimizer updates.
- Не запускать тяжёлые GPU/Lean/Cargo задачи агентом без явного указания. Пользователь выполняет их на своей RTX 5060 и предоставляет логи.
- Рабочая ветка — только `dev`. `main` не обновляется без прямого поручения. Запрещены самовольные CI/CD и инфраструктурные сервисы.

Текущий репозиторий содержит **исследовательские реализации и проверяемые подмножества**, а не завершённую рекуррентную LLM с 3–4 GB весов и обучаемой дисковой памятью. Историю измерений хранить в профильных документах лабораторий, не раздувать корневой README очередными журналами запуска.

FILE	crates/verineural/Cargo.toml
[package]
name = "verineural"
version.workspace = true
edition.workspace = true
rust-version.workspace = true
description = "Importable Rust library for neural computation and formal verification (Semantic IR, Lean proof, and experimental LLVM NVPTX/CUDA stage)"
publish = false

[lib]
name = "verineural"
path = "src/lib.rs"

# Stage 4 still has no Rust dependencies; NVIDIA driver is loaded dynamically.
# llc is supplied by flake.nix, and GPU execution requires a system NVIDIA driver.

FILE	crates/verineural/src/autodiff.rs
//! Bounded reverse-mode differentiation of the *same* typed Semantic Neural IR.
//! Creates a second ordinary NeuralGraph by appending derivatives to a clone.
//! No opaque callbacks, no architecture-specific kernels and no fictitious FP32
//! certificate: mathematical reverse rules and NVIDIA execution are separate.
use std::collections::{BTreeMap, BTreeSet};
use std::error::Error;
use std::fmt;

use crate::{DType, Domain, NeuralError, NeuralGraph, NodeId, Operation, Shape, Tensor};

#[derive(Debug)]
pub enum DifferentiationError {
    Neural(NeuralError),
    Invalid(&'static str),
    Unsupported {
        node: usize,
        operation: &'static str,
    },
}

impl fmt::Display for DifferentiationError {
    fn fmt(&self, f: &mut fmt::Formatter<'_>) -> fmt::Result {
        match self {
            Self::Neural(err) => write!(f, "{err}"),
            Self::Invalid(s) => write!(f, "invalid derivative request: {s}"),
            Self::Unsupported { node, operation } => write!(
                f,
                "reverse-mode node {node}: unsupported derivative for {operation}"
            ),
        }
    }
}
impl Error for DifferentiationError {}
impl From<NeuralError> for DifferentiationError {
    fn from(err: NeuralError) -> Self {
        Self::Neural(err)
    }
}

/// Differentiable graph contains the *primal* as an unchanged prefix.
/// Input/output NodeId values therefore retain their graph identity.
/// Added source tensors are explicit and appear in 'constants'.
#[derive(Clone, Debug)]
pub struct ReverseGraph {
    graph: NeuralGraph,
    root: NodeId,
    seed: Option<NodeId>,
    gradients: Vec<(NodeId, NodeId)>,
    constants: Vec<(NodeId, Tensor<f32>)>,
}

impl ReverseGraph {
    pub fn graph(&self) -> &NeuralGraph {
        &self.graph
    }
    pub fn root(&self) -> NodeId {
        self.root
    }
    pub fn seed(&self) -> NodeId {
        self.seed.expect("graph-provided VJP has no external seed")
    }
    pub fn gradients(&self) -> &[(NodeId, NodeId)] {
        &self.gradients
    }
    pub fn constants(&self) -> &[(NodeId, Tensor<f32>)] {
        &self.constants
    }
    pub fn gradient_of(&self, node: NodeId) -> Option<NodeId> {
        self.gradients
            .iter()
            .find(|(source, _)| *source == node)
            .map(|(_, grad)| *grad)
    }

    /// Add seed and internally generated zero/one tensors to primal bindings.
    /// Filter this result to GpuProgram::source_inputs before a sliced GPU run.
    pub fn bindings(
        &self,
        primal: &[(NodeId, Tensor<f32>)],
        seed: Tensor<f32>,
    ) -> Result<Vec<(NodeId, Tensor<f32>)>, DifferentiationError> {
        let source = self.seed.ok_or(DifferentiationError::Invalid(
            "graph-provided VJP does not accept an external seed",
        ))?;
        if seed.shape() != &self.graph.node(self.root)?.shape {
            return Err(DifferentiationError::Invalid(
                "seed shape differs from differentiated output",
            ));
        }
        if seed.values().iter().any(|v| !v.is_finite()) {
            return Err(DifferentiationError::Invalid("seed must be finite"));
        }
        let mut result = primal.to_vec();
        result.push((source, seed));
        result.extend(self.constants.iter().cloned());
        Ok(result)
    }
}

struct ReverseBuilder {
    graph: NeuralGraph,
    constants: Vec<(NodeId, Tensor<f32>)>,
    fills: BTreeMap<(Vec<usize>, u32), NodeId>,
}

impl ReverseBuilder {
    fn fill(&mut self, shape: &Shape, value: f32) -> Result<NodeId, DifferentiationError> {
        let key = (shape.dims().to_vec(), value.to_bits());
        if let Some(id) = self.fills.get(&key) {
            return Ok(*id);
        }
        let tensor = Tensor::from_vec(key.0.clone(), vec![value; shape.element_count()])?;
        let id = self.graph.input(shape.clone(), Domain::Finite);
        self.constants.push((id, tensor));
        self.fills.insert(key, id);
        Ok(id)
    }

    fn neg(&mut self, value: NodeId) -> Result<NodeId, DifferentiationError> {
        let shape = self.graph.node(value)?.shape.clone();
        let zero = self.fill(&shape, 0.)?;
        Ok(self.graph.sub(zero, value)?)
    }

    fn reduce_scalar(&mut self, grad: NodeId) -> Result<NodeId, DifferentiationError> {
        let shape = self.graph.node(grad)?.shape.clone();
        if shape.dims() == [1, 1] {
            return Ok(grad);
        }
        if shape.rank() != 2 || shape.dims()[0] != 1 {
            return Err(DifferentiationError::Invalid(
                "scalar broadcast adjoint supports one row",
            ));
        }
        let ones = self.fill(&Shape::new(vec![shape.dims()[1], 1])?, 1.)?;
        Ok(self.graph.matmul(grad, ones)?)
    }

    fn scatter_slice(
        &mut self,
        grad: NodeId,
        start: usize,
        source_width: usize,
    ) -> Result<NodeId, DifferentiationError> {
        let written = self.graph.node(grad)?.shape.element_count();
        let mut parts = Vec::new();
        if start != 0 {
            parts.push(self.fill(&Shape::new(vec![1, start])?, 0.)?);
        }
        parts.push(grad);
        if start + written < source_width {
            parts.push(self.fill(&Shape::new(vec![1, source_width - start - written])?, 0.)?);
        }
        Ok(self.graph.concat(1, &parts)?)
    }
}

fn pointwise_kind(operation: &Operation) -> Option<&'static str> {
    let Operation::Pointwise(spec) = operation else {
        return None;
    };
    match (
        spec.id(),
        spec.version(),
        spec.arity(),
        spec.expression().canonical().as_str(),
    ) {
        ("verineural.sub", "1", 2, "sub(arg:0,arg:1)") => Some("sub"),
        ("verineural.div", "1", 2, "div(arg:0,arg:1)") => Some("div"),
        ("verineural.exp", "1", 1, "exp(arg:0)") => Some("exp"),
        ("verineural.sqrt", "1", 1, "sqrt(arg:0)") => Some("sqrt"),
        _ => None,
    }
}

fn supported(operation: &Operation, shape: &Shape, inputs: &[Shape]) -> bool {
    match operation {
        Operation::Input
        | Operation::Add
        | Operation::Mul
        | Operation::MatMul
        | Operation::BiasAdd
        | Operation::Reshape(_) => true,
        Operation::Permute { axes } => axes.as_slice() == [1, 0] && shape.rank() == 2,
        Operation::ReverseAxis { axis } => shape.rank() == 2 && *axis < 2,
        Operation::SliceAxis { axis: 1, .. } => {
            shape.rank() == 2 && shape.dims()[0] == 1 && inputs[0].dims()[0] == 1
        }
        Operation::Concat { axis: 1 } => {
            shape.rank() == 2 && shape.dims()[0] == 1 && inputs.iter().all(|s| s.dims()[0] == 1)
        }
        Operation::BroadcastTo(_) => {
            inputs[0] == *shape
                || (inputs[0].dims() == [1, 1] && shape.rank() == 2 && shape.dims()[0] == 1)
        }
        Operation::Pointwise(_) => pointwise_kind(operation).is_some(),
        _ => false,
    }
}

/// The seed is dL/d(root), supplied by the consumer. The returned graph
/// computes vector-Jacobian products for arbitrary requested primal inputs.
/// Input sources not depending on 'root' receive exact zero gradient.
/// All *reachable* primal operations are checked before derivative construction.
pub fn differentiate(
    primal: &NeuralGraph,
    root: NodeId,
    wrt: &[NodeId],
) -> Result<ReverseGraph, DifferentiationError> {
    let output = primal.node(root)?;
    let mut seeded = primal.clone();
    let seed = seeded.input(output.shape.clone(), Domain::Finite);
    differentiate_impl(&seeded, &[(root, seed)], wrt, Some(seed))
}

/// Compute the sum of vector-Jacobian products for multiple output roots.
/// Each seed is an existing IR expression, treated as a terminal adjoint.
/// Gradients do NOT propagate through the expression producing a seed.
/// This allows GPU loss-gradient construction and parameter VJPs in one
/// executable CUDA Graph; no machine-code/FP32 certificate is claimed.
pub fn differentiate_with_seeds(
    primal: &NeuralGraph,
    roots: &[(NodeId, NodeId)],
    wrt: &[NodeId],
) -> Result<ReverseGraph, DifferentiationError> {
    differentiate_impl(primal, roots, wrt, None)
}

fn differentiate_impl(
    primal: &NeuralGraph,
    roots: &[(NodeId, NodeId)],
    wrt: &[NodeId],
    external_seed: Option<NodeId>,
) -> Result<ReverseGraph, DifferentiationError> {
    let Some(&(root, _)) = roots.first() else {
        return Err(DifferentiationError::Invalid(
            "at least one output/seed pair required",
        ));
    };
    let mut unique_roots = BTreeSet::new();
    for &(output, seed) in roots {
        let y = primal.node(output)?;
        let s = primal.node(seed)?;
        if !unique_roots.insert(output.index())
            || y.dtype != DType::F32
            || s.dtype != DType::F32
            || y.shape != s.shape
        {
            return Err(DifferentiationError::Invalid(
                "output/seed pairs must be unique, matching F32 tensors",
            ));
        }
    }
    if wrt.is_empty() {
        return Err(DifferentiationError::Invalid(
            "at least one gradient target required",
        ));
    }
    let mut seen = BTreeSet::new();
    for &id in wrt {
        let node = primal.node(id)?;
        if !seen.insert(id.index())
            || node.dtype != DType::F32
            || !matches!(node.operation, Operation::Input)
        {
            return Err(DifferentiationError::Invalid(
                "gradient targets must be distinct F32 source nodes",
            ));
        }
    }

    let mut reachable = BTreeSet::new();
    let mut pending = roots.iter().map(|&(y, _)| y).collect::<Vec<_>>();
    while let Some(id) = pending.pop() {
        let node = primal.node(id)?;
        if !reachable.insert(id.index()) {
            continue;
        }
        let inputs = node
            .inputs
            .iter()
            .map(|x| primal.node(*x).map(|n| n.shape.clone()))
            .collect::<Result<Vec<_>, _>>()?;
        if !supported(&node.operation, &node.shape, &inputs) {
            return Err(DifferentiationError::Unsupported {
                node: id.index(),
                operation: node.operation.name(),
            });
        }
        pending.extend(node.inputs.iter().copied());
    }

    // Retain only primal nodes that can transmit an adjoint to requested
    // targets. This matters for a 1,920-node network when training one small
    // parameter: backprop must not materialize irrelevant derivative kernels.
    let mut relevant = wrt.iter().map(|id| id.index()).collect::<BTreeSet<_>>();
    for &index in &reachable {
        if primal.nodes()[index]
            .inputs
            .iter()
            .any(|id| relevant.contains(&id.index()))
        {
            relevant.insert(index);
        }
    }
    let mut b = ReverseBuilder {
        graph: primal.clone(),
        constants: Vec::new(),
        fills: BTreeMap::new(),
    };
    let mut adjoints = BTreeMap::<usize, NodeId>::new();
    for &(y, seed) in roots {
        adjoints.insert(y.index(), seed);
    }
    for index in reachable.into_iter().rev() {
        if !relevant.contains(&index) {
            continue;
        }
        let Some(delta) = adjoints.get(&index).copied() else {
            continue;
        };
        let node = primal.nodes()[index].clone();
        let ids = &node.inputs;
        let contributions: Vec<(NodeId, NodeId)> = match &node.operation {
            Operation::Input => vec![],
            Operation::Add => vec![(ids[0], delta), (ids[1], delta)],
            Operation::Mul => vec![
                (ids[0], b.graph.mul(delta, ids[1])?),
                (ids[1], b.graph.mul(delta, ids[0])?),
            ],
            Operation::MatMul => {
                let a_t = b.graph.permute(ids[0], &[1, 0])?;
                let b_t = b.graph.permute(ids[1], &[1, 0])?;
                vec![
                    (ids[0], b.graph.matmul(delta, b_t)?),
                    (ids[1], b.graph.matmul(a_t, delta)?),
                ]
            }
            Operation::BiasAdd => {
                let bias_shape = &primal.node(ids[1])?.shape;
                let mut db = delta;
                let rows = node.shape.dims()[0];
                if rows > 1 {
                    let ones = b.fill(&Shape::new(vec![1, rows])?, 1.)?;
                    db = b.graph.matmul(ones, delta)?;
                }
                db = b.graph.reshape(db, bias_shape.clone())?;
                vec![(ids[0], delta), (ids[1], db)]
            }
            Operation::Reshape(_) => vec![(
                ids[0],
                b.graph.reshape(delta, primal.node(ids[0])?.shape.clone())?,
            )],
            Operation::Permute { .. } => vec![(ids[0], b.graph.permute(delta, &[1, 0])?)],
            Operation::ReverseAxis { axis } => vec![(ids[0], b.graph.reverse_axis(delta, *axis)?)],
            Operation::Concat { axis: 1 } => {
                let left = primal.node(ids[0])?.shape.dims()[1];
                let right = primal.node(ids[1])?.shape.dims()[1];
                vec![
                    (ids[0], b.graph.slice_axis(delta, 1, 0, left)?),
                    (ids[1], b.graph.slice_axis(delta, 1, left, right)?),
                ]
            }
            Operation::SliceAxis { axis: 1, start, .. } => {
                let width = primal.node(ids[0])?.shape.dims()[1];
                vec![(ids[0], b.scatter_slice(delta, *start, width)?)]
            }
            Operation::BroadcastTo(_) => {
                let source_shape = &primal.node(ids[0])?.shape;
                let grad = if source_shape == &node.shape {
                    delta
                } else {
                    b.reduce_scalar(delta)?
                };
                vec![(ids[0], grad)]
            }
            Operation::Pointwise(_) => match pointwise_kind(&node.operation) {
                Some("sub") => vec![(ids[0], delta), (ids[1], b.neg(delta)?)],
                Some("div") => {
                    let da = b.graph.div(delta, ids[1])?;
                    let scaled = b.graph.mul(delta, node.id)?;
                    let db = b.graph.div(scaled, ids[1])?;
                    vec![(ids[0], da), (ids[1], b.neg(db)?)]
                }
                Some("exp") => vec![(ids[0], b.graph.mul(delta, node.id)?)],
                Some("sqrt") => {
                    let two_y = b.graph.add(node.id, node.id)?;
                    vec![(ids[0], b.graph.div(delta, two_y)?)]
                }
                _ => unreachable!("prevalidated pointwise signature"),
            },
            _ => unreachable!("prevalidated differentiability rule"),
        };
        for (source, grad) in contributions {
            if !relevant.contains(&source.index()) {
                continue;
            }
            if let Some(existing) = adjoints.get(&source.index()).copied() {
                let summed = b.graph.add(existing, grad)?;
                adjoints.insert(source.index(), summed);
            } else {
                adjoints.insert(source.index(), grad);
            }
        }
    }
    let gradients = wrt
        .iter()
        .map(|&target| {
            let grad = match adjoints.get(&target.index()).copied() {
                Some(id) => id,
                None => b.fill(&primal.node(target)?.shape, 0.)?,
            };
            Ok((target, grad))
        })
        .collect::<Result<Vec<_>, DifferentiationError>>()?;
    Ok(ReverseGraph {
        graph: b.graph,
        root,
        seed: external_seed,
        gradients,
        constants: b.constants,
    })
}

FILE	crates/verineural/src/consumer.rs
//! Small consumer-facing binding/obligation helpers. The Semantic IR,
//! module contracts and Lean proof engine remain the only sources of truth.
use std::error::Error;
use std::fmt;
use std::path::Path;

use crate::{
    CheckedLean, FixedScan, LeanAxiomAudit, LeanProgram, LeanProofEngine, MathContract,
    MultiOutputModule, NeuralError, NeuralGraph, NeuralModule, NodeId, PortContract, Predicate,
    ProofError, ProofGoal, ProofGoalKind, ValueRef,
};

/// A structured error at a caller-owned component path and named port.
/// The underlying shape, domain or contract error is preserved, not translated
/// into an allegedly verified mathematical claim.
#[derive(Debug)]
pub struct BindingError {
    pub component_path: String,
    pub port: String,
    pub constraint: String,
    pub source: Option<NeuralError>,
}

impl fmt::Display for BindingError {
    fn fmt(&self, f: &mut fmt::Formatter<'_>) -> fmt::Result {
        write!(
            f,
            "component {} port {}: {}",
            self.component_path, self.port, self.constraint
        )?;
        if let Some(source) = &self.source {
            write!(f, ": {source}")?;
        }
        Ok(())
    }
}

impl Error for BindingError {
    fn source(&self) -> Option<&(dyn Error + 'static)> {
        self.source.as_ref().map(|source| source as &dyn Error)
    }
}

/// A proof failure is associated with the explicitly requested theorem.
/// A generated theorem is not a checked theorem.
#[derive(Debug)]
pub struct ObligationError {
    pub theorem: String,
    pub source: ProofError,
}

impl fmt::Display for ObligationError {
    fn fmt(&self, f: &mut fmt::Formatter<'_>) -> fmt::Result {
        write!(f, "proof obligation {}: {}", self.theorem, self.source)
    }
}

impl Error for ObligationError {
    fn source(&self) -> Option<&(dyn Error + 'static)> {
        Some(&self.source)
    }
}

/// Lightweight facade over the existing atomic module insertion/rollback.
pub struct ComponentBinder<'a> {
    graph: &'a mut NeuralGraph,
    path: String,
}

impl NeuralGraph {
    /// Label subsequent module calls without duplicating the graph or contracts.
    pub fn component(&mut self, path: impl Into<String>) -> ComponentBinder<'_> {
        ComponentBinder {
            graph: self,
            path: path.into(),
        }
    }
}

impl ComponentBinder<'_> {
    fn failed(
        &self,
        port: impl Into<String>,
        constraint: impl Into<String>,
        source: Option<NeuralError>,
    ) -> BindingError {
        BindingError {
            component_path: self.path.clone(),
            port: port.into(),
            constraint: constraint.into(),
            source,
        }
    }

    fn check_input(
        &self,
        id: NodeId,
        name: &str,
        required: &PortContract,
    ) -> Result<(), BindingError> {
        let actual = self.graph.node(id).map_err(|error| {
            self.failed(name, "input must belong to the current graph", Some(error))
        })?;
        if actual.shape != required.shape {
            return Err(self.failed(
                name,
                "input shape",
                Some(NeuralError::ShapeMismatch {
                    expected: required.shape.clone(),
                    actual: actual.shape.clone(),
                }),
            ));
        }
        if actual.dtype != required.dtype {
            return Err(self.failed(
                name,
                "input dtype",
                Some(NeuralError::DTypeMismatch {
                    operation: "component_input",
                    expected: required.dtype,
                    actual: actual.dtype,
                }),
            ));
        }
        if !actual.domain.satisfies(required.domain) {
            return Err(self.failed(
                name,
                "input value domain",
                Some(NeuralError::DomainNotEstablished {
                    required: required.domain,
                    actual: actual.domain,
                }),
            ));
        }
        Ok(())
    }

    /// Invoke one existing single-output module with positional ports.
    /// Port names in diagnostics are stable input_0, input_1, etc.
    pub fn single<M: NeuralModule>(
        &mut self,
        module: &M,
        inputs: &[NodeId],
    ) -> Result<NodeId, BindingError> {
        let contract: &MathContract = module.contract();
        if inputs.len() != contract.requires.len() {
            return Err(self.failed(
                "inputs",
                format!(
                    "expected {} inputs, received {}",
                    contract.requires.len(),
                    inputs.len()
                ),
                None,
            ));
        }
        for (index, (&id, required)) in inputs.iter().zip(&contract.requires).enumerate() {
            self.check_input(id, &format!("input_{index}"), required)?;
        }
        self.graph.apply_module(module, inputs).map_err(|source| {
            self.failed(
                "output",
                format!("{} postcondition or body", module.name()),
                Some(source),
            )
        })
    }

    /// Bind named input ports in arbitrary caller order. Reject missing,
    /// duplicate and unexpected bindings before mutating the graph.
    pub fn multi<M: MultiOutputModule>(
        &mut self,
        module: &M,
        bindings: &[(&str, NodeId)],
    ) -> Result<Vec<NodeId>, BindingError> {
        let ports = &module.contract().inputs;
        let mut ordered = Vec::with_capacity(ports.len());
        for required in ports {
            let mut found = None;
            for &(name, id) in bindings {
                if name == required.name && found.replace(id).is_some() {
                    return Err(self.failed(name, "duplicate port binding", None));
                }
            }
            let id = found
                .ok_or_else(|| self.failed(required.name, "missing required port binding", None))?;
            self.check_input(id, required.name, &required.port)?;
            ordered.push(id);
        }
        for &(name, _) in bindings {
            if !ports.iter().any(|port| port.name == name) {
                return Err(self.failed(name, "unexpected port binding", None));
            }
        }
        self.graph
            .apply_multi_module(module, &ordered)
            .map_err(|source| {
                self.failed(
                    "outputs",
                    format!("{} output postconditions or body", module.name()),
                    Some(source),
                )
            })
    }

    /// Resolve results by their declared names instead of array positions.
    pub fn multi_named<M: MultiOutputModule>(
        &mut self,
        module: &M,
        bindings: &[(&str, NodeId)],
    ) -> Result<std::collections::BTreeMap<String, NodeId>, BindingError> {
        let outputs = self.multi(module, bindings)?;
        Ok(module
            .contract()
            .outputs
            .iter()
            .zip(outputs)
            .map(|(port, node)| (port.name.to_owned(), node))
            .collect())
    }

    /// A finite scan, not a proof for an unbounded recurrent system.
    pub fn scan<M: MultiOutputModule>(
        &mut self,
        transition: &M,
        initial_state: NodeId,
        inputs: &[NodeId],
    ) -> Result<FixedScan, BindingError> {
        let ports = &transition.contract().inputs;
        if ports.len() == 2 && ports[0].name == "state" && ports[1].name == "input" {
            self.check_input(initial_state, "state", &ports[0].port)?;
            for (step, &input) in inputs.iter().enumerate() {
                self.check_input(input, &format!("input[{step}]"), &ports[1].port)?;
            }
        }
        self.graph
            .scan_fixed(transition, initial_state, inputs)
            .map_err(|source| {
                self.failed(
                    "next_state",
                    "bounded state-transition contract",
                    Some(source),
                )
            })
    }
}

impl ProofGoal {
    /// Make the source assumptions explicit; they are never inferred as facts.
    pub fn nonnegative(name: impl Into<String>, output: NodeId, assumptions: Vec<NodeId>) -> Self {
        Self {
            name: name.into(),
            output,
            kind: ProofGoalKind::Nonnegative { assumptions },
        }
    }

    pub fn bounded_above(name: impl Into<String>, lower: NodeId, output: NodeId) -> Self {
        Self {
            name: name.into(),
            output,
            kind: ProofGoalKind::Predicate(Predicate::pointwise_le(
                ValueRef::Node(lower),
                ValueRef::Output,
            )),
        }
    }

    /// Return an independently generated theorem, without claiming it checked.
    pub fn generate_source(
        &self,
        graph: &NeuralGraph,
        checker: &LeanProofEngine,
    ) -> Result<LeanProgram, ObligationError> {
        checker
            .generate_goal(graph, self)
            .map_err(|source| ObligationError {
                theorem: format!("architecture_property_{}", self.name),
                source,
            })
    }

    /// Check the Lean file and its transitive axiom dependencies.
    pub fn certify(
        &self,
        graph: &NeuralGraph,
        checker: &LeanProofEngine,
        path: &Path,
    ) -> Result<(CheckedLean, LeanAxiomAudit), ObligationError> {
        let program = self.generate_source(graph, checker)?;
        checker
            .verify_certified(&program, path)
            .map_err(|source| ObligationError {
                theorem: format!("architecture_property_{}", self.name),
                source,
            })
    }
}

FILE	crates/verineural/src/gpu/engine.rs
//! GPU compilation, validation and CUDA Graph session preparation.

use super::*;

impl GpuEngine {
    /// CUDA architecture must be an explicit LLVM -mcpu value (e.g. sm_86).
    pub fn new(llc: impl Into<PathBuf>, arch: impl Into<String>) -> Self {
        Self {
            llc: llc.into(),
            arch: arch.into(),
            launch: GpuLaunchConfig::default(),
            codegen_opt_level: GpuCodegenOptLevel::O0,
            allocation_slab: false,
        }
    }

    /// Select a checked launch policy. Fusion remains experimental.
    pub fn with_launch_config(mut self, launch: GpuLaunchConfig) -> Self {
        self.launch = launch;
        self
    }

    /// Experimental NVPTX codegen profile; O0 remains the safe default.
    /// The emitted PTX must still pass translation validation before execution.
    pub fn with_codegen_opt_level(mut self, level: GpuCodegenOptLevel) -> Self {
        self.codegen_opt_level = level;
        self
    }

    /// Opt into one CUDA allocation containing disjoint tensor buffers.
    /// Physical addresses change but Semantic IR, arithmetic and kernel
    /// ordering do not. Disabled by default pending GPU parity/benchmarks.
    /// The entire live graph must fit in one device allocation; allocation
    /// failures are returned, never silently retried using a different plan.
    pub fn with_allocation_slab(mut self, enabled: bool) -> Self {
        self.allocation_slab = enabled;
        self
    }

    /// Backward-compatible single-output entrypoint, using the same shared
    /// compilation path as multi-output graphs.
    pub fn compile(&self, graph: &NeuralGraph, output: NodeId) -> Result<GpuProgram, GpuError> {
        self.compile_outputs(graph, &[output])
    }

    /// Compile the union of all requested outputs into one LLVM/PTX module.
    /// No duplicated producer kernels, no disconnected output slices, and
    /// no fusion that discards an explicitly selected observable output.
    pub fn compile_outputs(
        &self,
        graph: &NeuralGraph,
        outputs: &[NodeId],
    ) -> Result<GpuProgram, GpuError> {
        if outputs.is_empty() {
            return Err(GpuError::InvalidInput {
                node: 0,
                reason: "multi-output GPU program requires at least one output",
            });
        }
        let mut seen_outputs = BTreeSet::new();
        for &id in outputs {
            graph.node(id)?;
            if !seen_outputs.insert(id.index()) {
                return Err(GpuError::InvalidInput {
                    node: id.index(),
                    reason: "multi-output GPU program has duplicate output",
                });
            }
        }
        let output = outputs[0];
        let mut reachable = BTreeSet::new();
        let mut pending = outputs.to_vec();
        while let Some(id) = pending.pop() {
            let node = graph.node(id)?;
            if !reachable.insert(id.index()) {
                continue;
            }
            if node.shape.element_count() > i32::MAX as usize {
                return Err(GpuError::UnsupportedSize {
                    elements: node.shape.element_count(),
                });
            }
            if !matches!(
                node.operation,
                Operation::Input
                    | Operation::Add
                    | Operation::Mul
                    | Operation::MatMul
                    | Operation::BiasAdd
                    | Operation::Relu
                    | Operation::Permute { .. }
                    | Operation::ReverseAxis { .. }
                    | Operation::Concat { .. }
                    | Operation::SliceAxis { .. }
                    | Operation::BroadcastTo(_)
                    | Operation::ArgMax { .. }
                    | Operation::Take { .. }
                    | Operation::Reshape(_)
                    | Operation::Pointwise(_)
            ) {
                return Err(GpuError::UnsupportedOperation {
                    node: id.index(),
                    operation: node.operation.name(),
                });
            }
            if let Operation::Pointwise(ref spec) = node.operation {
                let kind = supported_pointwise(spec);
                if kind.is_none()
                    || (matches!(kind, Some(TranslationKind::ExpApprox))
                        && !self.launch.approximate_exp())
                {
                    return Err(GpuError::UnsupportedOperation {
                        node: id.index(),
                        operation: node.operation.name(),
                    });
                }
            }
            pending.extend(node.inputs.iter().copied());
        }
        let live_nodes = reachable.into_iter().collect::<Vec<_>>();
        let source_inputs = live_nodes
            .iter()
            .filter_map(|&index| {
                let node = &graph.nodes()[index];
                matches!(node.operation, Operation::Input).then_some(node.id)
            })
            .collect::<Vec<_>>();
        // A producer can be skipped only when its sole reachable use is the
        // consuming Relu. Shared DAG nodes and Reshape aliases are left intact.
        let mut uses = vec![0usize; graph.nodes().len()];
        for &index in &live_nodes {
            for id in &graph.nodes()[index].inputs {
                uses[id.index()] += 1;
            }
        }
        // Selected roots are observable even when an in-graph consumer also
        // reads them. Never fold one into a different output's kernel.
        for &selected in outputs {
            uses[selected.index()] += 1;
        }
        // A materialized additional output may have later DAG consumers.
        // It can move to a later kernel only if no live consumer executes
        // before that kernel. This is independent of output observability.
        let mut earliest_consumer = vec![usize::MAX; graph.nodes().len()];
        for &index in &live_nodes {
            for id in &graph.nodes()[index].inputs {
                earliest_consumer[id.index()] = earliest_consumer[id.index()].min(index);
            }
        }
        let mut fused_relus = BTreeMap::new();
        let mut fused_pointwise_chains = BTreeMap::new();
        let mut fused_mul_adds = BTreeMap::new();
        let mut fused_mul_add_muls = BTreeMap::new();
        let mut fused_binary_pairs = BTreeMap::new();
        let mut fused_sqrt_add_divs = BTreeMap::new();
        let mut fused_mul_mul_add_divs = BTreeMap::new();
        let mut fused_mul_diamond_adds = BTreeMap::new();
        let mut fused_dual_outputs = BTreeMap::new();
        if self.launch.relu_fusion == ReluFusion::Experimental {
            for &index in &live_nodes {
                let node = &graph.nodes()[index];
                if !matches!(node.operation, Operation::Relu) {
                    continue;
                }
                let producer_id = node.inputs[0];
                let producer = graph.node(producer_id)?;
                if uses[producer_id.index()] != 1 {
                    continue;
                }
                match producer.operation {
                    Operation::Add | Operation::Mul => {
                        fused_relus.insert(index, producer_id.index());
                    }
                    Operation::BiasAdd => {
                        fused_relus.insert(index, producer_id.index());
                        let inner_id = producer.inputs[0];
                        let inner = graph.node(inner_id)?;
                        if uses[inner_id.index()] == 1
                            && matches!(inner.operation, Operation::Add | Operation::Mul)
                        {
                            fused_pointwise_chains
                                .insert(index, vec![inner_id.index(), producer_id.index()]);
                        }
                    }
                    _ => {}
                }
            }
        }
        let mut skipped = fused_relus.values().copied().collect::<BTreeSet<_>>();
        for chain in fused_pointwise_chains.values() {
            skipped.extend(chain.iter().copied());
        }
        if self.launch.pointwise_fusion() {
            // A four-stage rounded pointwise chain, limited by four
            // full-shape external inputs and explicit reuse of a multiplicand:
            // Div(Add(Mul(Mul(a,b), a|b), c), d).
            // Walk roots in reverse topological order and reserve all
            // exclusive intermediates before selecting shorter rewrites.
            for &index in live_nodes.iter().rev() {
                let root = &graph.nodes()[index];
                let div = matches!(&root.operation, Operation::Pointwise(spec)
                    if supported_pointwise(spec) == Some(TranslationKind::DivRne));
                if !div || skipped.contains(&index) {
                    continue;
                }
                let sum = graph.node(root.inputs[0])?;
                if !matches!(sum.operation, Operation::Add)
                    || uses[sum.id.index()] != 1
                    || skipped.contains(&sum.id.index())
                    || sum.shape != root.shape
                {
                    continue;
                }
                'candidate: for add_slot in 0..2 {
                    let second = graph.node(sum.inputs[add_slot])?;
                    if !matches!(second.operation, Operation::Mul)
                        || uses[second.id.index()] != 1
                        || skipped.contains(&second.id.index())
                        || second.shape != root.shape
                    {
                        continue;
                    }
                    for middle_slot in 0..2 {
                        let first = graph.node(second.inputs[middle_slot])?;
                        if !matches!(first.operation, Operation::Mul)
                            || uses[first.id.index()] != 1
                            || skipped.contains(&first.id.index())
                            || first.shape != root.shape
                        {
                            continue;
                        }
                        let externals = [
                            first.inputs[0],
                            first.inputs[1],
                            sum.inputs[1 - add_slot],
                            root.inputs[1],
                        ];
                        if externals
                            .iter()
                            .any(|id| graph.nodes()[id.index()].shape != root.shape)
                        {
                            continue;
                        }
                        if let Some(reused) = first
                            .inputs
                            .iter()
                            .position(|&id| id == second.inputs[1 - middle_slot])
                        {
                            fused_mul_mul_add_divs.insert(
                                index,
                                (
                                    first.id.index(),
                                    second.id.index(),
                                    sum.id.index(),
                                    reused,
                                    middle_slot,
                                    add_slot,
                                ),
                            );
                            skipped.extend([first.id.index(), second.id.index(), sum.id.index()]);
                            break 'candidate;
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
            // Opt-in architecture-neutral strict-order fusion:
            // Sqrt(x) -> Add(sqrt(x), epsilon) -> Div(numerator, sum).
            // Sources must have exactly the same shape and both internal
            // nodes exactly one reachable use (including selected outputs).
            for &index in live_nodes.iter().rev() {
                let root = &graph.nodes()[index];
                let is_div = matches!(&root.operation, Operation::Pointwise(spec)
                    if supported_pointwise(spec) == Some(TranslationKind::DivRne));
                if !is_div || skipped.contains(&index) {
                    continue;
                }
                let middle = graph.node(root.inputs[1])?;
                if !matches!(middle.operation, Operation::Add)
                    || uses[middle.id.index()] != 1
                    || skipped.contains(&middle.id.index())
                    || root.shape != middle.shape
                {
                    continue;
                }
                for slot in 0..2 {
                    let inner = graph.node(middle.inputs[slot])?;
                    let is_sqrt = matches!(&inner.operation, Operation::Pointwise(spec)
                        if supported_pointwise(spec) == Some(TranslationKind::SqrtRne));
                    if !is_sqrt
                        || uses[inner.id.index()] != 1
                        || skipped.contains(&inner.id.index())
                        || inner.shape != root.shape
                        || [inner.inputs[0], middle.inputs[1 - slot], root.inputs[0]]
                            .iter()
                            .any(|&id| graph.nodes()[id.index()].shape != root.shape)
                    {
                        continue;
                    }
                    fused_sqrt_add_divs.insert(index, (inner.id.index(), middle.id.index(), slot));
                    skipped.insert(inner.id.index());
                    skipped.insert(middle.id.index());
                    break;
                }
            }
            // Four-stage pointwise diamond: Add(Mul(a,b), Mul(Mul(c,d), c|d)).
            // The root Add may be selected, unlike its three Mul producers.
            for &index in live_nodes.iter().rev() {
                let root = &graph.nodes()[index];
                if !matches!(root.operation, Operation::Add) || skipped.contains(&index) {
                    continue;
                }
                'diamond: for left_slot in 0..2 {
                    let left = graph.node(root.inputs[left_slot])?;
                    let second = graph.node(root.inputs[1 - left_slot])?;
                    if !matches!(left.operation, Operation::Mul)
                        || !matches!(second.operation, Operation::Mul)
                        || uses[left.id.index()] != 1
                        || uses[second.id.index()] != 1
                        || skipped.contains(&left.id.index())
                        || skipped.contains(&second.id.index())
                        || left.id == second.id
                        || left.shape != root.shape
                        || second.shape != root.shape
                    {
                        continue;
                    }
                    for right_slot in 0..2 {
                        let first = graph.node(second.inputs[right_slot])?;
                        if !matches!(first.operation, Operation::Mul)
                            || uses[first.id.index()] != 1
                            || skipped.contains(&first.id.index())
                            || first.id == left.id
                            || first.shape != root.shape
                        {
                            continue;
                        }
                        let sources = [
                            left.inputs[0],
                            left.inputs[1],
                            first.inputs[0],
                            first.inputs[1],
                        ];
                        if sources
                            .iter()
                            .any(|&id| graph.nodes()[id.index()].shape != root.shape)
                        {
                            continue;
                        }
                        if let Some(reused) = first
                            .inputs
                            .iter()
                            .position(|&id| id == second.inputs[1 - right_slot])
                        {
                            fused_mul_diamond_adds.insert(
                                index,
                                (
                                    left.id.index(),
                                    first.id.index(),
                                    second.id.index(),
                                    reused,
                                    right_slot,
                                    left_slot,
                                ),
                            );
                            skipped.extend([left.id.index(), first.id.index(), second.id.index()]);
                            break 'diamond;
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
            // Longer chains take priority, but never cross observed values,
            // shared nodes or existing ReLU fusion boundaries.
            for &index in live_nodes.iter().rev() {
                let root = &graph.nodes()[index];
                if !matches!(root.operation, Operation::Mul) || skipped.contains(&index) {
                    continue;
                }
                'outer: for outer_slot in 0..2 {
                    let middle = graph.node(root.inputs[outer_slot])?;
                    if !matches!(middle.operation, Operation::Add)
                        || uses[middle.id.index()] != 1
                        || skipped.contains(&middle.id.index())
                        || middle.shape != root.shape
                    {
                        continue;
                    }
                    for add_slot in 0..2 {
                        let inner = graph.node(middle.inputs[add_slot])?;
                        if !matches!(inner.operation, Operation::Mul)
                            || uses[inner.id.index()] != 1
                            || skipped.contains(&inner.id.index())
                            || inner.shape != root.shape
                        {
                            continue;
                        }
                        let externals = [
                            inner.inputs[0],
                            inner.inputs[1],
                            middle.inputs[1 - add_slot],
                        ];
                        if externals
                            .iter()
                            .any(|&id| graph.nodes()[id.index()].shape != root.shape)
                        {
                            continue;
                        }
                        if let Some(reuse) = externals
                            .iter()
                            .position(|&id| id == root.inputs[1 - outer_slot])
                        {
                            fused_mul_add_muls.insert(
                                index,
                                (
                                    inner.id.index(),
                                    middle.id.index(),
                                    add_slot,
                                    outer_slot,
                                    reuse,
                                ),
                            );
                            skipped.insert(inner.id.index());
                            skipped.insert(middle.id.index());
                            break 'outer;
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
            for &index in &live_nodes {
                let node = &graph.nodes()[index];
                if !matches!(node.operation, Operation::Add) || skipped.contains(&index) {
                    continue;
                }
                for slot in 0..2 {
                    let producer = graph.node(node.inputs[slot])?;
                    if !matches!(producer.operation, Operation::Mul)
                        || uses[producer.id.index()] != 1
                        || skipped.contains(&producer.id.index())
                        || producer.shape != node.shape
                        || graph.node(node.inputs[1 - slot])?.shape != node.shape
                        || producer
                            .inputs
                            .iter()
                            .any(|&id| graph.nodes()[id.index()].shape != node.shape)
                    {
                        continue;
                    }
                    fused_mul_adds.insert(index, (producer.id.index(), slot));
                    skipped.insert(producer.id.index());
                    break;
                }
            }
            // Extend strict-order pair fusion to Add→Add, Add→Mul and
            // Mul→Mul. Existing Mul→Add has priority via fused_mul_adds.
            // No shared/selected intermediate, no alias-driven shape
            // broadcast, and no overlapping fusion roots.
            for &index in live_nodes.iter().rev() {
                let root = &graph.nodes()[index];
                if !matches!(root.operation, Operation::Add | Operation::Mul)
                    || skipped.contains(&index)
                    || fused_mul_adds.contains_key(&index)
                    || fused_mul_add_muls.contains_key(&index)
                {
                    continue;
                }
                for slot in 0..2 {
                    let inner = graph.node(root.inputs[slot])?;
                    if !matches!(inner.operation, Operation::Add | Operation::Mul)
                        || (matches!(root.operation, Operation::Add)
                            && matches!(inner.operation, Operation::Mul))
                        || uses[inner.id.index()] != 1
                        || skipped.contains(&inner.id.index())
                        || fused_mul_adds.contains_key(&inner.id.index())
                        || fused_mul_add_muls.contains_key(&inner.id.index())
                        || root.shape != inner.shape
                        || graph.nodes()[root.inputs[1 - slot].index()].shape != root.shape
                        || inner
                            .inputs
                            .iter()
                            .any(|&id| graph.nodes()[id.index()].shape != root.shape)
                    {
                        continue;
                    }
                    fused_binary_pairs.insert(index, (inner.id.index(), slot));
                    skipped.insert(inner.id.index());
                    break;
                }
            }
        }
        // Horizontal fusion of two independent live Add/Mul nodes of the same
        // shape. Both results are materialized, even for non-public nodes.
        // No consumer of the earlier result may run before the second node.
        // A bounded lookback avoids quadratic compilation on large BPTT DAGs.
        // FP32 operation order and all observable values are preserved.
        if self.launch.pointwise_fusion() {
            let candidates = if self.launch.internal_pointwise_fusion() {
                live_nodes
                    .iter()
                    .copied()
                    .filter(|&index| {
                        matches!(
                            graph.nodes()[index].operation,
                            Operation::Add | Operation::Mul
                        )
                    })
                    .collect::<Vec<_>>()
            } else {
                let mut selected = outputs.iter().map(|id| id.index()).collect::<Vec<_>>();
                selected.sort_unstable();
                selected
            };
            let mut reserved = BTreeSet::new();
            for (later_pos, &later) in candidates.iter().enumerate() {
                let second = &graph.nodes()[later];
                if !matches!(second.operation, Operation::Add | Operation::Mul)
                    || uses[later] == 0
                    || skipped.contains(&later)
                    || reserved.contains(&later)
                    || second.dtype != DType::F32
                    || second.inputs.iter().any(|id| skipped.contains(&id.index()))
                    || fused_mul_adds.contains_key(&later)
                    || fused_binary_pairs.contains_key(&later)
                    || fused_mul_add_muls.contains_key(&later)
                    || fused_mul_mul_add_divs.contains_key(&later)
                    || fused_mul_diamond_adds.contains_key(&later)
                {
                    continue;
                }
                for &earlier in candidates[..later_pos].iter().rev().take(64) {
                    let first = &graph.nodes()[earlier];
                    if reserved.contains(&earlier)
                        || skipped.contains(&earlier)
                        || uses[earlier] == 0
                        || earliest_consumer[earlier] <= later
                        || !matches!(first.operation, Operation::Add | Operation::Mul)
                        || first.dtype != DType::F32
                        || first.shape != second.shape
                        || first.inputs.iter().chain(&second.inputs).any(|id| {
                            skipped.contains(&id.index())
                                || graph.nodes()[id.index()].dtype != DType::F32
                                || graph.nodes()[id.index()].shape != second.shape
                        })
                        || fused_mul_adds.contains_key(&earlier)
                        || fused_binary_pairs.contains_key(&earlier)
                        || fused_mul_add_muls.contains_key(&earlier)
                        || fused_mul_mul_add_divs.contains_key(&earlier)
                        || fused_mul_diamond_adds.contains_key(&earlier)
                    {
                        continue;
                    }
                    fused_dual_outputs.insert(later, earlier);
                    reserved.extend([earlier, later]);
                    skipped.insert(earlier);
                    break;
                }
            }
        }
        let mut llvm_ir = String::from(
            "target datalayout = \"e-p:64:64:64-i1:8:8-i8:8:8-i16:16:16-i32:32:32-i64:64:64-f32:32:32-f64:64:64-v16:16:16-v32:32:32-v64:64:64-v128:128:128-n16:32:64\"\n\
             target triple = \"nvptx64-nvidia-cuda\"\n\n\
             declare i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.tid.x()\n\
             declare i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.ctaid.x()\n\
             declare i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.ntid.x()\n\n",
        );
        let mut specializations = BTreeMap::<String, usize>::new();
        let mut kernel_entries = BTreeMap::new();
        for &index in &live_nodes {
            let node = &graph.nodes()[index];
            if matches!(node.operation, Operation::Input)
                || graph.storage(node.id)?.is_alias()
                || skipped.contains(&index)
            {
                continue;
            }
            let mut body = String::new();
            if let Some(&earlier) = fused_dual_outputs.get(&index) {
                body.push_str(&dual_pointwise_kernel_ir(
                    index,
                    matches!(graph.nodes()[earlier].operation, Operation::Mul),
                    matches!(node.operation, Operation::Mul),
                ));
            } else if let Some(&(_, _, _, reused, right_slot, left_slot)) =
                fused_mul_diamond_adds.get(&index)
            {
                body.push_str(&mul_diamond_add_kernel_ir(
                    index,
                    reused,
                    right_slot == 1,
                    left_slot == 1,
                ));
            } else if let Some(&(_, _, _, reused, middle_slot, add_slot)) =
                fused_mul_mul_add_divs.get(&index)
            {
                body.push_str(&mul_mul_add_div_kernel_ir(
                    index,
                    reused,
                    middle_slot == 1,
                    add_slot == 1,
                ));
            } else if let Some(&(_, _, slot)) = fused_sqrt_add_divs.get(&index) {
                body.push_str(&sqrt_add_div_kernel_ir(index, slot == 1));
            } else if let Some(&(_, _, add_slot, outer_slot, reuse)) =
                fused_mul_add_muls.get(&index)
            {
                body.push_str(&mul_add_mul_kernel_ir(
                    index,
                    add_slot == 1,
                    outer_slot == 1,
                    reuse,
                ));
            } else if let Some(&(mul, slot)) = fused_mul_adds.get(&index) {
                debug_assert!(matches!(graph.nodes()[mul].operation, Operation::Mul));
                body.push_str(&mul_add_kernel_ir(index, slot == 1));
            } else if let Some(&(producer, slot)) = fused_binary_pairs.get(&index) {
                body.push_str(&binary_chain_kernel_ir(
                    index,
                    matches!(graph.nodes()[producer].operation, Operation::Add),
                    matches!(node.operation, Operation::Add),
                    slot == 1,
                ));
            } else if let Some(chain) = fused_pointwise_chains.get(&index) {
                let inner = &graph.nodes()[chain[0]];
                let bias_add = &graph.nodes()[chain[1]];
                body.push_str(&pointwise_chain_kernel_ir(
                    index,
                    &inner.operation,
                    bias_add.shape.dims()[1],
                ));
            } else if let Some(&producer) = fused_relus.get(&index) {
                let first = &graph.nodes()[producer];
                let columns = if matches!(first.operation, Operation::BiasAdd) {
                    first.shape.dims()[1]
                } else {
                    0
                };
                body.push_str(&kernel_ir(index, &first.operation, columns, true));
            } else if matches!(node.operation, Operation::MatMul) {
                let left = &graph.nodes()[node.inputs[0].index()];
                body.push_str(&matmul_kernel_ir(
                    index,
                    left.shape.dims()[1],
                    node.shape.dims()[1],
                ));
            } else {
                match &node.operation {
                    Operation::Permute { axes } if axes.as_slice() == [1, 0] => {
                        let input = &graph.nodes()[node.inputs[0].index()];
                        if input.shape.rank() != 2 {
                            return Err(GpuError::UnsupportedOperation {
                                node: index,
                                operation: node.operation.name(),
                            });
                        }
                        body.push_str(&transpose2d_kernel_ir(
                            index,
                            input.shape.dims()[0],
                            input.shape.dims()[1],
                        ));
                    }
                    Operation::ReverseAxis { axis } => {
                        let input = &graph.nodes()[node.inputs[0].index()];
                        if input.shape.rank() != 2 || *axis > 1 {
                            return Err(GpuError::UnsupportedOperation {
                                node: index,
                                operation: node.operation.name(),
                            });
                        }
                        body.push_str(&reverse2d_kernel_ir(
                            index,
                            input.shape.dims()[0],
                            input.shape.dims()[1],
                            *axis,
                        ));
                    }
                    Operation::Concat { axis }
                        if *axis == 0
                            || (*axis == 1
                                && node.shape.rank() == 2
                                && node.shape.dims()[0] == 1) =>
                    {
                        let left = &graph.nodes()[node.inputs[0].index()];
                        body.push_str(&concat_axis0_kernel_ir(index, left.shape.element_count()));
                    }
                    Operation::SliceAxis { axis: 1, start, .. } => {
                        body.push_str(&slice_last_row_kernel_ir(index, *start));
                    }
                    Operation::BroadcastTo(_) => {
                        body.push_str(&broadcast_scalar_kernel_ir(index));
                    }
                    Operation::ArgMax {
                        axis: 1,
                        tie_break: crate::ArgMaxTieBreak::First,
                    } => {
                        let input = &graph.nodes()[node.inputs[0].index()];
                        if input.shape.rank() != 2 {
                            return Err(GpuError::UnsupportedOperation {
                                node: index,
                                operation: node.operation.name(),
                            });
                        }
                        body.push_str(&argmax_last_kernel_ir(index, input.shape.dims()[1]));
                    }
                    Operation::Take { axis: 0 } => {
                        body.push_str(&take_axis0_kernel_ir(index, node.shape.element_count()));
                    }
                    Operation::Permute { .. }
                    | Operation::Concat { .. }
                    | Operation::SliceAxis { .. }
                    | Operation::ArgMax { .. }
                    | Operation::Take { .. } => {
                        return Err(GpuError::UnsupportedOperation {
                            node: index,
                            operation: node.operation.name(),
                        });
                    }
                    _ => {
                        let columns = if matches!(node.operation, Operation::BiasAdd) {
                            node.shape.dims()[1]
                        } else {
                            0
                        };
                        body.push_str(&kernel_ir(index, &node.operation, columns, false));
                    }
                }
            }
            // The generated LLVM body, including its ABI, exact FP32
            // instructions and shape-dependent constants, defines the key.
            // Only the synthetic function name is excluded. No heuristic
            // merging of merely similar graph operations is permitted.
            let name = format!("define ptx_kernel void @vn_node_{index}(");
            let signature = body.strip_prefix(&name).ok_or(GpuError::Fp32PtxRejected {
                reason: format!("generated kernel {index} lacks expected LLVM entrypoint"),
            })?;
            if let Some(&owner) = specializations.get(signature) {
                kernel_entries.insert(index, owner);
            } else {
                specializations.insert(signature.to_owned(), index);
                kernel_entries.insert(index, index);
                llvm_ir.push_str(&body);
            }
        }
        let program = GpuProgram {
            graph: graph.clone(),
            output,
            outputs: outputs.to_vec(),
            live_nodes,
            source_inputs,
            llvm_ir,
            kernel_entries,
            launch: self.launch,
            fused_relus,
            fused_pointwise_chains,
            fused_mul_adds,
            fused_mul_add_muls,
            fused_binary_pairs,
            fused_sqrt_add_divs,
            fused_mul_mul_add_divs,
            fused_mul_diamond_adds,
            fused_dual_outputs,
        };
        // Fail closed unless every launched kernel has matching memory and
        // translation evidence and every applied optimization has valid
        // structural preconditions.
        program.capability_plan()?;
        Ok(program)
    }

    /// Write the inspectable LLVM IR and lower it with LLVM's NVPTX backend.
    /// LLVM must be available in the devShell; a nonzero exit is an error.
    pub fn lower(&self, program: &GpuProgram, dir: &Path) -> Result<PathBuf, GpuError> {
        let profile = std::env::var_os("VERINEURAL_GPU_PREPARE_PROFILE").is_some();
        let lower_started = Instant::now();
        fs::create_dir_all(dir)?;
        let ir = dir.join("graph.ll");
        let ptx = dir.join("graph.ptx");
        fs::write(&ir, program.llvm_ir())?;
        let output = Command::new(&self.llc)
            .arg("-march=nvptx64")
            .arg(format!("-mcpu={}", self.arch))
            .arg(self.codegen_opt_level.llc_flag())
            .arg("-o")
            .arg(&ptx)
            .arg(&ir)
            .output()
            .map_err(|err| GpuError::LlvmFailed {
                diagnostics: format!(
                    "cannot launch LLVM NVPTX compiler '{}': {err}; \
                     verify that it is in PATH (project devShell: `nix develop`)",
                    self.llc.display()
                ),
            })?;
        if !output.status.success() {
            return Err(GpuError::LlvmFailed {
                diagnostics: format!(
                    "status={:?}\nstdout={}\nstderr={}",
                    output.status.code(),
                    String::from_utf8_lossy(&output.stdout),
                    String::from_utf8_lossy(&output.stderr)
                ),
            });
        }
        if profile {
            eprintln!(
                "gpu_nvptx_stage=llc elapsed_ms={:.3} artifact_dir={}",
                lower_started.elapsed().as_secs_f64() * 1000.,
                dir.display()
            );
        }
        let audit_started = Instant::now();
        if profile {
            eprintln!(
                "gpu_nvptx_stage=intern graph_kernels={} unique_functions={}",
                program.kernel_count()?,
                program.unique_kernel_count()
            );
        }
        // Translation validation must succeed before the PTX reaches CUDA JIT.
        // The generated plan is derived from Semantic IR and fusion/memory
        // contracts, while the report is checked from both emitted artifacts.
        let ptx_source = fs::read_to_string(&ptx)?;
        let plan = program.translation_plan()?;
        let validated = plan
            .validate(program.llvm_ir(), &ptx_source)
            .map_err(|err| GpuError::Fp32PtxRejected {
                reason: format!("per-kernel translation validation: {err}"),
            });
        let report = match validated {
            Ok(report) => report,
            Err(err) => {
                let _ = fs::remove_file(&ptx);
                return Err(err);
            }
        };
        fs::write(dir.join("translation.plan"), plan.to_text())?;
        fs::write(dir.join("translation.report"), report.to_text())?;
        fs::write(
            dir.join("capability.plan"),
            program.capability_plan()?.to_text(),
        )?;
        if profile {
            eprintln!(
                "gpu_nvptx_stage=translation_audit elapsed_ms={:.3} artifact_dir={}",
                audit_started.elapsed().as_secs_f64() * 1000.,
                dir.display()
            );
        }
        Ok(ptx)
    }

    pub fn prepare(
        &self,
        program: &GpuProgram,
        inputs: &[(NodeId, Tensor<f32>)],
        output_dir: &Path,
    ) -> Result<GpuExecution, GpuError> {
        // Opt-in setup attribution. Never alter kernel generation, stream
        // ordering, input bindings, FP32 arithmetic or proof claims.
        let profile = std::env::var_os("VERINEURAL_GPU_PREPARE_PROFILE").is_some();
        let total_started = Instant::now();
        let report = |phase: &str, started: Instant| {
            if profile {
                eprintln!(
                    "gpu_prepare_phase={phase} elapsed_ms={:.3} artifact_dir={}",
                    started.elapsed().as_secs_f64() * 1000.,
                    output_dir.display(),
                );
            }
        };
        let contracts = program.memory_contracts()?;
        let given = validate_inputs(program, inputs)?;
        report("preflight", total_started);
        let phase_started = Instant::now();
        let ptx_path = self.lower(program, output_dir)?;
        let ptx = fs::read(ptx_path)?;
        report("lower_and_audit", phase_started);
        let phase_started = Instant::now();
        let mut session = CudaSession::new(&ptx)?;
        report("cuda_module_load", phase_started);
        let phase_started = Instant::now();
        let mut buffers: BTreeMap<usize, u64> = BTreeMap::new();
        let mut input_addresses = BTreeMap::new();
        let skipped = program.skipped_nodes();

        // Preassign all materialized source/output allocations before any
        // CUDA Graph capture. A fused secondary output still needs storage;
        // zero-copy aliases share the exact address of their source.
        // Every checked offset belongs to the single owned CUDA allocation.
        let mut slab_addresses = BTreeMap::new();
        if self.allocation_slab {
            let mut entries = Vec::new();
            for &index in &program.live_nodes {
                if skipped.contains(&index)
                    && !program.fused_dual_outputs.values().any(|&n| n == index)
                {
                    continue;
                }
                let node = &program.graph.nodes()[index];
                if matches!(node.operation, Operation::Input)
                    || matches!(
                        program.graph.storage(node.id)?,
                        NodeStorage::OwnedContiguous { .. }
                    )
                {
                    entries.push((index, node.shape.element_count()));
                }
            }
            let sizes = entries.iter().map(|&(_, size)| size).collect::<Vec<_>>();
            let addresses = session.allocate_batch(&sizes)?;
            slab_addresses.extend(
                entries
                    .into_iter()
                    .zip(addresses)
                    .map(|((index, _), address)| (index, address)),
            );
        }
        let allocate_node = |session: &mut CudaSession, index: usize, elements: usize| {
            if self.allocation_slab {
                slab_addresses
                    .get(&index)
                    .copied()
                    .ok_or(GpuError::InvalidInput {
                        node: index,
                        reason: "missing preallocated slab tensor",
                    })
            } else {
                session.allocate(elements)
            }
        };
        for &index in &program.live_nodes {
            if skipped.contains(&index) && !program.fused_dual_outputs.values().any(|&n| n == index)
            {
                continue;
            }
            let node = &program.graph.nodes()[index];
            let storage = program.graph.storage(node.id)?;
            match (&node.operation, storage) {
                (Operation::Input, _) => {
                    let value = given[&index];
                    let ptr = allocate_node(&mut session, index, value.values().len())?;
                    session.copy_to_device(ptr, value.values())?;
                    input_addresses.insert(index, ptr);
                    buffers.insert(index, ptr);
                }
                (_, NodeStorage::Alias { source, .. }) => {
                    let ptr = buffers[&source.index()];
                    buffers.insert(index, ptr);
                }
                (
                    Operation::Add
                    | Operation::Mul
                    | Operation::MatMul
                    | Operation::BiasAdd
                    | Operation::Relu
                    | Operation::Permute { .. }
                    | Operation::ReverseAxis { .. }
                    | Operation::Concat { .. }
                    | Operation::SliceAxis { .. }
                    | Operation::BroadcastTo(_)
                    | Operation::ArgMax { .. }
                    | Operation::Take { .. }
                    | Operation::Pointwise(_),
                    NodeStorage::OwnedContiguous { .. },
                ) => {
                    let ptr = allocate_node(&mut session, index, node.shape.element_count())?;
                    buffers.insert(index, ptr);
                }
                _ => unreachable!("the compilation pass rejected unsupported nodes"),
            }
        }

        if profile {
            let materialized_tensors = buffers.values().copied().collect::<BTreeSet<_>>().len();
            eprintln!(
                "gpu_prepare_allocations mode={} materialized_tensors={} cuda_allocations={} artifact_dir={}",
                if self.allocation_slab {
                    "slab"
                } else {
                    "separate"
                },
                materialized_tensors,
                if self.allocation_slab {
                    usize::from(materialized_tensors != 0)
                } else {
                    materialized_tensors
                },
                output_dir.display(),
            );
        }
        report("allocate_and_initial_h2d", phase_started);
        let phase_started = Instant::now();
        // Validate the *allocated* buffers as well as the abstract shapes
        // before capturing any kernel into the CUDA Graph. Each output has
        // its own allocation; aliases are allowed only for zero-copy Reshape
        // inputs, never for an output being written by this kernel.
        let mut written_buffers = BTreeSet::new();
        for contract in &contracts {
            let output_ptr = buffers[&contract.kernel_node];
            session.require_allocation(output_ptr, contract.writes)?;
            for &(other, elements) in &contract.additional_writes {
                let ptr = buffers[&other];
                session.require_allocation(ptr, elements)?;
                if ptr == output_ptr || !written_buffers.insert(ptr) {
                    return Err(GpuError::InvalidInput {
                        node: contract.kernel_node,
                        reason: "multi-output CUDA kernel has overlapping output allocations",
                    });
                }
            }
            if !written_buffers.insert(output_ptr) {
                return Err(GpuError::InvalidInput {
                    node: contract.kernel_node,
                    reason: "two CUDA kernel nodes write the same output allocation",
                });
            }
            for &(source, elements) in &contract.reads {
                let input_ptr = buffers[&source];
                session.require_allocation(input_ptr, elements)?;
                if input_ptr == output_ptr
                    || contract
                        .additional_writes
                        .iter()
                        .any(|&(other, _)| input_ptr == buffers[&other])
                {
                    return Err(GpuError::InvalidInput {
                        node: contract.kernel_node,
                        reason: "in-place CUDA kernel write is not supported",
                    });
                }
            }
        }

        report("memory_contracts", phase_started);
        let kernel_count = contracts.len();
        let has_graph = kernel_count > 0;
        if has_graph {
            let phase_started = Instant::now();
            for entry in program
                .kernel_entries
                .values()
                .copied()
                .collect::<BTreeSet<_>>()
            {
                session.prepare_kernel(&format!("vn_node_{entry}"))?;
            }
            report("kernel_resolution", phase_started);
            let phase_started = Instant::now();
            session.begin_graph()?;
            for contract in &contracts {
                let index = contract.kernel_node;
                let entry = program.kernel_entries[&index];
                let inputs = contract
                    .reads
                    .iter()
                    .map(|&(node, _)| buffers[&node])
                    .collect::<Vec<_>>();
                if let Some(&(other, _)) = contract.additional_writes.first() {
                    if contract.additional_writes.len() != 1 || inputs.len() != 4 {
                        return Err(GpuError::InvalidInput {
                            node: index,
                            reason: "invalid dual-output kernel ABI",
                        });
                    }
                    session.launch4_dual(
                        &format!("vn_node_{entry}"),
                        [inputs[0], inputs[1], inputs[2], inputs[3]],
                        [buffers[&other], buffers[&index]],
                        contract.writes,
                        program.launch.threads_per_block,
                    )?;
                } else if inputs.len() == 4 {
                    session.launch4(
                        &format!("vn_node_{entry}"),
                        [inputs[0], inputs[1], inputs[2], inputs[3]],
                        buffers[&index],
                        contract.writes,
                        program.launch.threads_per_block,
                    )?;
                } else if inputs.len() == 3 {
                    session.launch3(
                        &format!("vn_node_{entry}"),
                        [inputs[0], inputs[1], inputs[2]],
                        buffers[&index],
                        contract.writes,
                        program.launch.threads_per_block,
                    )?;
                } else {
                    session.launch(
                        &format!("vn_node_{entry}"),
                        inputs[0],
                        inputs.get(1).copied().unwrap_or(0),
                        buffers[&index],
                        contract.writes,
                        program.launch.threads_per_block,
                    )?;
                }
            }
            report("graph_capture", phase_started);
            let phase_started = Instant::now();
            session.finish_graph()?;
            report("graph_instantiate", phase_started);
        }
        report("total_before_execution", total_started);

        let last = program.graph.node(program.output)?;
        let output_addresses = program
            .outputs
            .iter()
            .map(|&id| {
                let node = program.graph.node(id)?;
                let address = *buffers.get(&id.index()).ok_or(GpuError::InvalidInput {
                    node: id.index(),
                    reason: "selected output does not own a live CUDA buffer",
                })?;
                Ok((id, node.shape.clone(), address))
            })
            .collect::<Result<Vec<_>, GpuError>>()?;
        let output_address_lookup = output_addresses
            .iter()
            .enumerate()
            .map(|(slot, (id, _, _))| (id.index(), slot))
            .collect();
        Ok(GpuExecution {
            session,
            program: program.clone(),
            input_addresses,
            output_shape: last.shape.clone(),
            output_address: buffers[&program.output.index()],
            output_addresses,
            output_address_lookup,
            preserved_output_addresses: BTreeMap::new(),
            feedback_observable_outputs: None,
            feedback_snapshot_destinations: BTreeSet::new(),
            prepared_feedback: None,
            preserved_output_valid: Cell::new(false),
            execution_health: ExecutionHealth::default(),
            has_graph,
        })
    }

    /// Prepare independent executions of one compiled graph, each with its
    /// own CUDA allocations, non-blocking stream and source inventory.
    /// Validate every member's source set before preparing *any* session,
    /// so a malformed late member cannot trigger partial CUDA allocation.
    /// Each prepared session may be fed different tokens/state independently;
    /// this does not aggregate gradients or share trainable weights.
    pub fn prepare_independent(
        &self,
        program: &GpuProgram,
        batches: &[Vec<(NodeId, Tensor<f32>)>],
        output_dir: &Path,
    ) -> Result<Vec<GpuExecution>, GpuError> {
        if batches.is_empty() {
            return Err(GpuError::InvalidInput {
                node: program.output.index(),
                reason: "independent GPU batch must not be empty",
            });
        }
        for inputs in batches {
            validate_inputs(program, inputs)?;
        }
        batches
            .iter()
            .enumerate()
            .map(|(i, inputs)| {
                self.prepare(
                    program,
                    inputs,
                    &output_dir.join(format!("instance_{i:04}")),
                )
            })
            .collect()
    }

    /// Evaluate all outputs with one shared CUDA Graph capture and replay,
    /// preserving each output's Semantic IR dtype.
    pub fn execute_values(
        &self,
        program: &GpuProgram,
        inputs: &[(NodeId, Tensor<f32>)],
        output_dir: &Path,
    ) -> Result<Vec<(NodeId, TensorValue)>, GpuError> {
        let mut execution = self.prepare(program, inputs, output_dir)?;
        execution.replay()?;
        execution.read_values()
    }

    /// Backward-compatible all-F32 shared execution.
    pub fn execute_outputs(
        &self,
        program: &GpuProgram,
        inputs: &[(NodeId, Tensor<f32>)],
        output_dir: &Path,
    ) -> Result<Vec<(NodeId, Tensor<f32>)>, GpuError> {
        let mut execution = self.prepare(program, inputs, output_dir)?;
        execution.replay()?;
        execution.read_outputs()
    }

    /// Evaluate the primary output while preserving its Semantic IR dtype.
    pub fn execute_value(
        &self,
        program: &GpuProgram,
        inputs: &[(NodeId, Tensor<f32>)],
        output_dir: &Path,
    ) -> Result<TensorValue, GpuError> {
        let mut execution = self.prepare(program, inputs, output_dir)?;
        execution.replay()?;
        execution.read_value()
    }

    /// Backward-compatible F32 primary execution.
    pub fn execute(
        &self,
        program: &GpuProgram,
        inputs: &[(NodeId, Tensor<f32>)],
        output_dir: &Path,
    ) -> Result<Tensor<f32>, GpuError> {
        let mut execution = self.prepare(program, inputs, output_dir)?;
        execution.replay()?;
        execution.read_output()
    }
}


FILE	crates/verineural/src/gpu/execution.rs
//! Prepared CUDA Graph execution and reusable state/feedback transfers.

use super::*;

impl GpuExecution {
    /// Replace all reachable graph inputs without rebuilding the CUDA Graph.
    /// Validate the full batch before the first transfer, so rejected input
    /// metadata cannot partially replace the previous input set.
    /// Transfers finish on the owned non-blocking stream before returning.
    pub fn update_inputs(&mut self, inputs: &[(NodeId, Tensor<f32>)]) -> Result<(), GpuError> {
        self.execution_health.ensure_ready()?;
        let given = validate_inputs(&self.program, inputs)?;
        self.execution_health.invalidate_outputs();
        self.preserved_output_valid.set(false);
        for id in self.program.source_inputs() {
            self.execution_health
                .record_io(self.session.copy_to_device(
                    self.input_addresses[&id.index()],
                    given[&id.index()].values(),
                ))?;
        }
        self.execution_health
            .record_io(self.session.flush_input_copies())
    }

    /// Update an arbitrary *subset* of reachable F32 source tensors.
    /// All IDs, uniqueness, shapes and domains are checked before enqueueing
    /// the first H2D copy. Pinned host staging is kept alive until a single
    /// synchronization of the owned non-blocking stream. All other inputs
    /// retain their previous device values.
    pub fn update_input_subset(
        &mut self,
        inputs: &[(NodeId, &Tensor<f32>)],
    ) -> Result<(), GpuError> {
        self.update_input_subset_impl(inputs, false)
    }

    /// Experimental packed H2D upload, using one DMA and a cached CUDA Graph
    /// scatter. Validates the complete subset before any upload.
    pub fn update_input_subset_packed(
        &mut self,
        inputs: &[(NodeId, &Tensor<f32>)],
    ) -> Result<(), GpuError> {
        self.update_input_subset_impl(inputs, true)
    }

    fn update_input_subset_impl(
        &mut self,
        inputs: &[(NodeId, &Tensor<f32>)],
        packed: bool,
    ) -> Result<(), GpuError> {
        self.execution_health.ensure_ready()?;
        let mut seen = BTreeSet::new();
        for &(id, value) in inputs {
            if !seen.insert(id.index()) {
                return Err(GpuError::InvalidInput {
                    node: id.index(),
                    reason: "duplicate partial input update",
                });
            }
            if !self.input_addresses.contains_key(&id.index()) {
                return Err(GpuError::InvalidInput {
                    node: id.index(),
                    reason: "source is outside the compiled output slice",
                });
            }
            let node = self.program.graph.node(id)?;
            if value.shape() != &node.shape {
                return Err(GpuError::InvalidGraph(NeuralError::ShapeMismatch {
                    expected: node.shape.clone(),
                    actual: value.shape().clone(),
                }));
            }
            value.validate_domain(node.domain)?;
        }
        if inputs.is_empty() {
            return Ok(());
        }
        self.execution_health.invalidate_outputs();
        self.preserved_output_valid.set(false);
        if packed {
            let transfers = inputs
                .iter()
                .map(|&(id, value)| (self.input_addresses[&id.index()], value.values()))
                .collect::<Vec<_>>();
            self.execution_health
                .record_io(self.session.copy_f32_batch_to_device_packed(&transfers))
        } else {
            for &(id, value) in inputs {
                self.execution_health.record_io(
                    self.session
                        .copy_to_device(self.input_addresses[&id.index()], value.values()),
                )?;
            }
            self.execution_health
                .record_io(self.session.flush_input_copies())
        }
    }

    /// Rebind one named source without uploading unchanged parameters or state.
    /// Metadata and domain are checked before touching GPU memory.
    pub fn update_input(&mut self, id: NodeId, value: &Tensor<f32>) -> Result<(), GpuError> {
        self.execution_health.ensure_ready()?;
        let node = self.program.graph.node(id)?;
        if !self.input_addresses.contains_key(&id.index()) {
            return Err(GpuError::InvalidInput {
                node: id.index(),
                reason: "source is outside the compiled output slice",
            });
        }
        if value.shape() != &node.shape {
            return Err(GpuError::InvalidGraph(NeuralError::ShapeMismatch {
                expected: node.shape.clone(),
                actual: value.shape().clone(),
            }));
        }
        value.validate_domain(node.domain)?;
        let address = self.input_addresses[&id.index()];
        self.execution_health.invalidate_outputs();
        self.preserved_output_valid.set(false);
        self.execution_health
            .record_io(self.session.copy_to_device(address, value.values()))?;
        self.execution_health
            .record_io(self.session.flush_input_copies())
    }

    /// Establish the static state feedback memory contract before any replay.
    /// Public outputs that alias state inputs receive persistent device
    /// snapshots so step() cannot overwrite observable pure-step results.
    pub(crate) fn configure_model_feedback(
        &mut self,
        public_outputs: &[NodeId],
        links: &[(NodeId, NodeId)],
    ) -> Result<(), GpuError> {
        self.configure_feedback(public_outputs, links, false)
    }

    fn configure_feedback(
        &mut self,
        public_outputs: &[NodeId],
        links: &[(NodeId, NodeId)],
        runtime_domains: bool,
    ) -> Result<(), GpuError> {
        self.execution_health.ensure_ready()?;
        self.feedback_copy_plan(links, runtime_domains)?;
        let destinations = links
            .iter()
            .map(|&(state, _)| self.input_addresses[&state.index()])
            .collect::<BTreeSet<_>>();
        // Internal state roots are not observable to ModelExecution clients.
        let mut checked = BTreeSet::new();
        for &output in public_outputs {
            if !checked.insert(output.index()) {
                return Err(GpuError::InvalidInput {
                    node: output.index(),
                    reason: "duplicate observable feedback output",
                });
            }
            let (shape, address) = self
                .output_addresses
                .iter()
                .find(|(node, _, _)| *node == output)
                .map(|(_, shape, address)| (shape.clone(), *address))
                .ok_or(GpuError::InvalidInput {
                    node: output.index(),
                    reason: "public output is not in the compiled GPU program",
                })?;
            if destinations.contains(&address)
                && !self
                    .preserved_output_addresses
                    .contains_key(&output.index())
            {
                let snapshot = self.session.allocate(shape.element_count())?;
                self.preserved_output_addresses
                    .insert(output.index(), snapshot);
            }
        }
        self.feedback_snapshot_destinations.extend(destinations);
        self.feedback_observable_outputs = Some(public_outputs.to_vec());
        Ok(())
    }

    /// Save the pure step's observable values before writing feedback state.
    /// All copies stay on the owned non-blocking stream; no host round-trip.
    pub(crate) fn snapshot_outputs(&mut self) -> Result<(), GpuError> {
        self.execution_health.ensure_outputs_ready()?;
        self.preserved_output_valid.set(false);
        for (&index, &snapshot) in &self.preserved_output_addresses {
            let (_, shape, source) = self
                .output_addresses
                .iter()
                .find(|(node, _, _)| node.index() == index)
                .expect("configured public output has a live buffer");
            self.execution_health
                .record_io(self.session.copy_device_to_device(
                    snapshot,
                    *source,
                    shape.element_count(),
                ))?;
        }
        if !self.preserved_output_addresses.is_empty() {
            self.execution_health
                .record_io(self.session.synchronize())?;
        }
        self.preserved_output_valid.set(true);
        Ok(())
    }

    fn read_value_at(
        &mut self,
        id: NodeId,
        shape: &Shape,
        address: u64,
    ) -> Result<TensorValue, GpuError> {
        match self.program.graph.node(id)?.dtype {
            DType::F32 => {
                let mut values = vec![0.0f32; shape.element_count()];
                self.execution_health
                    .record_io(self.session.copy_to_host(&mut values, address))?;
                Ok(TensorValue::F32(Tensor::new(shape.clone(), values)?))
            }
            DType::Index => {
                let mut raw = vec![0i32; shape.element_count()];
                self.execution_health
                    .record_io(self.session.copy_indices_to_host(&mut raw, address))?;
                let values = raw
                    .into_iter()
                    .map(|value| {
                        usize::try_from(value).map_err(|_| GpuError::InvalidInput {
                            node: id.index(),
                            reason: "device index output is negative",
                        })
                    })
                    .collect::<Result<Vec<_>, _>>()?;
                Ok(TensorValue::Index(Tensor::new(shape.clone(), values)?))
            }
        }
    }

    /// Read one selected output while preserving its Semantic IR dtype.
    pub(crate) fn read_selected_value(&mut self, id: NodeId) -> Result<TensorValue, GpuError> {
        self.execution_health.ensure_outputs_ready()?;
        let (_, shape, live) = self
            .output_addresses
            .iter()
            .find(|(node, _, _)| *node == id)
            .cloned()
            .ok_or(GpuError::InvalidInput {
                node: id.index(),
                reason: "requested output is not selected",
            })?;
        let address = if self.preserved_output_valid.get() {
            self.preserved_output_addresses
                .get(&id.index())
                .copied()
                .unwrap_or(live)
        } else {
            live
        };
        self.read_value_at(id, &shape, address)
    }

    /// Backward-compatible F32 reader. Index outputs must use the typed API.
    pub(crate) fn read_selected_output(&mut self, id: NodeId) -> Result<Tensor<f32>, GpuError> {
        match self.read_selected_value(id)? {
            TensorValue::F32(tensor) => Ok(tensor),
            TensorValue::Index(_) => Err(GpuError::InvalidGraph(NeuralError::DTypeMismatch {
                operation: "read_selected_output",
                expected: DType::F32,
                actual: DType::Index,
            })),
        }
    }

    /// Validate feedback shape, dtype, domain, liveness and alias order.
    fn feedback_copy_plan(
        &self,
        links: &[(NodeId, NodeId)],
        runtime_domains: bool,
    ) -> Result<Vec<(u64, u64, usize)>, GpuError> {
        let mut destinations = BTreeSet::new();
        let output_lookup = self
            .output_addresses
            .iter()
            .map(|(id, _, address)| (id.index(), *address))
            .collect::<BTreeMap<_, _>>();
        let mut copies = Vec::with_capacity(links.len());
        for &(state, next) in links {
            let old = self.program.graph.node(state)?;
            let new = self.program.graph.node(next)?;
            if !destinations.insert(state.index()) {
                return Err(GpuError::InvalidInput {
                    node: state.index(),
                    reason: "duplicate state feedback destination",
                });
            }
            if old.shape != new.shape {
                return Err(GpuError::InvalidGraph(NeuralError::ShapeMismatch {
                    expected: old.shape.clone(),
                    actual: new.shape.clone(),
                }));
            }
            if new.dtype != old.dtype {
                return Err(GpuError::InvalidGraph(NeuralError::DTypeMismatch {
                    operation: "feedback_state",
                    expected: old.dtype,
                    actual: new.dtype,
                }));
            }
            if !runtime_domains && !new.domain.satisfies(old.domain) {
                return Err(GpuError::InvalidGraph(NeuralError::DomainNotEstablished {
                    required: old.domain,
                    actual: new.domain,
                }));
            }
            let &dest = self
                .input_addresses
                .get(&state.index())
                .ok_or(GpuError::InvalidInput {
                    node: state.index(),
                    reason: "feedback destination is not a live source",
                })?;
            let &src = output_lookup
                .get(&next.index())
                .ok_or(GpuError::InvalidInput {
                    node: next.index(),
                    reason: "feedback source is not a selected output",
                })?;
            copies.push((dest, src, old.shape.element_count()));
        }
        // Feedback is a parallel, simultaneous assignment. Reject duplicate
        // storage roots and cross-transfer read/write aliasing in O(n log n)
        // rather than comparing every pair of hundreds of optimizer tensors.
        let destinations = copies
            .iter()
            .map(|&(dest, _, _)| dest)
            .collect::<BTreeSet<_>>();
        if destinations.len() != copies.len()
            || copies
                .iter()
                .any(|&(dest, src, _)| dest != src && destinations.contains(&src))
        {
            return Err(GpuError::InvalidInput {
                node: 0,
                reason: "overlapping state feedback sources require staging",
            });
        }
        Ok(copies)
    }

    fn prepared_feedback_plan(
        &mut self,
        links: &[(NodeId, NodeId)],
        runtime_domains: bool,
    ) -> Result<Rc<PreparedFeedback>, GpuError> {
        if let Some(cached) = &self.prepared_feedback {
            if cached.runtime_domains == runtime_domains && cached.links.as_slice() == links {
                return Ok(Rc::clone(cached));
            }
        }
        // A miss must run the original complete preflight before publishing
        // the cache entry or enqueuing a single GPU state transfer.
        let copies = self.feedback_copy_plan(links, runtime_domains)?;
        let mut checked_sources = Vec::new();
        let mut checked_requirements = Vec::new();
        let mut checked_values = 0usize;
        if runtime_domains {
            let output_lookup = self
                .output_addresses
                .iter()
                .map(|(id, _, address)| (id.index(), *address))
                .collect::<BTreeMap<_, _>>();
            for &(state, next) in links {
                let old = self.program.graph.node(state)?;
                let new = self.program.graph.node(next)?;
                if new.domain.satisfies(old.domain) {
                    continue;
                }
                if old.dtype != DType::F32 {
                    return Err(GpuError::InvalidInput {
                        node: state.index(),
                        reason: "runtime feedback domain check requires F32",
                    });
                }
                let elements = old.shape.element_count();
                let &address = output_lookup
                    .get(&next.index())
                    .ok_or(GpuError::InvalidInput {
                        node: next.index(),
                        reason: "feedback source is not a selected output",
                    })?;
                checked_sources.push((address, elements, old.domain == Domain::NonNegativeFinite));
                checked_requirements.push((old.domain, old.shape.clone()));
                checked_values += elements;
            }
        }
        let transfers = copies
            .iter()
            .copied()
            .filter(|(dst, src, _)| dst != src)
            .collect::<Vec<_>>();
        let feedback_values = transfers.iter().map(|&(_, _, n)| n).sum();
        let prepared = Rc::new(PreparedFeedback {
            links: links.to_vec(),
            runtime_domains,
            copies,
            transfers,
            checked_sources,
            checked_requirements,
            checked_values,
            feedback_values,
        });
        self.prepared_feedback = Some(Rc::clone(&prepared));
        Ok(prepared)
    }

    /// Strict feedback for statically established source domains.
    /// Selected outputs aliasing state destinations are device-snapshotted.
    pub fn feedback_state(&mut self, links: &[(NodeId, NodeId)]) -> Result<(), GpuError> {
        self.feedback_state_impl(links, false, false).map(|_| ())
    }

    /// Experimental feedback for outputs with weaker *static* domain
    /// contracts. A separate CUDA Graph checks their FP32 bit patterns and
    /// returns one 32-bit failure flag before **any** state copy. On rejection,
    /// full tensors are read solely to report the exact host-domain error.
    /// No assumption that arbitrary FP32 arithmetic remains finite is
    /// smuggled into IR. The guard is runtime hardware validation, not proof.
    pub fn feedback_state_checked(&mut self, links: &[(NodeId, NodeId)]) -> Result<(), GpuError> {
        self.feedback_state_checked_profiled(links).map(|_| ())
    }

    /// Checked feedback plus stage-separated host timings. Validation is
    /// mandatory and happens before any state mutation, just as in the
    /// unprofiled API. No extra device readback is performed for profiling.
    pub fn feedback_state_checked_profiled(
        &mut self,
        links: &[(NodeId, NodeId)],
    ) -> Result<GpuFeedbackProfile, GpuError> {
        self.feedback_state_impl(links, true, false)
    }

    /// Diagnostic-only variant: measures the copy CUDA Graph with stream
    /// events. This introduces an extra barrier and must never be used to
    /// claim end-to-end speedups. Runtime domain checks remain mandatory.
    pub fn feedback_state_checked_device_profiled(
        &mut self,
        links: &[(NodeId, NodeId)],
    ) -> Result<GpuFeedbackProfile, GpuError> {
        self.feedback_state_impl(links, true, true)
    }

    fn feedback_state_impl(
        &mut self,
        links: &[(NodeId, NodeId)],
        runtime_domains: bool,
        device_events: bool,
    ) -> Result<GpuFeedbackProfile, GpuError> {
        let plan_started = Instant::now();
        self.execution_health.ensure_outputs_ready()?;
        let plan = self.prepared_feedback_plan(links, runtime_domains)?;
        let mut profile = GpuFeedbackProfile {
            plan_host: plan_started.elapsed(),
            checked_values: plan.checked_values,
            feedback_values: plan.feedback_values,
            ..GpuFeedbackProfile::default()
        };
        if plan.copies.is_empty() {
            return Ok(profile);
        }
        if runtime_domains && !plan.checked_sources.is_empty() {
            let validation_started = Instant::now();
            // Descriptors may be cached, but current FP32 output bytes must
            // be checked before every state mutation.
            let domains_valid = self
                .execution_health
                .record_io(self.session.validate_output_domains(&plan.checked_sources))?;
            if !domains_valid {
                // Reject before writing state; exact host oracle is reserved
                // for the exceptional path and retains source order.
                let buffers = plan
                    .checked_sources
                    .iter()
                    .map(|&(address, size, _)| (address, size))
                    .collect::<Vec<_>>();
                let copied = self
                    .execution_health
                    .record_io(self.session.copy_f32_batch_to_host(&buffers))?;
                for ((required, shape), values) in plan.checked_requirements.iter().zip(copied) {
                    Tensor::new(shape.clone(), values)?.validate_domain(*required)?;
                }
                return Err(GpuError::Driver(
                    "GPU domain guard rejected outputs not rejected by the host oracle".into(),
                ));
            }
            profile.validation_d2h = validation_started.elapsed();
        }
        if plan
            .copies
            .iter()
            .any(|&(dst, _, _)| !self.feedback_snapshot_destinations.contains(&dst))
        {
            let observable = self
                .feedback_observable_outputs
                .clone()
                .unwrap_or_else(|| self.program.outputs().to_vec());
            self.configure_feedback(&observable, links, runtime_domains)?;
        }
        let snapshot_started = Instant::now();
        self.snapshot_outputs()?;
        profile.snapshot_d2d = snapshot_started.elapsed();
        let feedback_started = Instant::now();
        if device_events {
            profile.device_copy = Some(
                self.execution_health.record_io(
                    self.session
                        .launch_feedback_copies_device_timed(&plan.transfers),
                )?,
            );
        } else {
            self.execution_health
                .record_io(self.session.launch_feedback_copies(&plan.transfers))?;
        }
        profile.feedback_d2d = feedback_started.elapsed();
        let sync_started = Instant::now();
        self.execution_health
            .record_io(self.session.synchronize())?;
        profile.stream_sync = sync_started.elapsed();
        Ok(profile)
    }

    /// Read a current source (for state inspection) without another replay.
    pub fn read_source(&mut self, id: NodeId) -> Result<Tensor<f32>, GpuError> {
        self.execution_health.ensure_ready()?;
        let node = self.program.graph.node(id)?;
        let address =
            self.input_addresses
                .get(&id.index())
                .copied()
                .ok_or(GpuError::InvalidInput {
                    node: id.index(),
                    reason: "source is outside the compiled output slice",
                })?;
        let mut values = vec![0.0f32; node.shape.element_count()];
        self.execution_health
            .record_io(self.session.copy_to_host(&mut values, address))?;
        Ok(Tensor::new(node.shape.clone(), values)?)
    }

    /// Queue a CUDA Graph replay without synchronizing the stream.
    ///
    /// Other independent executions can enqueue work on their own
    /// non-blocking streams before any synchronization. The outputs remain
    /// inaccessible until `complete_replay` returns successfully. Every
    /// data transfer, feedback and second replay fail closed while pending.
    pub fn enqueue_replay(&self) -> Result<(), GpuError> {
        self.execution_health.begin_replay()?;
        self.preserved_output_valid.set(false);
        if self.has_graph {
            self.execution_health
                .record_io(self.session.launch_graph())?;
        }
        Ok(())
    }

    /// Synchronize this execution's stream and publish the replay outputs.
    pub fn complete_replay(&self) -> Result<(), GpuError> {
        self.execution_health.ensure_pending()?;
        self.execution_health
            .record_io(self.session.synchronize())?;
        self.execution_health.finish_replay()
    }

    /// Legacy synchronous single-execution path, preserving its contract.
    pub fn replay(&self) -> Result<(), GpuError> {
        self.enqueue_replay()?;
        self.complete_replay()
    }

    /// Launch independent CUDA Graph executions on distinct non-blocking
    /// streams before waiting for any of them. No sharing or aliasing of
    /// mutable source buffers between these owned executions is allowed by
    /// their separate CUDA allocations. This is independent inference/
    /// training-task parallelism, **not** gradient accumulation.
    ///
    /// Synchronize every already-launched stream even on an enqueue or
    /// completion error, preventing a stranded pending execution. CUDA
    /// hardware may serialize kernels; concurrency is not guaranteed.
    pub fn replay_independent_batch(executions: &mut [Self]) -> Result<(), GpuError> {
        if executions.is_empty() {
            return Err(GpuError::InvalidInput {
                node: 0,
                reason: "independent GPU execution batch must not be empty",
            });
        }
        // Fail before launching any new work when another member is still
        // pending or has an unrecoverable CUDA failure.
        for execution in executions.iter() {
            execution.execution_health.ensure_ready()?;
        }
        let mut queued = 0usize;
        for execution in executions.iter() {
            if let Err(err) = execution.enqueue_replay() {
                for previous in &executions[..queued] {
                    let _ = previous.complete_replay();
                }
                return Err(err);
            }
            queued += 1;
        }
        let mut first_error = None;
        for execution in executions.iter().take(queued) {
            if let Err(err) = execution.complete_replay() {
                if first_error.is_none() {
                    first_error = Some(err);
                }
            }
        }
        if let Some(err) = first_error {
            Err(err)
        } else {
            Ok(())
        }
    }

    /// Read the primary output while preserving its Semantic IR dtype.
    pub fn read_value(&mut self) -> Result<TensorValue, GpuError> {
        self.execution_health.ensure_outputs_ready()?;
        let id = self.program.output;
        let shape = self.output_shape.clone();
        let address = if self.preserved_output_valid.get() {
            self.preserved_output_addresses
                .get(&id.index())
                .copied()
                .unwrap_or(self.output_address)
        } else {
            self.output_address
        };
        self.read_value_at(id, &shape, address)
    }

    /// Backward-compatible F32 primary-output reader.
    pub fn read_output(&mut self) -> Result<Tensor<f32>, GpuError> {
        match self.read_value()? {
            TensorValue::F32(tensor) => Ok(tensor),
            TensorValue::Index(_) => Err(GpuError::InvalidGraph(NeuralError::DTypeMismatch {
                operation: "read_output",
                expected: DType::F32,
                actual: DType::Index,
            })),
        }
    }

    /// Read each selected output in declaration order, preserving every dtype.
    pub fn read_values(&mut self) -> Result<Vec<(NodeId, TensorValue)>, GpuError> {
        self.execution_health.ensure_outputs_ready()?;
        let outputs = self.output_addresses.clone();
        let mut result = Vec::with_capacity(outputs.len());
        for (node, shape, pointer) in outputs {
            let address = if self.preserved_output_valid.get() {
                self.preserved_output_addresses
                    .get(&node.index())
                    .copied()
                    .unwrap_or(pointer)
            } else {
                pointer
            };
            result.push((node, self.read_value_at(node, &shape, address)?));
        }
        Ok(result)
    }

    /// Read a requested subset of selected F32 outputs in caller order.
    /// All source IDs, duplicate IDs and dtypes are prevalidated before DMA.
    /// One stream barrier completes all queued D2H copies, with pinned staging
    /// retained until then. Results aliasing preserved state snapshots use the
    /// same snapshot selection as read_selected_value().
    pub fn read_outputs_selected(
        &mut self,
        selected: &[NodeId],
    ) -> Result<Vec<(NodeId, Tensor<f32>)>, GpuError> {
        self.read_outputs_selected_profiled(selected)
            .map(|(outputs, _)| outputs)
    }

    /// Identical output semantics to `read_outputs_selected`, additionally
    /// reporting wall-clock host/transfer phases and copied F32 byte count.
    pub fn read_outputs_selected_profiled(
        &mut self,
        selected: &[NodeId],
    ) -> Result<GpuProfiledReadback, GpuError> {
        self.read_outputs_selected_profiled_impl(selected, false)
    }

    /// Experimental: gather all selected outputs through a reusable CUDA
    /// Graph and issue one D2H transfer. No new FP32 computation is performed.
    pub fn read_outputs_selected_packed_profiled(
        &mut self,
        selected: &[NodeId],
    ) -> Result<GpuProfiledReadback, GpuError> {
        self.read_outputs_selected_profiled_impl(selected, true)
    }

    fn read_outputs_selected_profiled_impl(
        &mut self,
        selected: &[NodeId],
        packed: bool,
    ) -> Result<GpuProfiledReadback, GpuError> {
        self.execution_health.ensure_outputs_ready()?;
        let preflight_started = Instant::now();
        let mut seen = BTreeSet::new();
        let mut sources = Vec::with_capacity(selected.len());
        for &id in selected {
            if !seen.insert(id.index()) {
                return Err(GpuError::InvalidInput {
                    node: id.index(),
                    reason: "duplicate selected read output",
                });
            }
            let &slot =
                self.output_address_lookup
                    .get(&id.index())
                    .ok_or(GpuError::InvalidInput {
                        node: id.index(),
                        reason: "requested output is not selected",
                    })?;
            let (_, shape, original) = &self.output_addresses[slot];
            let node = self.program.graph.node(id)?;
            if node.dtype != DType::F32 {
                return Err(GpuError::InvalidGraph(NeuralError::DTypeMismatch {
                    operation: "read_outputs_selected",
                    expected: DType::F32,
                    actual: node.dtype,
                }));
            }
            let address = if self.preserved_output_valid.get() {
                self.preserved_output_addresses
                    .get(&id.index())
                    .copied()
                    .unwrap_or(*original)
            } else {
                *original
            };
            sources.push((id, shape.clone(), address));
        }
        let preflight = preflight_started.elapsed();
        if sources.is_empty() {
            return Ok((
                Vec::new(),
                GpuReadbackProfile {
                    preflight,
                    ..GpuReadbackProfile::default()
                },
            ));
        }
        let buffers = sources
            .iter()
            .map(|(_, shape, address)| (*address, shape.element_count()))
            .collect::<Vec<_>>();
        let transfer = if packed {
            self.session
                .copy_f32_batch_to_host_packed_profiled(&buffers)
        } else {
            self.session.copy_f32_batch_to_host_profiled(&buffers)
        };
        let (copied, timing) = self.execution_health.record_io(transfer)?;
        let construct_started = Instant::now();
        let outputs = sources
            .into_iter()
            .zip(copied)
            .map(|((id, shape, _), values)| Ok((id, Tensor::new(shape, values)?)))
            .collect::<Result<Vec<_>, GpuError>>()?;
        Ok((
            outputs,
            GpuReadbackProfile {
                preflight,
                enqueue: timing.enqueue,
                synchronize: timing.synchronize,
                host_copy: timing.host_copy,
                tensor_construct: construct_started.elapsed(),
                transfers: timing.transfers,
                bytes: timing.bytes,
            },
        ))
    }

    /// Backward-compatible all-F32 reader, now batched in declaration order.
    /// Mixed/Index output sets fail closed.
    pub fn read_outputs(&mut self) -> Result<Vec<(NodeId, Tensor<f32>)>, GpuError> {
        let selected = self.program.outputs().to_vec();
        self.read_outputs_selected(&selected)
    }

    pub fn benchmark(
        &self,
        warmup_launches: usize,
        measured_launches: usize,
    ) -> Result<GpuBenchmark, GpuError> {
        self.execution_health.ensure_ready()?;
        if measured_launches == 0 {
            return Err(GpuError::InvalidBenchmark { iterations: 0 });
        }
        if !self.has_graph {
            return Err(GpuError::NoKernelGraph);
        }
        self.execution_health.invalidate_outputs();
        self.preserved_output_valid.set(false);
        let milliseconds = self.execution_health.record_io(
            self.session
                .benchmark_graph(warmup_launches, measured_launches),
        )?;
        if !milliseconds.is_finite() || milliseconds < 0.0 {
            return Err(GpuError::Driver(
                "CUDA event benchmark returned an invalid duration".into(),
            ));
        }
        // benchmark_graph synchronizes the stop event, so the final measured
        // replay has completed and its output buffers are safe to read.
        self.execution_health.outputs_completed();
        Ok(GpuBenchmark {
            warmup_launches,
            measured_launches,
            elapsed: Duration::from_secs_f64(f64::from(milliseconds) / 1000.0),
        })
    }
}


FILE	crates/verineural/src/gpu/kernels.rs
//! Architecture-neutral LLVM/NVPTX kernel templates.

use super::*;

pub(super) fn kernel_ir(index: usize, op: &Operation, columns: usize, fuse_relu: bool) -> String {
    // This is a single output per CUDA thread, without shared memory or
    // synchronization. The optional rewrite consumes two source buffers.
    let computation = match op {
        Operation::Add => String::from(
            "  %bp = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %b, i32 %idx\n\
               %y = load float, ptr addrspace(1) %bp, align 4\n\
               %value = call float asm sideeffect \"add.rn.f32 $0, $1, $2;\", \"=f,f,f\"(float %x, float %y)\n",
        ),
        Operation::Mul => String::from(
            "  %bp = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %b, i32 %idx\n\
               %y = load float, ptr addrspace(1) %bp, align 4\n\
               %value = call float asm sideeffect \"mul.rn.f32 $0, $1, $2;\", \"=f,f,f\"(float %x, float %y)\n",
        ),
        Operation::Pointwise(spec) => match supported_pointwise(spec) {
            Some(TranslationKind::Sub) => String::from(
                "  %bp = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %b, i32 %idx\n\
                   %y = load float, ptr addrspace(1) %bp, align 4\n\
                   %value = call float asm sideeffect \"sub.rn.f32 $0, $1, $2;\", \"=f,f,f\"(float %x, float %y)\n",
            ),
            Some(TranslationKind::DivRne) => String::from(
                "  %bp = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %b, i32 %idx\n\
                   %y = load float, ptr addrspace(1) %bp, align 4\n\
                   %value = call float asm sideeffect \"div.rn.f32 $0, $1, $2;\", \"=f,f,f\"(float %x, float %y)\n",
            ),
            Some(TranslationKind::SqrtRne) => String::from(
                "  %value = call float asm sideeffect \"sqrt.rn.f32 $0, $1;\", \"=f,f\"(float %x)\n",
            ),
            Some(TranslationKind::ExpApprox) => format!(
                "  %scaled = call float asm sideeffect \"mul.rn.f32 $0, $1, $2;\", \"=f,f,f\"(float %x, float {LOG2_E_F32_LLVM})\n\
                   %value = call float asm sideeffect \"ex2.approx.f32 $0, $1;\", \"=f,f\"(float %scaled)\n",
            ),
            _ => unreachable!("pointwise signatures were validated before codegen"),
        },
        Operation::BiasAdd => format!(
            "  %col = urem i32 %idx, {columns}\n\
               %bp = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %b, i32 %col\n\
               %y = load float, ptr addrspace(1) %bp, align 4\n\
               %value = call float asm sideeffect \"add.rn.f32 $0, $1, $2;\", \"=f,f,f\"(float %x, float %y)\n",
        ),
        Operation::Relu => String::from(
            "  %nan = fcmp uno float %x, %x\n\
               %positive = fcmp ogt float %x, 0.000000e+00\n\
               %keep = or i1 %nan, %positive\n\
               %value = select i1 %keep, float %x, float 0.000000e+00\n",
        ),
        _ => unreachable!("only supported pointwise operations require this kernel"),
    };
    let tail = if fuse_relu {
        "  %nan_fused = fcmp uno float %value, %value\n\
           %positive_fused = fcmp ogt float %value, 0.000000e+00\n\
           %keep_fused = or i1 %nan_fused, %positive_fused\n\
           %fused_result = select i1 %keep_fused, float %value, float 0.000000e+00\n"
    } else {
        ""
    };
    let result = if fuse_relu { "%fused_result" } else { "%value" };
    pointwise_kernel_ir(index, &format!("{computation}{tail}"), result)
}

/// Opt-in strict-order fusion of a pointwise Mul followed by Add.
/// Two explicit PTX RN instructions prevent LLVM from contracting the pair
/// into FMA. %a/%b are the Mul operands; %bias is the other Add operand.
/// The original Add operand order is preserved, including signed zero/NaN
/// cases where commutation must not be assumed.
/// 3-op, 3-source fusion: Mul(a,b) -> Add(product,c) -> Mul(sum,one-of-a/b/c).
/// Strictly preserve BOTH binary operand orders and two explicit mul.rn
/// instructions; no reassociation or implicit FMA.
/// Strictly rounded, architecture-neutral 3-op pointwise chain:
/// sqrt.rn(x) → add.rn(sqrt(x), epsilon) → div.rn(numerator, sum).
/// Never contract, reorder the Add operands, or skip intermediate rounding.
/// Four sequential, individually rounded FP32 operations. Operand reuse
/// is explicit and cannot be replaced with reassociation or FMA.
/// Four separate RN operations on a full-shape, four-source pointwise
/// diamond with explicit repeated input. No reassociation or FMA.
pub(super) fn mul_diamond_add_kernel_ir(
    index: usize,
    reused: usize,
    right_mul_on_right: bool,
    left_mul_on_right: bool,
) -> String {
    let factor = if reused == 0 { "%z" } else { "%w" };
    let repeat_args = if right_mul_on_right {
        format!("(float {factor}, float %right)")
    } else {
        format!("(float %right, float {factor})")
    };
    let add_args = if left_mul_on_right {
        "(float %repeated, float %left)"
    } else {
        "(float %left, float %repeated)"
    };
    format!(
        r#"define ptx_kernel void @vn_node_{index}(ptr addrspace(1) %a, ptr addrspace(1) %b, ptr addrspace(1) %c, ptr addrspace(1) %d, ptr addrspace(1) %out, i32 %length) {{
entry:
  %tid = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.tid.x()
  %block = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.ctaid.x()
  %width = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.ntid.x()
  %base = mul i32 %block, %width
  %idx = add i32 %base, %tid
  %valid = icmp ult i32 %idx, %length
  br i1 %valid, label %compute, label %done
compute:
  %ap = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %a, i32 %idx
  %bp = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %b, i32 %idx
  %cp = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %c, i32 %idx
  %dp = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %d, i32 %idx
  %x = load float, ptr addrspace(1) %ap, align 4
  %y = load float, ptr addrspace(1) %bp, align 4
  %z = load float, ptr addrspace(1) %cp, align 4
  %w = load float, ptr addrspace(1) %dp, align 4
  %left = call float asm sideeffect "mul.rn.f32 $0, $1, $2;", "=f,f,f"(float %x, float %y)
  %right = call float asm sideeffect "mul.rn.f32 $0, $1, $2;", "=f,f,f"(float %z, float %w)
  %repeated = call float asm sideeffect "mul.rn.f32 $0, $1, $2;", "=f,f,f"{repeat_args}
  %value = call float asm sideeffect "add.rn.f32 $0, $1, $2;", "=f,f,f"{add_args}
  %op = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %out, i32 %idx
  store float %value, ptr addrspace(1) %op, align 4
  br label %done
done:
  ret void
}}

"#
    )
}

pub(super) fn mul_mul_add_div_kernel_ir(
    index: usize,
    reused: usize,
    multiply_on_right: bool,
    add_on_right: bool,
) -> String {
    let factor = if reused == 0 { "%x" } else { "%y" };
    let product_args = if multiply_on_right {
        format!("(float {factor}, float %first)")
    } else {
        format!("(float %first, float {factor})")
    };
    let add_args = if add_on_right {
        "(float %z, float %second)"
    } else {
        "(float %second, float %z)"
    };
    format!(
        r#"define ptx_kernel void @vn_node_{index}(ptr addrspace(1) %a, ptr addrspace(1) %b, ptr addrspace(1) %c, ptr addrspace(1) %d, ptr addrspace(1) %out, i32 %length) {{
entry:
  %tid = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.tid.x()
  %block = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.ctaid.x()
  %width = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.ntid.x()
  %base = mul i32 %block, %width
  %idx = add i32 %base, %tid
  %valid = icmp ult i32 %idx, %length
  br i1 %valid, label %compute, label %done
compute:
  %ap = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %a, i32 %idx
  %bp = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %b, i32 %idx
  %cp = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %c, i32 %idx
  %dp = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %d, i32 %idx
  %x = load float, ptr addrspace(1) %ap, align 4
  %y = load float, ptr addrspace(1) %bp, align 4
  %z = load float, ptr addrspace(1) %cp, align 4
  %w = load float, ptr addrspace(1) %dp, align 4
  %first = call float asm sideeffect "mul.rn.f32 $0, $1, $2;", "=f,f,f"(float %x, float %y)
  %second = call float asm sideeffect "mul.rn.f32 $0, $1, $2;", "=f,f,f"{product_args}
  %third = call float asm sideeffect "add.rn.f32 $0, $1, $2;", "=f,f,f"{add_args}
  %value = call float asm sideeffect "div.rn.f32 $0, $1, $2;", "=f,f,f"(float %third, float %w)
  %op = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %out, i32 %idx
  store float %value, ptr addrspace(1) %op, align 4
  br label %done
done:
  ret void
}}

"#
    )
}

pub(super) fn sqrt_add_div_kernel_ir(index: usize, sqrt_on_right: bool) -> String {
    let add_operands = if sqrt_on_right {
        "(float %y, float %root)"
    } else {
        "(float %root, float %y)"
    };
    format!(
        r#"define ptx_kernel void @vn_node_{index}(ptr addrspace(1) %a, ptr addrspace(1) %b, ptr addrspace(1) %bias, ptr addrspace(1) %out, i32 %length) {{
entry:
  %tid = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.tid.x()
  %block = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.ctaid.x()
  %width = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.ntid.x()
  %base = mul i32 %block, %width
  %idx = add i32 %base, %tid
  %valid = icmp ult i32 %idx, %length
  br i1 %valid, label %compute, label %done
compute:
  %ap = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %a, i32 %idx
  %bp = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %b, i32 %idx
  %biasp = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %bias, i32 %idx
  %x = load float, ptr addrspace(1) %ap, align 4
  %y = load float, ptr addrspace(1) %bp, align 4
  %z = load float, ptr addrspace(1) %biasp, align 4
  %root = call float asm sideeffect "sqrt.rn.f32 $0, $1;", "=f,f"(float %x)
  %shifted = call float asm sideeffect "add.rn.f32 $0, $1, $2;", "=f,f,f"{add_operands}
  %value = call float asm sideeffect "div.rn.f32 $0, $1, $2;", "=f,f,f"(float %z, float %shifted)
  %op = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %out, i32 %idx
  store float %value, ptr addrspace(1) %op, align 4
  br label %done
done:
  ret void
}}

"#
    )
}

pub(super) fn mul_add_mul_kernel_ir(index: usize, add_right: bool, outer_right: bool, reuse: usize) -> String {
    let add_operands = if add_right {
        "(float %z, float %product)"
    } else {
        "(float %product, float %z)"
    };
    let factor = ["%x", "%y", "%z"][reuse];
    let outer_operands = if outer_right {
        format!("(float {factor}, float %middle)")
    } else {
        format!("(float %middle, float {factor})")
    };
    format!(
        r#"define ptx_kernel void @vn_node_{index}(ptr addrspace(1) %a, ptr addrspace(1) %b, ptr addrspace(1) %bias, ptr addrspace(1) %out, i32 %length) {{
entry:
  %tid = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.tid.x()
  %block = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.ctaid.x()
  %width = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.ntid.x()
  %base = mul i32 %block, %width
  %idx = add i32 %base, %tid
  %valid = icmp ult i32 %idx, %length
  br i1 %valid, label %compute, label %done
compute:
  %ap = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %a, i32 %idx
  %bp = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %b, i32 %idx
  %biasp = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %bias, i32 %idx
  %x = load float, ptr addrspace(1) %ap, align 4
  %y = load float, ptr addrspace(1) %bp, align 4
  %z = load float, ptr addrspace(1) %biasp, align 4
  %product = call float asm sideeffect "mul.rn.f32 $0, $1, $2;", "=f,f,f"(float %x, float %y)
  %middle = call float asm sideeffect "add.rn.f32 $0, $1, $2;", "=f,f,f"{add_operands}
  %value = call float asm sideeffect "mul.rn.f32 $0, $1, $2;", "=f,f,f"{outer_operands}
  %op = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %out, i32 %idx
  store float %value, ptr addrspace(1) %op, align 4
  br label %done
done:
  ret void
}}

"#
    )
}

/// Three-input pointwise chain with two explicit independent RN
/// instructions, preserving both operand orders and intermediate rounding.
/// One physical CUDA Graph kernel for two independent public F32 results.
/// The four source pointers preserve the exact source operand order for both
/// operations. No FMA, fast-math, reassociation or output aliasing is allowed.
pub(super) fn dual_pointwise_kernel_ir(index: usize, first_mul: bool, second_mul: bool) -> String {
    let first = if first_mul {
        "mul.rn.f32"
    } else {
        "add.rn.f32"
    };
    let second = if second_mul {
        "mul.rn.f32"
    } else {
        "add.rn.f32"
    };
    format!(
        r#"define ptx_kernel void @vn_node_{index}(ptr addrspace(1) %a, ptr addrspace(1) %b, ptr addrspace(1) %c, ptr addrspace(1) %d, ptr addrspace(1) %extra, ptr addrspace(1) %out, i32 %length) {{
entry:
  %tid = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.tid.x()
  %block = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.ctaid.x()
  %width = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.ntid.x()
  %base = mul i32 %block, %width
  %idx = add i32 %base, %tid
  %valid = icmp ult i32 %idx, %length
  br i1 %valid, label %compute, label %done
compute:
  %ap = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %a, i32 %idx
  %bp = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %b, i32 %idx
  %cp = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %c, i32 %idx
  %dp = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %d, i32 %idx
  %x = load float, ptr addrspace(1) %ap, align 4
  %y = load float, ptr addrspace(1) %bp, align 4
  %z = load float, ptr addrspace(1) %cp, align 4
  %w = load float, ptr addrspace(1) %dp, align 4
  %first = call float asm sideeffect "{first} $0, $1, $2;", "=f,f,f"(float %x, float %y)
  %second = call float asm sideeffect "{second} $0, $1, $2;", "=f,f,f"(float %z, float %w)
  %extra_ptr = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %extra, i32 %idx
  %op = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %out, i32 %idx
  store float %first, ptr addrspace(1) %extra_ptr, align 4
  store float %second, ptr addrspace(1) %op, align 4
  br label %done
done:
  ret void
}}

"#
    )
}

pub(super) fn binary_chain_kernel_ir(
    index: usize,
    first_add: bool,
    second_add: bool,
    producer_on_right: bool,
) -> String {
    let first = if first_add {
        "add.rn.f32"
    } else {
        "mul.rn.f32"
    };
    let second = if second_add {
        "add.rn.f32"
    } else {
        "mul.rn.f32"
    };
    let operands = if producer_on_right {
        "(float %z, float %middle)"
    } else {
        "(float %middle, float %z)"
    };
    format!(
        r#"define ptx_kernel void @vn_node_{index}(ptr addrspace(1) %a, ptr addrspace(1) %b, ptr addrspace(1) %bias, ptr addrspace(1) %out, i32 %length) {{
entry:
  %tid = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.tid.x()
  %block = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.ctaid.x()
  %width = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.ntid.x()
  %base = mul i32 %block, %width
  %idx = add i32 %base, %tid
  %valid = icmp ult i32 %idx, %length
  br i1 %valid, label %compute, label %done
compute:
  %ap = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %a, i32 %idx
  %bp = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %b, i32 %idx
  %biasp = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %bias, i32 %idx
  %x = load float, ptr addrspace(1) %ap, align 4
  %y = load float, ptr addrspace(1) %bp, align 4
  %z = load float, ptr addrspace(1) %biasp, align 4
  %middle = call float asm sideeffect "{first} $0, $1, $2;", "=f,f,f"(float %x, float %y)
  %value = call float asm sideeffect "{second} $0, $1, $2;", "=f,f,f"{operands}
  %op = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %out, i32 %idx
  store float %value, ptr addrspace(1) %op, align 4
  br label %done
done:
  ret void
}}

"#
    )
}

pub(super) fn mul_add_kernel_ir(index: usize, multiply_on_right: bool) -> String {
    let operands = if multiply_on_right {
        "(float %z, float %product)"
    } else {
        "(float %product, float %z)"
    };
    format!(
        r#"define ptx_kernel void @vn_node_{index}(ptr addrspace(1) %a, ptr addrspace(1) %b, ptr addrspace(1) %bias, ptr addrspace(1) %out, i32 %length) {{
entry:
  %tid = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.tid.x()
  %block = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.ctaid.x()
  %width = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.ntid.x()
  %base = mul i32 %block, %width
  %idx = add i32 %base, %tid
  %valid = icmp ult i32 %idx, %length
  br i1 %valid, label %compute, label %done
compute:
  %ap = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %a, i32 %idx
  %bp = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %b, i32 %idx
  %biasp = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %bias, i32 %idx
  %x = load float, ptr addrspace(1) %ap, align 4
  %y = load float, ptr addrspace(1) %bp, align 4
  %z = load float, ptr addrspace(1) %biasp, align 4
  %product = call float asm sideeffect "mul.rn.f32 $0, $1, $2;", "=f,f,f"(float %x, float %y)
  %value = call float asm sideeffect "add.rn.f32 $0, $1, $2;", "=f,f,f"{operands}
  %op = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %out, i32 %idx
  store float %value, ptr addrspace(1) %op, align 4
  br label %done
done:
  ret void
}}

"#
    )
}

pub(super) fn pointwise_chain_kernel_ir(index: usize, inner_op: &Operation, columns: usize) -> String {
    let inner = match inner_op {
        Operation::Add => "add.rn.f32",
        Operation::Mul => "mul.rn.f32",
        _ => unreachable!("only Add/Mul start the supported pointwise chain"),
    };
    format!(
        r#"define ptx_kernel void @vn_node_{index}(ptr addrspace(1) %a, ptr addrspace(1) %b, ptr addrspace(1) %bias, ptr addrspace(1) %out, i32 %length) {{
entry:
  %tid = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.tid.x()
  %block = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.ctaid.x()
  %width = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.ntid.x()
  %base = mul i32 %block, %width
  %idx = add i32 %base, %tid
  %valid = icmp ult i32 %idx, %length
  br i1 %valid, label %compute, label %done
compute:
  %ap = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %a, i32 %idx
  %bp = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %b, i32 %idx
  %x = load float, ptr addrspace(1) %ap, align 4
  %y = load float, ptr addrspace(1) %bp, align 4
  %inner = call float asm sideeffect "{inner} $0, $1, $2;", "=f,f,f"(float %x, float %y)
  %col = urem i32 %idx, {columns}
  %biasp = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %bias, i32 %col
  %bias_value = load float, ptr addrspace(1) %biasp, align 4
  %biased = call float asm sideeffect "add.rn.f32 $0, $1, $2;", "=f,f,f"(float %inner, float %bias_value)
  %nan = fcmp uno float %biased, %biased
  %positive = fcmp ogt float %biased, 0.000000e+00
  %keep = or i1 %nan, %positive
  %result = select i1 %keep, float %biased, float 0.000000e+00
  %op = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %out, i32 %idx
  store float %result, ptr addrspace(1) %op, align 4
  br label %done
done:
  ret void
}}

"#
    )
}

pub(super) fn pointwise_kernel_ir(index: usize, computation: &str, result: &str) -> String {
    format!(
        "define ptx_kernel void @vn_node_{index}(ptr addrspace(1) %a, ptr addrspace(1) %b, ptr addrspace(1) %out, i32 %length) {{\n\
         entry:\n\
           %tid = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.tid.x()\n\
           %block = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.ctaid.x()\n\
           %width = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.ntid.x()\n\
           %base = mul i32 %block, %width\n\
           %idx = add i32 %base, %tid\n\
           %valid = icmp ult i32 %idx, %length\n\
           br i1 %valid, label %compute, label %done\n\
         compute:\n\
           %ap = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %a, i32 %idx\n\
           %x = load float, ptr addrspace(1) %ap, align 4\n\
         {computation}\
           %op = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %out, i32 %idx\n\
           store float {result}, ptr addrspace(1) %op, align 4\n\
           br label %done\n\
         done:\n\
           ret void\n\
         }}\n\n"
    )
}

// Stage 6: simple one-output-per-thread row-major MatMul.
// Deliberately no fusion, tiling, TF32 or fast-math. LLVM/CUDA remain TCB.
pub(super) fn matmul_kernel_ir(index: usize, inner: usize, columns: usize) -> String {
    format!(
        "define ptx_kernel void @vn_node_{index}(ptr addrspace(1) %a, ptr addrspace(1) %b, ptr addrspace(1) %out, i32 %length) {{\n\
         entry:\n\
           %tid = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.tid.x()\n\
           %block = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.ctaid.x()\n\
           %width = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.ntid.x()\n\
           %base = mul i32 %block, %width\n\
           %idx = add i32 %base, %tid\n\
           %valid = icmp ult i32 %idx, %length\n\
           br i1 %valid, label %compute, label %done\n\
         compute:\n\
           %row = udiv i32 %idx, {columns}\n\
           %col = urem i32 %idx, {columns}\n\
           br label %loop\n\
         loop:\n\
           %j = phi i32 [ 0, %compute ], [ %next, %body ]\n\
           %sum = phi float [ 0.000000e+00, %compute ], [ %updated, %body ]\n\
           %more = icmp ult i32 %j, {inner}\n\
           br i1 %more, label %body, label %store\n\
         body:\n\
           %lhsBase = mul i32 %row, {inner}\n\
           %lhsIdx = add i32 %lhsBase, %j\n\
           %rhsBase = mul i32 %j, {columns}\n\
           %rhsIdx = add i32 %rhsBase, %col\n\
           %ap = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %a, i32 %lhsIdx\n\
           %bp = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %b, i32 %rhsIdx\n\
           %x = load float, ptr addrspace(1) %ap, align 4\n\
           %y = load float, ptr addrspace(1) %bp, align 4\n\
           %product = call float asm sideeffect \"mul.rn.f32 $0, $1, $2;\", \"=f,f,f\"(float %x, float %y)\n\
           %updated = call float asm sideeffect \"add.rn.f32 $0, $1, $2;\", \"=f,f,f\"(float %sum, float %product)\n\
           %next = add i32 %j, 1\n\
           br label %loop\n\
         store:\n\
           %op = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %out, i32 %idx\n\
           store float %sum, ptr addrspace(1) %op, align 4\n\
           br label %done\n\
         done:\n\
           ret void\n\
         }}\n\n"
    )
}

pub(super) fn transpose2d_kernel_ir(index: usize, rows: usize, columns: usize) -> String {
    format!(
        r#"define ptx_kernel void @vn_node_{index}(ptr addrspace(1) %a, ptr addrspace(1) %b, ptr addrspace(1) %out, i32 %length) {{
entry:
  %tid = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.tid.x()
  %block = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.ctaid.x()
  %width = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.ntid.x()
  %base = mul i32 %block, %width
  %idx = add i32 %base, %tid
  %valid = icmp ult i32 %idx, %length
  br i1 %valid, label %compute, label %done
compute:
  %in_row = urem i32 %idx, {rows}
  %in_col = udiv i32 %idx, {rows}
  %row_base = mul i32 %in_row, {columns}
  %source_idx = add i32 %row_base, %in_col
  %ap = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %a, i32 %source_idx
  %x = load float, ptr addrspace(1) %ap, align 4
  %op = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %out, i32 %idx
  store float %x, ptr addrspace(1) %op, align 4
  br label %done
done:
  ret void
}}

"#
    )
}

pub(super) fn reverse2d_kernel_ir(index: usize, rows: usize, columns: usize, axis: usize) -> String {
    let source = if axis == 0 {
        format!(
            "  %row = udiv i32 %idx, {columns}\n\
             %col = urem i32 %idx, {columns}\n\
             %rows_minus_one = add i32 0, {}\n\
             %reversed_row = sub i32 %rows_minus_one, %row\n\
             %row_base = mul i32 %reversed_row, {columns}\n\
             %source_idx = add i32 %row_base, %col\n",
            rows - 1
        )
    } else {
        format!(
            "  %row = udiv i32 %idx, {columns}\n\
             %col = urem i32 %idx, {columns}\n\
             %columns_minus_one = add i32 0, {}\n\
             %reversed_col = sub i32 %columns_minus_one, %col\n\
             %row_base = mul i32 %row, {columns}\n\
             %source_idx = add i32 %row_base, %reversed_col\n",
            columns - 1
        )
    };
    format!(
        "define ptx_kernel void @vn_node_{index}(ptr addrspace(1) %a, ptr addrspace(1) %b, ptr addrspace(1) %out, i32 %length) {{\n\
         entry:\n\
           %tid = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.tid.x()\n\
           %block = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.ctaid.x()\n\
           %width = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.ntid.x()\n\
           %base = mul i32 %block, %width\n\
           %idx = add i32 %base, %tid\n\
           %valid = icmp ult i32 %idx, %length\n\
           br i1 %valid, label %compute, label %done\n\
         compute:\n\
         {source}\
           %ap = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %a, i32 %source_idx\n\
           %x = load float, ptr addrspace(1) %ap, align 4\n\
           %op = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %out, i32 %idx\n\
           store float %x, ptr addrspace(1) %op, align 4\n\
           br label %done\n\
         done:\n\
           ret void\n\
         }}\n\n"
    )
}

// Contiguous structural kernels. No neural-architecture operation is hidden here.
pub(super) fn slice_last_row_kernel_ir(index: usize, start: usize) -> String {
    format!(
        r#"define ptx_kernel void @vn_node_{index}(ptr addrspace(1) %a, ptr addrspace(1) %b, ptr addrspace(1) %out, i32 %length) {{
entry:
  %tid = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.tid.x()
  %block = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.ctaid.x()
  %width = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.ntid.x()
  %base = mul i32 %block, %width
  %idx = add i32 %base, %tid
  %valid = icmp ult i32 %idx, %length
  br i1 %valid, label %compute, label %done
compute:
  %source_idx = add i32 %idx, {start}
  %ap = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %a, i32 %source_idx
  %x = load float, ptr addrspace(1) %ap, align 4
  %op = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %out, i32 %idx
  store float %x, ptr addrspace(1) %op, align 4
  br label %done
done:
  ret void
}}

"#
    )
}

pub(super) fn broadcast_scalar_kernel_ir(index: usize) -> String {
    format!(
        r#"define ptx_kernel void @vn_node_{index}(ptr addrspace(1) %a, ptr addrspace(1) %b, ptr addrspace(1) %out, i32 %length) {{
entry:
  %tid = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.tid.x()
  %block = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.ctaid.x()
  %width = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.ntid.x()
  %base = mul i32 %block, %width
  %idx = add i32 %base, %tid
  %valid = icmp ult i32 %idx, %length
  br i1 %valid, label %compute, label %done
compute:
  %ap = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %a, i32 0
  %x = load float, ptr addrspace(1) %ap, align 4
  %op = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %out, i32 %idx
  store float %x, ptr addrspace(1) %op, align 4
  br label %done
done:
  ret void
}}

"#
    )
}

pub(super) fn concat_axis0_kernel_ir(index: usize, left: usize) -> String {
    format!(
        r#"define ptx_kernel void @vn_node_{index}(ptr addrspace(1) %a, ptr addrspace(1) %b, ptr addrspace(1) %out, i32 %length) {{
entry:
  %tid = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.tid.x()
  %block = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.ctaid.x()
  %width = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.ntid.x()
  %base = mul i32 %block, %width
  %idx = add i32 %base, %tid
  %valid = icmp ult i32 %idx, %length
  br i1 %valid, label %compute, label %done
compute:
  %from_left = icmp ult i32 %idx, {left}
  br i1 %from_left, label %left, label %right
left:
  %ap = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %a, i32 %idx
  %left_value = load float, ptr addrspace(1) %ap, align 4
  br label %store
right:
  %right_idx = sub i32 %idx, {left}
  %bp = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %b, i32 %right_idx
  %right_value = load float, ptr addrspace(1) %bp, align 4
  br label %store
store:
  %value = phi float [ %left_value, %left ], [ %right_value, %right ]
  %op = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %out, i32 %idx
  store float %value, ptr addrspace(1) %op, align 4
  br label %done
done:
  ret void
}}

"#
    )
}

pub(super) fn argmax_last_kernel_ir(index: usize, width: usize) -> String {
    format!(
        r#"define ptx_kernel void @vn_node_{index}(ptr addrspace(1) %a, ptr addrspace(1) %b, ptr addrspace(1) %out, i32 %length) {{
entry:
  %tid = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.tid.x()
  %block = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.ctaid.x()
  %threads = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.ntid.x()
  %grid_base = mul i32 %block, %threads
  %idx = add i32 %grid_base, %tid
  %valid = icmp ult i32 %idx, %length
  br i1 %valid, label %compute, label %done
compute:
  %row_base = mul i32 %idx, {width}
  %first_ptr = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %a, i32 %row_base
  %first = load float, ptr addrspace(1) %first_ptr, align 4
  br label %loop
loop:
  %lane = phi i32 [ 1, %compute ], [ %next, %body ]
  %best_lane = phi i32 [ 0, %compute ], [ %chosen_lane, %body ]
  %best_value = phi float [ %first, %compute ], [ %chosen_value, %body ]
  %more = icmp ult i32 %lane, {width}
  br i1 %more, label %body, label %store
body:
  %candidate_idx = add i32 %row_base, %lane
  %candidate_ptr = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %a, i32 %candidate_idx
  %candidate = load float, ptr addrspace(1) %candidate_ptr, align 4
  %candidate_numeric = fcmp ord float %candidate, %candidate
  %best_nan = fcmp uno float %best_value, %best_value
  %greater = fcmp ogt float %candidate, %best_value
  %better_than_best = or i1 %best_nan, %greater
  %replace = and i1 %candidate_numeric, %better_than_best
  %chosen_lane = select i1 %replace, i32 %lane, i32 %best_lane
  %chosen_value = select i1 %replace, float %candidate, float %best_value
  %next = add i32 %lane, 1
  br label %loop
store:
  %op = getelementptr i32, ptr addrspace(1) %out, i32 %idx
  store i32 %best_lane, ptr addrspace(1) %op, align 4
  br label %done
done:
  ret void
}}

"#
    )
}

pub(super) fn take_axis0_kernel_ir(index: usize, lane: usize) -> String {
    format!(
        r#"define ptx_kernel void @vn_node_{index}(ptr addrspace(1) %a, ptr addrspace(1) %b, ptr addrspace(1) %out, i32 %length) {{
entry:
  %tid = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.tid.x()
  %block = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.ctaid.x()
  %width = call i32 @llvm.nvvm.read.ptx.sreg.ntid.x()
  %base = mul i32 %block, %width
  %idx = add i32 %base, %tid
  %valid = icmp ult i32 %idx, %length
  br i1 %valid, label %compute, label %done
compute:
  %bp = getelementptr i32, ptr addrspace(1) %b, i32 0
  %selected = load i32, ptr addrspace(1) %bp, align 4
  %selected_base = mul i32 %selected, {lane}
  %source_idx = add i32 %selected_base, %idx
  %ap = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %a, i32 %source_idx
  %x = load float, ptr addrspace(1) %ap, align 4
  %op = getelementptr float, ptr addrspace(1) %out, i32 %idx
  store float %x, ptr addrspace(1) %op, align 4
  br label %done
done:
  ret void
}}

"#
    )
}


FILE	crates/verineural/src/gpu/program.rs
//! Semantic IR GPU program lowering, capability and proof/memory contracts.

use super::*;

impl GpuProgram {
    pub fn llvm_ir(&self) -> &str {
        &self.llvm_ir
    }

    pub fn source_inputs(&self) -> &[NodeId] {
        &self.source_inputs
    }

    pub fn output(&self) -> NodeId {
        self.output
    }

    /// Ordered, distinct architecture outputs served by the same kernel DAG.
    pub fn outputs(&self) -> &[NodeId] {
        &self.outputs
    }

    /// Exactly one kernel per live Semantic IR producer, even when multiple
    /// selected outputs depend on it. Zero-copy Reshape retains its alias.
    pub fn kernel_count(&self) -> Result<usize, GpuError> {
        Ok(self.memory_contracts()?.len())
    }

    /// Number of distinct compiled NVPTX functions, not CUDA Graph launches.
    /// Identical code templates share an entrypoint but never share arguments
    /// or output storage. The physical graph still has `kernel_count()` nodes.
    pub fn unique_kernel_count(&self) -> usize {
        self.kernel_entries
            .values()
            .copied()
            .collect::<BTreeSet<_>>()
            .len()
    }

    /// Function owner for a launched Semantic IR producer (not an alias).
    pub fn kernel_entry(&self, node: usize) -> Option<usize> {
        self.kernel_entries.get(&node).copied()
    }

    /// Conservative pre-JIT size of graph tensor allocations, in bytes.
    /// Exactly matches the materialized Input/OwnedContiguous allocations
    /// used by GpuEngine::prepare(), including secondary fused outputs.
    /// Excludes PTX/JIT, CUDA Graph metadata, transfers and auxiliary buffers;
    /// it is a budget guard, NOT a VRAM peak measurement.
    pub fn tensor_allocation_bytes(&self) -> Result<usize, GpuError> {
        let skipped = self.skipped_nodes();
        let mut total = 0usize;
        for &index in &self.live_nodes {
            if skipped.contains(&index) && !self.fused_dual_outputs.values().any(|&n| n == index) {
                continue;
            }
            let node = &self.graph.nodes()[index];
            if matches!(node.operation, Operation::Input)
                || matches!(
                    self.graph.storage(node.id)?,
                    NodeStorage::OwnedContiguous { .. }
                )
            {
                let elements = node.shape.element_count();
                let bytes = elements
                    .checked_mul(std::mem::size_of::<f32>())
                    .ok_or(GpuError::UnsupportedSize { elements })?;
                total = total
                    .checked_add(bytes)
                    .ok_or(GpuError::UnsupportedSize { elements })?;
            }
        }
        Ok(total)
    }

    pub const fn launch_config(&self) -> GpuLaunchConfig {
        self.launch
    }

    /// (consumer Relu node, producer binary node) pairs for the selected IR rewrite.
    pub fn fused_relus(&self) -> &BTreeMap<usize, usize> {
        &self.fused_relus
    }

    pub fn fused_pointwise_chains(&self) -> &BTreeMap<usize, Vec<usize>> {
        &self.fused_pointwise_chains
    }

    pub fn fused_mul_adds(&self) -> &BTreeMap<usize, (usize, usize)> {
        &self.fused_mul_adds
    }

    pub fn fused_mul_add_muls(&self) -> &BTreeMap<usize, (usize, usize, usize, usize, usize)> {
        &self.fused_mul_add_muls
    }

    /// Other strict-order binary pointwise pairs fused into one CUDA kernel.
    pub fn fused_binary_pairs(&self) -> &BTreeMap<usize, (usize, usize)> {
        &self.fused_binary_pairs
    }

    /// Opt-in rounded Sqrt→Add→Div chains with exclusive intermediate uses.
    pub fn fused_sqrt_add_divs(&self) -> &BTreeMap<usize, (usize, usize, usize)> {
        &self.fused_sqrt_add_divs
    }

    pub fn fused_mul_mul_add_divs(
        &self,
    ) -> &BTreeMap<usize, (usize, usize, usize, usize, usize, usize)> {
        &self.fused_mul_mul_add_divs
    }

    /// Four-op pointwise DAG fusion which preserves the selected Add root.
    pub fn fused_mul_diamond_adds(
        &self,
    ) -> &BTreeMap<usize, (usize, usize, usize, usize, usize, usize)> {
        &self.fused_mul_diamond_adds
    }

    pub fn removed_kernel_count(&self) -> usize {
        self.skipped_nodes().len()
    }

    /// Bounded, multi-output, strict-RNE fusion of independent live pointwise
    /// roots, including non-public intermediates whose consumers occur later.
    /// Both buffers remain materialized; IR and observable values are unchanged.
    pub fn fused_dual_outputs(&self) -> &BTreeMap<usize, usize> {
        &self.fused_dual_outputs
    }

    pub(super) fn skipped_nodes(&self) -> BTreeSet<usize> {
        let mut skipped = self.fused_relus.values().copied().collect::<BTreeSet<_>>();
        for chain in self.fused_pointwise_chains.values() {
            skipped.extend(chain.iter().copied());
        }
        skipped.extend(self.fused_mul_adds.values().map(|&(mul, _)| mul));
        skipped.extend(
            self.fused_binary_pairs
                .values()
                .map(|&(producer, _)| producer),
        );
        for &(mul, add, _, _, _) in self.fused_mul_add_muls.values() {
            skipped.insert(mul);
            skipped.insert(add);
        }
        for &(sqrt, add, _) in self.fused_sqrt_add_divs.values() {
            skipped.insert(sqrt);
            skipped.insert(add);
        }
        for &(inner, middle, add, _, _, _) in self.fused_mul_mul_add_divs.values() {
            skipped.extend([inner, middle, add]);
        }
        for &(left, first, second, _, _, _) in self.fused_mul_diamond_adds.values() {
            skipped.extend([left, first, second]);
        }
        skipped.extend(self.fused_dual_outputs.values().copied());
        skipped
    }

    /// Independently describe and check every launched kernel's element
    /// addresses. The same input selection drives CUDA graph capture.
    pub fn memory_contracts(&self) -> Result<Vec<GpuMemoryContract>, GpuError> {
        let mut result = Vec::new();
        let skipped = self.skipped_nodes();
        for &index in &self.live_nodes {
            if skipped.contains(&index) {
                continue;
            }
            let node = &self.graph.nodes()[index];
            if matches!(node.operation, Operation::Input) || self.graph.storage(node.id)?.is_alias()
            {
                continue;
            }
            let writes = node.shape.element_count();
            let (read_nodes, pattern): (Vec<usize>, GpuMemoryPattern) = if let Some(&earlier) =
                self.fused_dual_outputs.get(&index)
            {
                let first = &self.graph.nodes()[earlier];
                (
                    first
                        .inputs
                        .iter()
                        .chain(&node.inputs)
                        .map(|id| id.index())
                        .collect(),
                    GpuMemoryPattern::Pointwise,
                )
            } else if let Some(&(left, first, _, _, _, _)) = self.fused_mul_diamond_adds.get(&index)
            {
                let lhs = &self.graph.nodes()[left];
                let rhs = &self.graph.nodes()[first];
                (
                    vec![
                        lhs.inputs[0].index(),
                        lhs.inputs[1].index(),
                        rhs.inputs[0].index(),
                        rhs.inputs[1].index(),
                    ],
                    GpuMemoryPattern::Pointwise,
                )
            } else if let Some(&(inner, _, add, _, _, add_slot)) =
                self.fused_mul_mul_add_divs.get(&index)
            {
                let first = &self.graph.nodes()[inner];
                let sum = &self.graph.nodes()[add];
                (
                    vec![
                        first.inputs[0].index(),
                        first.inputs[1].index(),
                        sum.inputs[1 - add_slot].index(),
                        node.inputs[1].index(),
                    ],
                    GpuMemoryPattern::Pointwise,
                )
            } else if let Some(&(sqrt, add, slot)) = self.fused_sqrt_add_divs.get(&index) {
                let inner = &self.graph.nodes()[sqrt];
                let middle = &self.graph.nodes()[add];
                (
                    vec![
                        inner.inputs[0].index(),
                        middle.inputs[1 - slot].index(),
                        node.inputs[0].index(),
                    ],
                    GpuMemoryPattern::Pointwise,
                )
            } else if let Some(&(mul, add, slot, _, _)) = self.fused_mul_add_muls.get(&index) {
                let inner = &self.graph.nodes()[mul];
                let middle = &self.graph.nodes()[add];
                (
                    vec![
                        inner.inputs[0].index(),
                        inner.inputs[1].index(),
                        middle.inputs[1 - slot].index(),
                    ],
                    GpuMemoryPattern::Pointwise,
                )
            } else if let Some(&(mul, slot)) = self.fused_mul_adds.get(&index) {
                let producer = &self.graph.nodes()[mul];
                (
                    vec![
                        producer.inputs[0].index(),
                        producer.inputs[1].index(),
                        node.inputs[1 - slot].index(),
                    ],
                    GpuMemoryPattern::Pointwise,
                )
            } else if let Some(&(producer, slot)) = self.fused_binary_pairs.get(&index) {
                let inner = &self.graph.nodes()[producer];
                (
                    vec![
                        inner.inputs[0].index(),
                        inner.inputs[1].index(),
                        node.inputs[1 - slot].index(),
                    ],
                    GpuMemoryPattern::Pointwise,
                )
            } else if let Some(chain) = self.fused_pointwise_chains.get(&index) {
                let inner = &self.graph.nodes()[chain[0]];
                let bias = &self.graph.nodes()[chain[1]];
                (
                    vec![
                        inner.inputs[0].index(),
                        inner.inputs[1].index(),
                        bias.inputs[1].index(),
                    ],
                    GpuMemoryPattern::BiasAdd {
                        columns: node.shape.dims()[1],
                    },
                )
            } else {
                let producer = self.fused_relus.get(&index).copied().unwrap_or(index);
                let op_node = &self.graph.nodes()[producer];
                let pattern = match &op_node.operation {
                    Operation::BiasAdd => GpuMemoryPattern::BiasAdd {
                        columns: node.shape.dims()[1],
                    },
                    Operation::MatMul => {
                        let left = &self.graph.nodes()[op_node.inputs[0].index()];
                        GpuMemoryPattern::MatMul {
                            rows: left.shape.dims()[0],
                            inner: left.shape.dims()[1],
                            columns: node.shape.dims()[1],
                        }
                    }
                    Operation::Permute { axes } => {
                        let input = &self.graph.nodes()[op_node.inputs[0].index()];
                        if input.shape.rank() != 2 || axes.as_slice() != [1, 0] {
                            return Err(GpuError::UnsupportedOperation {
                                node: index,
                                operation: op_node.operation.name(),
                            });
                        }
                        GpuMemoryPattern::Transpose2D {
                            rows: input.shape.dims()[0],
                            columns: input.shape.dims()[1],
                        }
                    }
                    Operation::ReverseAxis { axis } => {
                        let input = &self.graph.nodes()[op_node.inputs[0].index()];
                        if input.shape.rank() != 2 {
                            return Err(GpuError::UnsupportedOperation {
                                node: index,
                                operation: op_node.operation.name(),
                            });
                        }
                        match axis {
                            0 => GpuMemoryPattern::ReverseRows2D {
                                rows: input.shape.dims()[0],
                                columns: input.shape.dims()[1],
                            },
                            1 => GpuMemoryPattern::ReverseColumns2D {
                                rows: input.shape.dims()[0],
                                columns: input.shape.dims()[1],
                            },
                            _ => {
                                return Err(GpuError::UnsupportedOperation {
                                    node: index,
                                    operation: op_node.operation.name(),
                                });
                            }
                        }
                    }
                    Operation::Concat { axis } => {
                        let left = &self.graph.nodes()[op_node.inputs[0].index()];
                        let right = &self.graph.nodes()[op_node.inputs[1].index()];
                        if *axis != 0
                            && !(*axis == 1
                                && left.shape.rank() == 2
                                && left.shape.dims()[0] == 1
                                && right.shape.dims()[0] == 1)
                        {
                            return Err(GpuError::UnsupportedOperation {
                                node: index,
                                operation: op_node.operation.name(),
                            });
                        }
                        GpuMemoryPattern::ConcatAxis0 {
                            left: left.shape.element_count(),
                        }
                    }
                    Operation::SliceAxis {
                        axis: 1,
                        start,
                        len,
                    } => {
                        let input = &self.graph.nodes()[op_node.inputs[0].index()];
                        if input.shape.rank() != 2
                            || input.shape.dims()[0] != 1
                            || *len != writes
                            || start
                                .checked_add(*len)
                                .is_none_or(|end| end > input.shape.dims()[1])
                        {
                            return Err(GpuError::UnsupportedOperation {
                                node: index,
                                operation: op_node.operation.name(),
                            });
                        }
                        GpuMemoryPattern::SliceLastRow {
                            start: *start,
                            source_width: input.shape.dims()[1],
                        }
                    }
                    Operation::BroadcastTo(_) => {
                        let input = &self.graph.nodes()[op_node.inputs[0].index()];
                        // Broadcasting a one-element tensor uses source
                        // address zero for every output lane, independently
                        // of output rank. General axis-wise broadcasting
                        // still has no GPU lowering and must fail closed.
                        if input.shape.element_count() != 1 {
                            return Err(GpuError::UnsupportedOperation {
                                node: index,
                                operation: op_node.operation.name(),
                            });
                        }
                        GpuMemoryPattern::BroadcastScalar
                    }
                    Operation::ArgMax { axis, tie_break } => {
                        let input = &self.graph.nodes()[op_node.inputs[0].index()];
                        if input.shape.rank() != 2
                            || *axis != 1
                            || !matches!(tie_break, crate::ArgMaxTieBreak::First)
                        {
                            return Err(GpuError::UnsupportedOperation {
                                node: index,
                                operation: op_node.operation.name(),
                            });
                        }
                        GpuMemoryPattern::ArgMaxLast {
                            width: input.shape.dims()[1],
                        }
                    }
                    Operation::Take { axis: 0 } => {
                        let data = &self.graph.nodes()[op_node.inputs[0].index()];
                        GpuMemoryPattern::TakeAxis0 {
                            lane: writes,
                            choices: data.shape.dims()[0],
                        }
                    }
                    _ => GpuMemoryPattern::Pointwise,
                };
                (
                    op_node.inputs.iter().map(|id| id.index()).collect(),
                    pattern,
                )
            };
            let required = match pattern {
                GpuMemoryPattern::Pointwise => vec![writes; read_nodes.len()],
                GpuMemoryPattern::BiasAdd { columns } => {
                    if read_nodes.len() == 3 {
                        vec![writes, writes, columns]
                    } else {
                        vec![writes, columns]
                    }
                }
                GpuMemoryPattern::MatMul {
                    rows,
                    inner,
                    columns,
                } => {
                    if rows.checked_mul(columns) != Some(writes) {
                        return Err(GpuError::InvalidInput {
                            node: index,
                            reason: "MatMul output extent does not match row-major indexing",
                        });
                    }
                    vec![
                        rows.checked_mul(inner)
                            .ok_or(GpuError::UnsupportedSize { elements: writes })?,
                        inner
                            .checked_mul(columns)
                            .ok_or(GpuError::UnsupportedSize { elements: writes })?,
                    ]
                }
                GpuMemoryPattern::Transpose2D { rows, columns } => {
                    if rows.checked_mul(columns) != Some(writes) {
                        return Err(GpuError::InvalidInput {
                            node: index,
                            reason: "transpose2d output extent mismatch",
                        });
                    }
                    vec![writes]
                }
                GpuMemoryPattern::ReverseRows2D { rows, columns }
                | GpuMemoryPattern::ReverseColumns2D { rows, columns } => {
                    if rows == 0 || columns == 0 || rows.checked_mul(columns) != Some(writes) {
                        return Err(GpuError::InvalidInput {
                            node: index,
                            reason: "reverse2d output extent mismatch",
                        });
                    }
                    vec![writes]
                }
                GpuMemoryPattern::SliceLastRow {
                    start,
                    source_width,
                } => {
                    if read_nodes.len() != 1
                        || start
                            .checked_add(writes)
                            .is_none_or(|end| end > source_width)
                    {
                        return Err(GpuError::InvalidInput {
                            node: index,
                            reason: "slice source extent mismatch",
                        });
                    }
                    vec![source_width]
                }
                GpuMemoryPattern::BroadcastScalar => vec![1],
                GpuMemoryPattern::ConcatAxis0 { left } => {
                    if read_nodes.len() != 2 {
                        return Err(GpuError::InvalidInput {
                            node: index,
                            reason: "concat_axis0 requires two source tensors",
                        });
                    }
                    let right = writes.checked_sub(left).ok_or(GpuError::InvalidInput {
                        node: index,
                        reason: "concat_axis0 left extent exceeds output",
                    })?;
                    vec![left, right]
                }
                GpuMemoryPattern::ArgMaxLast { width } => vec![
                    writes
                        .checked_mul(width)
                        .ok_or(GpuError::UnsupportedSize { elements: writes })?,
                ],
                GpuMemoryPattern::TakeAxis0 { lane, choices } => {
                    let data = &self.graph.nodes()[read_nodes[0]];
                    if lane != writes
                        || choices == 0
                        || choices.checked_mul(lane) != Some(data.shape.element_count())
                    {
                        return Err(GpuError::InvalidInput {
                            node: index,
                            reason: "take_axis0 source extent mismatch",
                        });
                    }
                    vec![data.shape.element_count(), 1]
                }
            };
            // CUDA templates form idx = block * width + lane with u32
            // wrap semantics, then test idx < length as unsigned. Bound the
            // *whole* grid so even unused trailing lanes cannot wrap.
            let width = self.launch.threads_per_block as usize;
            let launch_extent = writes.div_ceil(width).checked_mul(width);
            if !matches!(read_nodes.len(), 1..=4)
                || read_nodes.len() != required.len()
                || writes == 0
                || writes > i32::MAX as usize
                || launch_extent.is_none_or(|n| n > u32::MAX as usize)
                || read_nodes.iter().any(|&source| source >= index)
            {
                return Err(GpuError::InvalidInput {
                    node: index,
                    reason: "unsupported CUDA kernel memory access or launch bounds",
                });
            }
            if let GpuMemoryPattern::BiasAdd { columns } = pattern {
                if columns == 0 || writes % columns != 0 {
                    return Err(GpuError::InvalidInput {
                        node: index,
                        reason: "BiasAdd requires nonempty aligned rows",
                    });
                }
            }
            let mut reads = Vec::with_capacity(read_nodes.len());
            for (source, needed) in read_nodes.into_iter().zip(required) {
                if self.graph.nodes()[source].shape.element_count() != needed
                    || needed > i32::MAX as usize
                {
                    return Err(GpuError::InvalidInput {
                        node: index,
                        reason: "kernel input extent differs from its indexed access",
                    });
                }
                reads.push((source, needed));
            }
            result.push(GpuMemoryContract {
                kernel_node: index,
                reads,
                writes,
                additional_writes: self
                    .fused_dual_outputs
                    .get(&index)
                    .map_or_else(Vec::new, |&earlier| vec![(earlier, writes)]),
                pattern,
            });
        }
        Ok(result)
    }

    /// Derive the expected kernel composition from the original reachable
    /// graph, checked fusion decisions and exact memory contracts, not PTX.
    /// Each plan row is later cross-checked against LLVM and PTX per kernel.
    pub fn translation_plan(&self) -> Result<TranslationPlan, GpuError> {
        let mut kernels = Vec::new();
        for contract in self.memory_contracts()? {
            let node = &self.graph.nodes()[contract.kernel_node];
            let kind = if let Some(&earlier) = self.fused_dual_outputs.get(&contract.kernel_node) {
                TranslationKind::DualPointwise {
                    earlier,
                    first_mul: matches!(self.graph.nodes()[earlier].operation, Operation::Mul),
                    second_mul: matches!(node.operation, Operation::Mul),
                }
            } else if let Some(&(_, _, _, reused, right_slot, left_slot)) =
                self.fused_mul_diamond_adds.get(&contract.kernel_node)
            {
                TranslationKind::MulDiamondAdd {
                    reused_source: reused as u8,
                    right_mul_on_right: right_slot == 1,
                    left_mul_on_right: left_slot == 1,
                }
            } else if let Some(&(_, _, _, reused, middle_slot, add_slot)) =
                self.fused_mul_mul_add_divs.get(&contract.kernel_node)
            {
                TranslationKind::MulMulAddDiv {
                    reused_source: reused as u8,
                    multiply_on_right: middle_slot == 1,
                    add_on_right: add_slot == 1,
                }
            } else if let Some(&(_, _, slot)) = self.fused_sqrt_add_divs.get(&contract.kernel_node)
            {
                TranslationKind::SqrtAddDiv {
                    sqrt_on_right: slot == 1,
                }
            } else if let Some(&(_, _, add_slot, outer_slot, reuse)) =
                self.fused_mul_add_muls.get(&contract.kernel_node)
            {
                TranslationKind::MulAddMul {
                    add_mul_on_right: add_slot == 1,
                    mul_add_on_right: outer_slot == 1,
                    reused_source: reuse as u8,
                }
            } else if let Some(&(_, slot)) = self.fused_mul_adds.get(&contract.kernel_node) {
                TranslationKind::MulAdd {
                    multiply_on_right: slot == 1,
                }
            } else if let Some(&(producer, slot)) =
                self.fused_binary_pairs.get(&contract.kernel_node)
            {
                TranslationKind::BinaryChain {
                    first_add: matches!(self.graph.nodes()[producer].operation, Operation::Add),
                    second_add: matches!(node.operation, Operation::Add),
                    producer_on_right: slot == 1,
                }
            } else if let Some(chain) = self.fused_pointwise_chains.get(&contract.kernel_node) {
                let inner = &self.graph.nodes()[chain[0]].operation;
                let columns = match contract.pattern {
                    GpuMemoryPattern::BiasAdd { columns } => columns,
                    _ => {
                        return Err(GpuError::Fp32PtxRejected {
                            reason: "fused chain lacks BiasAdd memory contract".into(),
                        });
                    }
                };
                match inner {
                    Operation::Add => TranslationKind::AddBiasRelu { columns },
                    Operation::Mul => TranslationKind::MulBiasRelu { columns },
                    _ => {
                        return Err(GpuError::Fp32PtxRejected {
                            reason: "unsupported fused inner operation".into(),
                        });
                    }
                }
            } else if let Some(&producer) = self.fused_relus.get(&contract.kernel_node) {
                match self.graph.nodes()[producer].operation {
                    Operation::Add => TranslationKind::AddRelu,
                    Operation::Mul => TranslationKind::MulRelu,
                    Operation::BiasAdd => {
                        let columns = match contract.pattern {
                            GpuMemoryPattern::BiasAdd { columns } => columns,
                            _ => {
                                return Err(GpuError::Fp32PtxRejected {
                                    reason: "fused bias lacks broadcast memory contract".into(),
                                });
                            }
                        };
                        TranslationKind::BiasAddRelu { columns }
                    }
                    _ => {
                        return Err(GpuError::Fp32PtxRejected {
                            reason: "unsupported fused producer operation".into(),
                        });
                    }
                }
            } else {
                match node.operation {
                    Operation::Add => TranslationKind::Add,
                    Operation::Mul => TranslationKind::Mul,
                    Operation::Pointwise(ref spec) => {
                        supported_pointwise(spec).ok_or(GpuError::UnsupportedOperation {
                            node: contract.kernel_node,
                            operation: node.operation.name(),
                        })?
                    }
                    Operation::BiasAdd => {
                        let columns = match contract.pattern {
                            GpuMemoryPattern::BiasAdd { columns } => columns,
                            _ => {
                                return Err(GpuError::Fp32PtxRejected {
                                    reason: "bias lacks broadcast memory contract".into(),
                                });
                            }
                        };
                        TranslationKind::BiasAdd { columns }
                    }
                    Operation::MatMul => {
                        let (inner, columns) = match contract.pattern {
                            GpuMemoryPattern::MatMul { inner, columns, .. } => (inner, columns),
                            _ => {
                                return Err(GpuError::Fp32PtxRejected {
                                    reason: "MatMul lacks reduction memory contract".into(),
                                });
                            }
                        };
                        TranslationKind::MatMul { inner, columns }
                    }
                    Operation::Permute { .. } => match contract.pattern {
                        GpuMemoryPattern::Transpose2D { rows, columns } => {
                            TranslationKind::Transpose2D { rows, columns }
                        }
                        _ => {
                            return Err(GpuError::Fp32PtxRejected {
                                reason: "Permute lacks transpose2d memory contract".into(),
                            });
                        }
                    },
                    Operation::ReverseAxis { axis: 0 } => match contract.pattern {
                        GpuMemoryPattern::ReverseRows2D { rows, columns } => {
                            TranslationKind::ReverseRows2D { rows, columns }
                        }
                        _ => {
                            return Err(GpuError::Fp32PtxRejected {
                                reason: "ReverseAxis(0) lacks memory contract".into(),
                            });
                        }
                    },
                    Operation::ReverseAxis { axis: 1 } => match contract.pattern {
                        GpuMemoryPattern::ReverseColumns2D { rows, columns } => {
                            TranslationKind::ReverseColumns2D { rows, columns }
                        }
                        _ => {
                            return Err(GpuError::Fp32PtxRejected {
                                reason: "ReverseAxis(1) lacks memory contract".into(),
                            });
                        }
                    },
                    Operation::BroadcastTo(_) => match contract.pattern {
                        GpuMemoryPattern::BroadcastScalar => TranslationKind::BroadcastScalar,
                        _ => {
                            return Err(GpuError::Fp32PtxRejected {
                                reason: "BroadcastTo lacks scalar memory contract".into(),
                            });
                        }
                    },
                    Operation::SliceAxis { axis: 1, .. } => match contract.pattern {
                        GpuMemoryPattern::SliceLastRow {
                            start,
                            source_width,
                        } => TranslationKind::SliceLastRow {
                            start,
                            source_width,
                        },
                        _ => {
                            return Err(GpuError::Fp32PtxRejected {
                                reason: "SliceAxis(1) lacks memory contract".into(),
                            });
                        }
                    },
                    Operation::Concat { .. } => match contract.pattern {
                        GpuMemoryPattern::ConcatAxis0 { left } => {
                            TranslationKind::ConcatAxis0 { left }
                        }
                        _ => {
                            return Err(GpuError::Fp32PtxRejected {
                                reason: "Concat(0) lacks memory contract".into(),
                            });
                        }
                    },
                    Operation::ArgMax { axis: 1, .. } => match contract.pattern {
                        GpuMemoryPattern::ArgMaxLast { width } => {
                            TranslationKind::ArgMaxLast { width }
                        }
                        _ => {
                            return Err(GpuError::Fp32PtxRejected {
                                reason: "ArgMax(last) lacks memory contract".into(),
                            });
                        }
                    },
                    Operation::Take { axis: 0 } => match contract.pattern {
                        GpuMemoryPattern::TakeAxis0 { lane, .. } => {
                            TranslationKind::TakeAxis0 { lane }
                        }
                        _ => {
                            return Err(GpuError::Fp32PtxRejected {
                                reason: "Take(0) lacks memory contract".into(),
                            });
                        }
                    },
                    Operation::Relu => TranslationKind::Relu,
                    _ => {
                        return Err(GpuError::Fp32PtxRejected {
                            reason: "unexpected operation in kernel translation plan".into(),
                        });
                    }
                }
            };
            kernels.push(TranslationKernel {
                node: contract.kernel_node,
                entry_node: self.kernel_entries[&contract.kernel_node],
                kind,
                reads: contract.reads,
                writes: contract.writes,
            });
        }
        Ok(TranslationPlan {
            threads_per_block: self.launch.threads_per_block(),
            kernels,
        })
    }

    /// Cross-check the concrete lowering profile before it can be called
    /// supported by higher layers. This validates evidence coverage and fusion
    /// preconditions only; it does not execute Lean, LLVM, CUDA or the GPU.
    pub fn capability_plan(&self) -> Result<GpuCapabilityPlan, GpuError> {
        let contracts = self.memory_contracts()?;
        let translation = self.translation_plan()?;
        if contracts.len() != translation.kernels.len() {
            return Err(GpuError::Fp32PtxRejected {
                reason: "capability plan kernel/memory coverage mismatch".into(),
            });
        }

        let mut kernels = Vec::with_capacity(contracts.len());
        for (contract, rule) in contracts.iter().zip(&translation.kernels) {
            if contract.kernel_node != rule.node
                || contract.reads != rule.reads
                || contract.writes != rule.writes
                || contract.additional_writes != rule.kind.extra_writes(contract.writes)
            {
                return Err(GpuError::Fp32PtxRejected {
                    reason: format!(
                        "capability evidence mismatch for kernel node {}",
                        contract.kernel_node
                    ),
                });
            }
            kernels.push(GpuKernelCapability {
                node: contract.kernel_node,
                operation: self.graph.nodes()[contract.kernel_node].operation.name(),
                memory_pattern: contract.pattern,
                translation_kind: rule.kind,
                reads: contract.reads.clone(),
                writes: contract.writes,
                additional_writes: contract.additional_writes.clone(),
            });
        }

        let skipped = self.skipped_nodes();
        let launched = kernels
            .iter()
            .map(|kernel| kernel.node)
            .collect::<BTreeSet<_>>();
        let mut expected = BTreeSet::new();
        for &index in &self.live_nodes {
            let node = &self.graph.nodes()[index];
            if !skipped.contains(&index)
                && !matches!(node.operation, Operation::Input)
                && !self.graph.storage(node.id)?.is_alias()
            {
                expected.insert(index);
            }
        }
        if launched != expected {
            return Err(GpuError::Fp32PtxRejected {
                reason: "capability plan does not cover every launched semantic node".into(),
            });
        }

        let mut uses = vec![0usize; self.graph.nodes().len()];
        for &index in &self.live_nodes {
            for input in &self.graph.nodes()[index].inputs {
                uses[input.index()] += 1;
            }
        }
        for output in &self.outputs {
            uses[output.index()] += 1;
        }
        let selected = self
            .outputs
            .iter()
            .map(|id| id.index())
            .collect::<BTreeSet<_>>();
        let mut optimizations = Vec::new();
        let mut covered_removed = BTreeSet::new();

        for (&root, chain) in &self.fused_pointwise_chains {
            if chain.len() != 2 {
                return Err(GpuError::Fp32PtxRejected {
                    reason: "fused pointwise chain has invalid length".into(),
                });
            }
            let inner = chain[0];
            let bias = chain[1];
            let root_node = &self.graph.nodes()[root];
            let inner_node = &self.graph.nodes()[inner];
            let bias_node = &self.graph.nodes()[bias];
            let exclusive = uses[inner] == 1 && uses[bias] == 1;
            let preserves = !selected.contains(&inner) && !selected.contains(&bias);
            let compatible = matches!(root_node.operation, Operation::Relu)
                && root_node.inputs.len() == 1
                && root_node.inputs[0].index() == bias
                && matches!(bias_node.operation, Operation::BiasAdd)
                && bias_node.inputs[0].index() == inner
                && matches!(inner_node.operation, Operation::Add | Operation::Mul)
                && self.fused_relus.get(&root).copied() == Some(bias);
            if !exclusive || !preserves || !compatible {
                return Err(GpuError::Fp32PtxRejected {
                    reason: format!("invalid pointwise fusion capability at node {root}"),
                });
            }
            covered_removed.insert(inner);
            covered_removed.insert(bias);
            optimizations.push(GpuOptimizationCapability {
                root,
                kind: GpuOptimizationKind::PointwiseBiasReluFusion,
                removed_nodes: chain.clone(),
                exclusive_reachable_use: true,
                selected_outputs_preserved: true,
            });
        }

        for (&root, &producer) in &self.fused_relus {
            if self.fused_pointwise_chains.contains_key(&root) {
                continue;
            }
            let root_node = &self.graph.nodes()[root];
            let producer_node = &self.graph.nodes()[producer];
            let exclusive = uses[producer] == 1;
            let preserves = !selected.contains(&producer);
            let compatible = matches!(root_node.operation, Operation::Relu)
                && root_node.inputs.len() == 1
                && root_node.inputs[0].index() == producer
                && matches!(
                    producer_node.operation,
                    Operation::Add | Operation::Mul | Operation::BiasAdd
                );
            if !exclusive || !preserves || !compatible {
                return Err(GpuError::Fp32PtxRejected {
                    reason: format!("invalid relu fusion capability at node {root}"),
                });
            }
            covered_removed.insert(producer);
            optimizations.push(GpuOptimizationCapability {
                root,
                kind: GpuOptimizationKind::ReluProducerFusion,
                removed_nodes: vec![producer],
                exclusive_reachable_use: true,
                selected_outputs_preserved: true,
            });
        }

        for (&root, &(mul, add, add_slot, outer_slot, reuse)) in &self.fused_mul_add_muls {
            let root_node = &self.graph.nodes()[root];
            let middle = &self.graph.nodes()[add];
            let inner = &self.graph.nodes()[mul];
            let valid_slots = add_slot < 2 && outer_slot < 2 && reuse < 3;
            let external = if valid_slots {
                [
                    inner.inputs[0],
                    inner.inputs[1],
                    middle.inputs[1 - add_slot],
                ]
            } else {
                return Err(GpuError::Fp32PtxRejected {
                    reason: format!("invalid mul-add-mul slots at node {root}"),
                });
            };
            let compatible = matches!(root_node.operation, Operation::Mul)
                && matches!(middle.operation, Operation::Add)
                && matches!(inner.operation, Operation::Mul)
                && root_node.inputs[outer_slot].index() == add
                && middle.inputs[add_slot].index() == mul
                && root_node.inputs[1 - outer_slot] == external[reuse]
                && root_node.shape == middle.shape
                && middle.shape == inner.shape
                && external
                    .iter()
                    .all(|id| self.graph.nodes()[id.index()].shape == root_node.shape)
                && uses[mul] == 1
                && uses[add] == 1
                && !selected.contains(&mul)
                && !selected.contains(&add)
                && !covered_removed.contains(&mul)
                && !covered_removed.contains(&add)
                && !self.fused_relus.contains_key(&root)
                && !self.fused_pointwise_chains.contains_key(&root)
                && !self.fused_mul_adds.contains_key(&root);
            if !compatible {
                return Err(GpuError::Fp32PtxRejected {
                    reason: format!("invalid mul-add-mul fusion capability at node {root}"),
                });
            }
            covered_removed.insert(mul);
            covered_removed.insert(add);
            optimizations.push(GpuOptimizationCapability {
                root,
                kind: GpuOptimizationKind::MulAddMulFusion,
                removed_nodes: vec![mul, add],
                exclusive_reachable_use: true,
                selected_outputs_preserved: true,
            });
        }

        for (&root, &(mul, slot)) in &self.fused_mul_adds {
            let root_node = &self.graph.nodes()[root];
            let producer = &self.graph.nodes()[mul];
            let exclusive = uses[mul] == 1;
            let preserves = !selected.contains(&mul);
            let compatible = slot < 2
                && matches!(root_node.operation, Operation::Add)
                && matches!(producer.operation, Operation::Mul)
                && root_node.inputs[slot].index() == mul
                && root_node.shape == producer.shape
                && producer
                    .inputs
                    .iter()
                    .all(|&id| self.graph.nodes()[id.index()].shape == root_node.shape)
                && self.graph.nodes()[root_node.inputs[1 - slot].index()].shape == root_node.shape
                && !covered_removed.contains(&mul)
                && !self.fused_relus.contains_key(&root)
                && !self.fused_pointwise_chains.contains_key(&root);
            if !exclusive || !preserves || !compatible {
                return Err(GpuError::Fp32PtxRejected {
                    reason: format!("invalid mul-add fusion capability at node {root}"),
                });
            }
            covered_removed.insert(mul);
            optimizations.push(GpuOptimizationCapability {
                root,
                kind: GpuOptimizationKind::MulAddFusion,
                removed_nodes: vec![mul],
                exclusive_reachable_use: true,
                selected_outputs_preserved: true,
            });
        }

        for (&root, &(left, right_first, right_second, reused, right_slot, left_slot)) in
            &self.fused_mul_diamond_adds
        {
            if reused > 1 || right_slot > 1 || left_slot > 1 {
                return Err(GpuError::Fp32PtxRejected {
                    reason: format!("invalid MulDiamondAdd selectors at node {root}"),
                });
            }
            let output = &self.graph.nodes()[root];
            let lhs = &self.graph.nodes()[left];
            let rhs = &self.graph.nodes()[right_first];
            let repeated = &self.graph.nodes()[right_second];
            let compatible = matches!(output.operation, Operation::Add)
                && matches!(lhs.operation, Operation::Mul)
                && matches!(rhs.operation, Operation::Mul)
                && matches!(repeated.operation, Operation::Mul)
                && output.inputs[left_slot].index() == left
                && output.inputs[1 - left_slot].index() == right_second
                && repeated.inputs[right_slot].index() == right_first
                && repeated.inputs[1 - right_slot] == rhs.inputs[reused]
                && [left, right_first, right_second]
                    .iter()
                    .all(|&id| uses[id] == 1)
                && [left, right_first, right_second]
                    .iter()
                    .all(|id| !selected.contains(id))
                && [left, right_first, right_second]
                    .iter()
                    .all(|id| !covered_removed.contains(id))
                && lhs.shape == output.shape
                && rhs.shape == output.shape
                && repeated.shape == output.shape
                && lhs
                    .inputs
                    .iter()
                    .chain(&rhs.inputs)
                    .all(|&id| self.graph.nodes()[id.index()].shape == output.shape)
                && !self.fused_mul_adds.contains_key(&root)
                && !self.fused_binary_pairs.contains_key(&root)
                && !self.fused_mul_add_muls.contains_key(&root);
            if !compatible {
                return Err(GpuError::Fp32PtxRejected {
                    reason: format!("invalid MulDiamondAdd fusion at node {root}"),
                });
            }
            covered_removed.extend([left, right_first, right_second]);
            optimizations.push(GpuOptimizationCapability {
                root,
                kind: GpuOptimizationKind::MulDiamondAddFusion,
                removed_nodes: vec![left, right_first, right_second],
                exclusive_reachable_use: true,
                selected_outputs_preserved: true,
            });
        }

        for (&root, &(inner, middle, add, reused, middle_slot, add_slot)) in
            &self.fused_mul_mul_add_divs
        {
            if reused > 1 || middle_slot > 1 || add_slot > 1 {
                return Err(GpuError::Fp32PtxRejected {
                    reason: format!("invalid four-operation fusion selectors at {root}"),
                });
            }
            let output = &self.graph.nodes()[root];
            let first = &self.graph.nodes()[inner];
            let second = &self.graph.nodes()[middle];
            let sum = &self.graph.nodes()[add];
            let div = matches!(&output.operation, Operation::Pointwise(spec)
                if supported_pointwise(spec) == Some(TranslationKind::DivRne));
            let sources = [
                first.inputs[0],
                first.inputs[1],
                sum.inputs[1 - add_slot],
                output.inputs[1],
            ];
            let compatible = div
                && matches!(first.operation, Operation::Mul)
                && matches!(second.operation, Operation::Mul)
                && matches!(sum.operation, Operation::Add)
                && output.inputs[0].index() == add
                && sum.inputs[add_slot].index() == middle
                && second.inputs[middle_slot].index() == inner
                && second.inputs[1 - middle_slot] == first.inputs[reused]
                && output.shape == first.shape
                && output.shape == second.shape
                && output.shape == sum.shape
                && sources
                    .iter()
                    .all(|id| self.graph.nodes()[id.index()].shape == output.shape)
                && [inner, middle, add].iter().all(|&id| uses[id] == 1)
                && [inner, middle, add].iter().all(|id| !selected.contains(id))
                && [inner, middle, add]
                    .iter()
                    .all(|id| !covered_removed.contains(id))
                && !self.fused_mul_adds.contains_key(&add)
                && !self.fused_binary_pairs.contains_key(&add);
            if !compatible {
                return Err(GpuError::Fp32PtxRejected {
                    reason: format!("invalid four-operation fusion at node {root}"),
                });
            }
            covered_removed.extend([inner, middle, add]);
            optimizations.push(GpuOptimizationCapability {
                root,
                kind: GpuOptimizationKind::MulMulAddDivFusion,
                removed_nodes: vec![inner, middle, add],
                exclusive_reachable_use: true,
                selected_outputs_preserved: true,
            });
        }

        for (&root, &(sqrt, add, slot)) in &self.fused_sqrt_add_divs {
            let output = &self.graph.nodes()[root];
            let middle = &self.graph.nodes()[add];
            let inner = &self.graph.nodes()[sqrt];
            let div = matches!(&output.operation, Operation::Pointwise(spec)
                if supported_pointwise(spec) == Some(TranslationKind::DivRne));
            let square_root = matches!(&inner.operation, Operation::Pointwise(spec)
                if supported_pointwise(spec) == Some(TranslationKind::SqrtRne));
            let compatible = slot < 2
                && div
                && square_root
                && matches!(middle.operation, Operation::Add)
                && output.inputs[1].index() == add
                && middle.inputs[slot].index() == sqrt
                && output.shape == middle.shape
                && middle.shape == inner.shape
                && [inner.inputs[0], middle.inputs[1 - slot], output.inputs[0]]
                    .iter()
                    .all(|&id| self.graph.nodes()[id.index()].shape == output.shape)
                && uses[sqrt] == 1
                && uses[add] == 1
                && !selected.contains(&sqrt)
                && !selected.contains(&add)
                && !covered_removed.contains(&sqrt)
                && !covered_removed.contains(&add)
                && !self.fused_mul_adds.contains_key(&add)
                && !self.fused_mul_add_muls.contains_key(&add)
                && !self.fused_binary_pairs.contains_key(&add);
            if !compatible {
                return Err(GpuError::Fp32PtxRejected {
                    reason: format!("invalid sqrt-add-div fusion at node {root}"),
                });
            }
            covered_removed.insert(sqrt);
            covered_removed.insert(add);
            optimizations.push(GpuOptimizationCapability {
                root,
                kind: GpuOptimizationKind::SqrtAddDivFusion,
                removed_nodes: vec![sqrt, add],
                exclusive_reachable_use: true,
                selected_outputs_preserved: true,
            });
        }

        for (&root, &(producer, slot)) in &self.fused_binary_pairs {
            let output = &self.graph.nodes()[root];
            let inner = &self.graph.nodes()[producer];
            let compatible = slot < 2
                && matches!(output.operation, Operation::Add | Operation::Mul)
                && matches!(inner.operation, Operation::Add | Operation::Mul)
                && !(matches!(output.operation, Operation::Add)
                    && matches!(inner.operation, Operation::Mul))
                && output.inputs[slot].index() == producer
                && output.shape == inner.shape
                && inner
                    .inputs
                    .iter()
                    .all(|id| self.graph.nodes()[id.index()].shape == output.shape)
                && self.graph.nodes()[output.inputs[1 - slot].index()].shape == output.shape
                && uses[producer] == 1
                && !selected.contains(&producer)
                && !covered_removed.contains(&producer)
                && !self.fused_mul_adds.contains_key(&root)
                && !self.fused_mul_add_muls.contains_key(&root)
                && !self.fused_mul_adds.contains_key(&producer)
                && !self.fused_mul_add_muls.contains_key(&producer)
                && !self.fused_relus.contains_key(&root)
                && !self.fused_pointwise_chains.contains_key(&root);
            if !compatible {
                return Err(GpuError::Fp32PtxRejected {
                    reason: format!("invalid binary pointwise fusion at node {root}"),
                });
            }
            covered_removed.insert(producer);
            optimizations.push(GpuOptimizationCapability {
                root,
                kind: GpuOptimizationKind::BinaryPointwiseFusion,
                removed_nodes: vec![producer],
                exclusive_reachable_use: true,
                selected_outputs_preserved: true,
            });
        }

        for (&root, &earlier) in &self.fused_dual_outputs {
            let left = &self.graph.nodes()[earlier];
            let right = &self.graph.nodes()[root];
            let valid = earlier < root
                && self.live_nodes.binary_search(&earlier).is_ok()
                && self.live_nodes.binary_search(&root).is_ok()
                && uses[earlier] >= 1
                && uses[root] >= 1
                && self.live_nodes.iter().all(|&consumer| {
                    consumer > root
                        || self.graph.nodes()[consumer]
                            .inputs
                            .iter()
                            .all(|input| input.index() != earlier)
                })
                && matches!(left.operation, Operation::Add | Operation::Mul)
                && matches!(right.operation, Operation::Add | Operation::Mul)
                && left.shape == right.shape
                && left.dtype == DType::F32
                && right.dtype == DType::F32
                && left.inputs.iter().chain(&right.inputs).all(|id| {
                    self.graph.nodes()[id.index()].shape == right.shape
                        && self.graph.nodes()[id.index()].dtype == DType::F32
                        && !skipped.contains(&id.index())
                })
                && !covered_removed.contains(&earlier);
            if !valid {
                return Err(GpuError::Fp32PtxRejected {
                    reason: format!("invalid dual-output pointwise fusion at node {root}"),
                });
            }
            covered_removed.insert(earlier);
            optimizations.push(GpuOptimizationCapability {
                root,
                kind: GpuOptimizationKind::DualPointwiseOutputFusion,
                removed_nodes: vec![earlier],
                // The standalone kernel is removed, not the materialized
                // value. Downstream fanout is permitted after this root.
                exclusive_reachable_use: uses[earlier] == 1,
                selected_outputs_preserved: true,
            });
        }
        if covered_removed != skipped {
            return Err(GpuError::Fp32PtxRejected {
                reason: "capability plan does not explain every removed fusion kernel".into(),
            });
        }

        Ok(GpuCapabilityPlan {
            kernels,
            optimizations,
            boundary: GpuAssuranceBoundary {
                memory_address_arithmetic: GpuAssuranceStatus::GeneratedLeanObligation,
                llvm_ptx_structure: GpuAssuranceStatus::RequiredAtLowering,
                ideal_to_fp32: GpuAssuranceStatus::SeparateNumericProofRequired,
                cuda_runtime: GpuAssuranceStatus::RuntimeAcceptanceRequired,
                jit_sass_correspondence: GpuAssuranceStatus::NotEstablished,
            },
        })
    }

    /// Named Lean theorems for natural-number address bounds of the actual
    /// launched kernel contracts. Generation is not proof; certified builders
    /// must kernel-check and axiom-audit this program.
    pub fn memory_lean_program(&self) -> Result<LeanProgram, GpuError> {
        let mut source = format!(
            "{}\n\n{}\n",
            include_str!("../../../../lean/VeriNeural/Basic.lean"),
            include_str!("../../../../lean/VeriNeural/Memory.lean")
        );
        source.push_str("\nnamespace VeriNeural.Generated\n");
        let mut theorems = Vec::new();
        for contract in self.memory_contracts()? {
            source.push_str(&format!(
                "-- IR kernel {}: {} source tensors, {} output elements.\n",
                contract.kernel_node,
                contract.reads.len(),
                contract.writes
            ));
            let output_name = format!("memory_node_{}_output_bound", contract.kernel_node);
            source.push_str(&format!(
                "theorem {output_name} (index : Nat) (active : index < {}) : index < {} := by\n  exact VeriNeural.pointwise_address_bound active\n\n",
                contract.writes, contract.writes
            ));
            theorems.push(output_name);
            for &(other, extent) in &contract.additional_writes {
                let name = format!(
                    "memory_node_{}_additional_{}_output_bound",
                    contract.kernel_node, other
                );
                source.push_str(&format!(
                    "theorem {name} (index : Nat) (active : index < {extent}) : index < {extent} := by\n  exact VeriNeural.pointwise_address_bound active\n\n"
                ));
                theorems.push(name);
            }
            match contract.pattern {
                GpuMemoryPattern::Pointwise => {}
                GpuMemoryPattern::BiasAdd { columns } => {
                    let name = format!("memory_node_{}_bias_bound", contract.kernel_node);
                    source.push_str(&format!(
                        "theorem {name} (index : Nat) : index % {columns} < {columns} := by\n  exact VeriNeural.bias_address_bound (by decide)\n\n"
                    ));
                    theorems.push(name);
                }
                GpuMemoryPattern::MatMul {
                    rows,
                    inner,
                    columns,
                } => {
                    let name = format!("memory_node_{}_matmul_bounds", contract.kernel_node);
                    source.push_str(&format!(
                        "theorem {name} (index j : Nat) (active : index < {rows} * {columns}) (reduction : j < {inner}) :\n    (index / {columns}) * {inner} + j < {rows} * {inner} ∧\n    j * {columns} + index % {columns} < {inner} * {columns} := by\n  exact VeriNeural.matmul_address_bounds (by decide) active reduction\n\n"
                    ));
                    theorems.push(name);
                }
                GpuMemoryPattern::Transpose2D { rows, columns } => {
                    let name = format!("memory_node_{}_transpose_bound", contract.kernel_node);
                    source.push_str(&format!(
                        "theorem {name} (index : Nat) (active : index < {rows} * {columns}) :\n    (index % {rows}) * {columns} + index / {rows} < {rows} * {columns} := by\n  exact VeriNeural.transpose2d_address_bound (by decide) active\n\n"
                    ));
                    theorems.push(name);
                }
                GpuMemoryPattern::ReverseRows2D { rows, columns } => {
                    let name = format!("memory_node_{}_reverse_rows_bound", contract.kernel_node);
                    source.push_str(&format!(
                        "theorem {name} (index : Nat) (active : index < {rows} * {columns}) :\n    ({rows} - 1 - index / {columns}) * {columns} + index % {columns} < {rows} * {columns} := by\n  exact VeriNeural.reverse_rows2d_address_bound (by decide) (by decide) active\n\n"
                    ));
                    theorems.push(name);
                }
                GpuMemoryPattern::ReverseColumns2D { rows, columns } => {
                    let name =
                        format!("memory_node_{}_reverse_columns_bound", contract.kernel_node);
                    source.push_str(&format!(
                        "theorem {name} (index : Nat) (active : index < {rows} * {columns}) :\n    (index / {columns}) * {columns} + ({columns} - 1 - index % {columns}) < {rows} * {columns} := by\n  exact VeriNeural.reverse_columns2d_address_bound (by decide) active\n\n"
                    ));
                    theorems.push(name);
                }
                GpuMemoryPattern::BroadcastScalar => {
                    let name = format!(
                        "memory_node_{}_broadcast_scalar_bound",
                        contract.kernel_node
                    );
                    source.push_str(&format!("theorem {name} : 0 < 1 := by decide\n\n"));
                    theorems.push(name);
                }
                GpuMemoryPattern::SliceLastRow {
                    start,
                    source_width,
                } => {
                    let name = format!("memory_node_{}_slice_bound", contract.kernel_node);
                    source.push_str(&format!(
                        "theorem {name} (index : Nat) (active : index < {}) : index + {start} < {source_width} := by\n  exact VeriNeural.slice_last_row_address_bound active (by decide)\n\n",
                        contract.writes
                    ));
                    theorems.push(name);
                }
                GpuMemoryPattern::ConcatAxis0 { left } => {
                    let right = contract.reads[1].1;
                    let left_name =
                        format!("memory_node_{}_concat_left_bound", contract.kernel_node);
                    source.push_str(&format!(
                        "theorem {left_name} (index : Nat) (active : index < {left}) : index < {left} := by\n  exact VeriNeural.pointwise_address_bound active\n\n"
                    ));
                    theorems.push(left_name);
                    let right_name =
                        format!("memory_node_{}_concat_right_bound", contract.kernel_node);
                    source.push_str(&format!(
                        "theorem {right_name} (index : Nat) (branch : {left} ≤ index) (active : index < {left} + {right}) : index - {left} < {right} := by\n  exact VeriNeural.concat_axis0_right_address_bound branch active\n\n"
                    ));
                    theorems.push(right_name);
                }
                GpuMemoryPattern::ArgMaxLast { width } => {
                    let rows = contract.writes;
                    let first_name =
                        format!("memory_node_{}_argmax_first_bound", contract.kernel_node);
                    source.push_str(&format!(
                        "theorem {first_name} (index : Nat) (active : index < {rows}) : index * {width} < {rows} * {width} := by\n  exact VeriNeural.argmax_first_address_bound (by decide) active\n\n"
                    ));
                    theorems.push(first_name);
                    let candidate_name = format!(
                        "memory_node_{}_argmax_candidate_bound",
                        contract.kernel_node
                    );
                    source.push_str(&format!(
                        "theorem {candidate_name} (index lane : Nat) (active : index < {rows}) (candidate : lane < {width}) : index * {width} + lane < {rows} * {width} := by\n  exact VeriNeural.argmax_candidate_address_bound active candidate\n\n"
                    ));
                    theorems.push(candidate_name);
                }
                GpuMemoryPattern::TakeAxis0 { lane, choices } => {
                    let index_name =
                        format!("memory_node_{}_take_index_nonempty", contract.kernel_node);
                    source.push_str(&format!("theorem {index_name} : 0 < 1 := by decide\n\n"));
                    theorems.push(index_name);
                    let bound_name = format!("memory_node_{}_take_bound", contract.kernel_node);
                    source.push_str(&format!(
                        "theorem {bound_name} (selected index : Nat) (selectedBound : selected < {choices}) (active : index < {lane}) : selected * {lane} + index < {choices} * {lane} := by\n  exact VeriNeural.take_axis0_address_bound selectedBound active\n\n"
                    ));
                    theorems.push(bound_name);
                }
            }
        }
        source.push_str("end VeriNeural.Generated\n");
        Ok(LeanProgram::generated(source, theorems, Vec::new()))
    }

    /// Backwards-compatible source view over the named memory obligations.
    pub fn memory_lean_source(&self) -> Result<String, GpuError> {
        Ok(self.memory_lean_program()?.source().to_owned())
    }

    /// The Lean proof of the *ideal integer* fusion rule, not PTX/FP32 equivalence.
    /// None when no fusion was actually applied.
    pub fn fusion_lean_source(&self) -> Option<String> {
        (!self.fused_relus.is_empty()).then(|| {
            format!(
                "{}\n\n{}",
                include_str!("../../../../lean/VeriNeural/Basic.lean"),
                include_str!("../../../../lean/VeriNeural/Fusion.lean"),
            )
        })
    }
}


FILE	crates/verineural/src/ir.rs
use std::collections::{BTreeMap, BTreeSet};
use std::ops::Range;
use std::sync::atomic::{AtomicU64, Ordering};

use crate::{NeuralError, PointwiseExpr, PointwiseSpec, Shape};

static NEXT_GRAPH_ID: AtomicU64 = AtomicU64::new(1);

/// A *declared* value domain; source-node assertions are not proofs.
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum Domain {
    Any,
    Finite,
    NonNegativeFinite,
}

/// Semantic element type carried by a graph node. Source tensors are currently
/// binary32; index tensors are produced by indexing primitives such as argmax.
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum DType {
    F32,
    Index,
}

impl DType {
    pub const fn name(self) -> &'static str {
        match self {
            Self::F32 => "binary32",
            Self::Index => "index",
        }
    }
}

/// Deterministic tie handling for argmax. The first maximal lane wins.
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum ArgMaxTieBreak {
    First,
}

impl ArgMaxTieBreak {
    pub const fn name(self) -> &'static str {
        match self {
            Self::First => "first",
        }
    }
}

impl Domain {
    pub const fn name(self) -> &'static str {
        match self {
            Self::Any => "any",
            Self::Finite => "finite",
            Self::NonNegativeFinite => "nonnegative_finite",
        }
    }

    /// Whether this domain is at least as restrictive as the required domain.
    pub fn satisfies(self, required: Self) -> bool {
        matches!(
            (self, required),
            (_, Self::Any)
                | (Self::Finite, Self::Finite)
                | (
                    Self::NonNegativeFinite,
                    Self::Finite | Self::NonNegativeFinite
                )
        )
    }
}

/// FP32 rounding requirement (not yet checked against executable code).
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum RoundingMode {
    NearestTiesToEven,
}

/// Whether multiplication and addition may be silently contracted.
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum FmaMode {
    SeparateOperations,
}

/// Subnormal treatment required by a future backend.
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum SubnormalMode {
    Preserve,
}

/// Order required for accumulation within a reduction.
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum ReductionOrder {
    LeftToRight,
}

/// Explicit *target* numerical policy. It carries no proof of IEEE compliance.
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct FP32Policy {
    pub rounding: RoundingMode,
    pub fma: FmaMode,
    pub subnormals: SubnormalMode,
    pub reduction: ReductionOrder,
}

impl FP32Policy {
    pub const fn strict() -> Self {
        Self {
            rounding: RoundingMode::NearestTiesToEven,
            fma: FmaMode::SeparateOperations,
            subnormals: SubnormalMode::Preserve,
            reduction: ReductionOrder::LeftToRight,
        }
    }
}

impl Default for FP32Policy {
    fn default() -> Self {
        Self::strict()
    }
}

/// GPUs are not lowered or verified in stage 2.
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum GpuSemantics {
    NotLowered,
}

/// The supported Rust IR DSL. No general Rust parser or arbitrary closures yet.
#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum Operation {
    Input,
    Add,
    Mul,
    MatMul,
    BiasAdd,
    Relu,
    /// Elementwise 1 when x > 0, otherwise 0 (including NaN in host f32).
    PositiveMask,
    /// Choose true/false tensors by mask > 0, preserving selected element bits.
    SelectPositive,
    Sqrt,
    Reshape(Shape),
    /// A versioned external atomic operation with declarative pointwise semantics.
    Pointwise(PointwiseSpec),
    /// Reduce one row-major tensor axis with an explicit left-to-right sum.
    ReduceSum {
        axis: usize,
    },
    /// Deterministic maximum along one axis, with first-tie policy.
    ReduceMax {
        axis: usize,
    },
    /// Right-aligned, singleton-axis broadcasting.
    BroadcastTo(Shape),
    /// Reorder tensor axes. `axes[output_axis] = input_axis`.
    Permute {
        axes: Vec<usize>,
    },
    /// Reverse one tensor axis without changing its shape.
    ReverseAxis {
        axis: usize,
    },
    /// Concatenate two same-rank tensors along one axis.
    Concat {
        axis: usize,
    },
    /// Select a static contiguous interval of one axis, preserving rank.
    SliceAxis {
        axis: usize,
        start: usize,
        len: usize,
    },
    /// Reduce one axis to deterministic index values. F32 NaN/tie behavior is
    /// fixed by the selected policy instead of delegated to a backend accident.
    ArgMax {
        axis: usize,
        tie_break: ArgMaxTieBreak,
    },
    /// Select one lane from `data` using a one-element Index tensor.
    Take {
        axis: usize,
    },
}

impl Operation {
    pub const fn name(&self) -> &'static str {
        match self {
            Self::Input => "input",
            Self::Add => "add",
            Self::Mul => "mul",
            Self::MatMul => "matmul",
            Self::BiasAdd => "bias_add",
            Self::Relu => "relu",
            Self::PositiveMask => "positive_mask",
            Self::SelectPositive => "select_positive",
            Self::Sqrt => "sqrt",
            Self::Reshape(_) => "reshape",
            Self::Pointwise(_) => "pointwise",
            Self::ReduceSum { .. } => "reduce_sum",
            Self::ReduceMax { .. } => "reduce_max",
            Self::BroadcastTo(_) => "broadcast_to",
            Self::Permute { .. } => "permute",
            Self::ReverseAxis { .. } => "reverse_axis",
            Self::Concat { .. } => "concat",
            Self::SliceAxis { .. } => "slice_axis",
            Self::ArgMax { .. } => "argmax",
            Self::Take { .. } => "take",
        }
    }

    pub const fn arity(&self) -> usize {
        match self {
            Self::Input => 0,
            Self::Add | Self::Mul | Self::MatMul | Self::BiasAdd => 2,
            Self::SelectPositive => 3,
            Self::Relu
            | Self::PositiveMask
            | Self::Sqrt
            | Self::Reshape(_)
            | Self::BroadcastTo(_) => 1,
            Self::Pointwise(spec) => spec.arity(),
            Self::ReduceSum { .. }
            | Self::ReduceMax { .. }
            | Self::Permute { .. }
            | Self::ReverseAxis { .. }
            | Self::SliceAxis { .. }
            | Self::ArgMax { .. } => 1,
            Self::Concat { .. } | Self::Take { .. } => 2,
        }
    }

    /// One source of truth for graph and concrete host-operation shape rules.
    pub fn infer_shape(&self, inputs: &[Shape]) -> Result<Shape, NeuralError> {
        if matches!(self, Self::Input) {
            return Err(NeuralError::InputCannotBeApplied);
        }
        if inputs.len() != self.arity() {
            return Err(NeuralError::WrongArity {
                operation: self.name(),
                expected: self.arity(),
                actual: inputs.len(),
            });
        }
        match self {
            Self::Add | Self::Mul | Self::SelectPositive | Self::Pointwise(_) => {
                for other in &inputs[1..] {
                    if inputs[0] != *other {
                        return Err(NeuralError::ShapeMismatch {
                            expected: inputs[0].clone(),
                            actual: other.clone(),
                        });
                    }
                }
                Ok(inputs[0].clone())
            }
            Self::MatMul => {
                for shape in inputs {
                    if shape.rank() != 2 {
                        return Err(NeuralError::RankMismatch {
                            operation: self.name(),
                            expected: 2,
                            actual: shape.rank(),
                        });
                    }
                }
                let a = inputs[0].dims();
                let b = inputs[1].dims();
                if a[1] != b[0] {
                    return Err(NeuralError::InnerDimensionMismatch {
                        left: a[1],
                        right: b[0],
                    });
                }
                Shape::new(vec![a[0], b[1]])
            }
            Self::BiasAdd => {
                if inputs[0].rank() != 2 {
                    return Err(NeuralError::RankMismatch {
                        operation: self.name(),
                        expected: 2,
                        actual: inputs[0].rank(),
                    });
                }
                if inputs[1].rank() != 1 {
                    return Err(NeuralError::RankMismatch {
                        operation: self.name(),
                        expected: 1,
                        actual: inputs[1].rank(),
                    });
                }
                if inputs[0].dims()[1] != inputs[1].dims()[0] {
                    return Err(NeuralError::BiasWidthMismatch {
                        columns: inputs[0].dims()[1],
                        bias_length: inputs[1].dims()[0],
                    });
                }
                Ok(inputs[0].clone())
            }
            Self::Relu | Self::PositiveMask | Self::Sqrt => Ok(inputs[0].clone()),
            Self::ReduceSum { axis } | Self::ReduceMax { axis } => {
                let input = &inputs[0];
                if *axis >= input.rank() {
                    return Err(NeuralError::InvalidAxis {
                        axis: *axis,
                        rank: input.rank(),
                    });
                }
                let mut dims = input.dims().to_vec();
                dims.remove(*axis);
                Shape::new(dims)
            }
            Self::BroadcastTo(output) => {
                let input = &inputs[0];
                if input.rank() > output.rank()
                    || input
                        .dims()
                        .iter()
                        .rev()
                        .zip(output.dims().iter().rev())
                        .any(|(&source, &target)| source != 1 && source != target)
                {
                    return Err(NeuralError::ShapeMismatch {
                        expected: output.clone(),
                        actual: input.clone(),
                    });
                }
                Ok(output.clone())
            }
            Self::Permute { axes } => {
                let input = &inputs[0];
                if axes.len() != input.rank() {
                    return Err(NeuralError::InvalidPermutation {
                        rank: input.rank(),
                        axes: axes.clone(),
                    });
                }
                let mut seen = vec![false; input.rank()];
                for &axis in axes {
                    if axis >= input.rank() || seen[axis] {
                        return Err(NeuralError::InvalidPermutation {
                            rank: input.rank(),
                            axes: axes.clone(),
                        });
                    }
                    seen[axis] = true;
                }
                Shape::new(
                    axes.iter()
                        .map(|&axis| input.dims()[axis])
                        .collect::<Vec<_>>(),
                )
            }
            Self::ReverseAxis { axis } => {
                if *axis >= inputs[0].rank() {
                    return Err(NeuralError::InvalidAxis {
                        axis: *axis,
                        rank: inputs[0].rank(),
                    });
                }
                Ok(inputs[0].clone())
            }
            Self::SliceAxis { axis, start, len } => {
                let input = &inputs[0];
                if *axis >= input.rank() {
                    return Err(NeuralError::InvalidAxis {
                        axis: *axis,
                        rank: input.rank(),
                    });
                }
                let extent = input.dims()[*axis];
                let end = start.checked_add(*len).ok_or(NeuralError::InvalidSlice {
                    axis: *axis,
                    start: *start,
                    len: *len,
                    extent,
                })?;
                if *len == 0 || *start >= extent || end > extent {
                    return Err(NeuralError::InvalidSlice {
                        axis: *axis,
                        start: *start,
                        len: *len,
                        extent,
                    });
                }
                let mut dims = input.dims().to_vec();
                dims[*axis] = *len;
                Shape::new(dims)
            }
            Self::Concat { axis } => {
                let left = &inputs[0];
                let right = &inputs[1];
                if left.rank() != right.rank() {
                    return Err(NeuralError::RankMismatch {
                        operation: self.name(),
                        expected: left.rank(),
                        actual: right.rank(),
                    });
                }
                if *axis >= left.rank() {
                    return Err(NeuralError::InvalidAxis {
                        axis: *axis,
                        rank: left.rank(),
                    });
                }
                for dim in 0..left.rank() {
                    if dim != *axis && left.dims()[dim] != right.dims()[dim] {
                        return Err(NeuralError::ShapeMismatch {
                            expected: left.clone(),
                            actual: right.clone(),
                        });
                    }
                }
                let mut dims = left.dims().to_vec();
                dims[*axis] = dims[*axis]
                    .checked_add(right.dims()[*axis])
                    .ok_or(NeuralError::ElementCountOverflow)?;
                Shape::new(dims)
            }
            Self::ArgMax { axis, .. } => {
                let input = &inputs[0];
                if *axis >= input.rank() {
                    return Err(NeuralError::InvalidAxis {
                        axis: *axis,
                        rank: input.rank(),
                    });
                }
                let mut dims = input.dims().to_vec();
                dims.remove(*axis);
                Shape::new(dims)
            }
            Self::Take { axis } => {
                let data = &inputs[0];
                let index = &inputs[1];
                if *axis >= data.rank() {
                    return Err(NeuralError::InvalidAxis {
                        axis: *axis,
                        rank: data.rank(),
                    });
                }
                if index.element_count() != 1 {
                    return Err(NeuralError::IndexElementCountMismatch {
                        expected: 1,
                        actual: index.element_count(),
                    });
                }
                let mut dims = data.dims().to_vec();
                dims.remove(*axis);
                Shape::new(dims)
            }
            Self::Reshape(output) => {
                if inputs[0].element_count() != output.element_count() {
                    return Err(NeuralError::ElementCountMismatch {
                        expected: inputs[0].element_count(),
                        actual: output.element_count(),
                    });
                }
                Ok(output.clone())
            }
            Self::Input => unreachable!("handled before shape inference"),
        }
    }

    fn required_domain(&self) -> Domain {
        match self {
            Self::Sqrt => Domain::NonNegativeFinite,
            _ => Domain::Any,
        }
    }

    fn infer_dtype(&self, inputs: &[DType]) -> Result<DType, NeuralError> {
        let require = |position: usize, expected: DType| -> Result<(), NeuralError> {
            let actual = inputs[position];
            if actual != expected {
                return Err(NeuralError::DTypeMismatch {
                    operation: self.name(),
                    expected,
                    actual,
                });
            }
            Ok(())
        };
        match self {
            Self::Input => Err(NeuralError::InputCannotBeApplied),
            Self::Take { .. } => {
                require(0, DType::F32)?;
                require(1, DType::Index)?;
                Ok(DType::F32)
            }
            Self::ArgMax { .. } => {
                require(0, DType::F32)?;
                Ok(DType::Index)
            }
            _ => {
                for position in 0..inputs.len() {
                    require(position, DType::F32)?;
                }
                Ok(DType::F32)
            }
        }
    }

    /// Conservative domain propagation; finite inputs may overflow in FP32.
    fn infer_domain(&self, inputs: &[Domain]) -> Domain {
        match self {
            Self::Relu => {
                if inputs[0].satisfies(Domain::Finite) {
                    Domain::NonNegativeFinite
                } else {
                    Domain::Any
                }
            }
            Self::Sqrt | Self::PositiveMask => Domain::NonNegativeFinite,
            Self::SelectPositive => {
                if inputs[1].satisfies(Domain::NonNegativeFinite)
                    && inputs[2].satisfies(Domain::NonNegativeFinite)
                {
                    Domain::NonNegativeFinite
                } else if inputs[1].satisfies(Domain::Finite) && inputs[2].satisfies(Domain::Finite)
                {
                    Domain::Finite
                } else {
                    Domain::Any
                }
            }
            Self::Reshape(_)
            | Self::BroadcastTo(_)
            | Self::ReduceMax { .. }
            | Self::Permute { .. }
            | Self::ReverseAxis { .. }
            | Self::SliceAxis { .. } => inputs[0],
            Self::Concat { .. } => {
                if inputs
                    .iter()
                    .all(|domain| domain.satisfies(Domain::NonNegativeFinite))
                {
                    Domain::NonNegativeFinite
                } else if inputs.iter().all(|domain| domain.satisfies(Domain::Finite)) {
                    Domain::Finite
                } else {
                    Domain::Any
                }
            }
            Self::Take { .. } => inputs[0],
            Self::ArgMax { .. } => Domain::Any,
            Self::Input
            | Self::Add
            | Self::Mul
            | Self::MatMul
            | Self::BiasAdd
            | Self::Pointwise(_)
            | Self::ReduceSum { .. } => Domain::Any,
        }
    }
}

/// A port's structural and value-domain requirements or guarantees.
#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct PortContract {
    pub shape: Shape,
    pub dtype: DType,
    pub domain: Domain,
}

impl PortContract {
    pub fn new(shape: Shape, domain: Domain) -> Self {
        Self {
            shape,
            dtype: DType::F32,
            domain,
        }
    }

    pub fn index(shape: Shape) -> Self {
        Self {
            shape,
            dtype: DType::Index,
            domain: Domain::Any,
        }
    }

    fn typed(shape: Shape, dtype: DType, domain: Domain) -> Self {
        Self {
            shape,
            dtype,
            domain,
        }
    }

    pub fn any(shape: Shape) -> Self {
        Self::new(shape, Domain::Any)
    }

    pub fn finite(shape: Shape) -> Self {
        Self::new(shape, Domain::Finite)
    }

    pub fn nonnegative(shape: Shape) -> Self {
        Self::new(shape, Domain::NonNegativeFinite)
    }
}

/// Independent mathematical claims about a module's output (ideal-Int semantics).
/// Declaration is never proof. Claims create mandatory Lean obligations.
#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum ContractClaim {
    Nonnegative,
    EqualsInput(usize),
    /// A user-declared, independently proved ideal-Int predicate.
    Predicate(Predicate),
}

/// A reference in a proof predicate. Module contracts use Input/Output,
/// architecture goals use Node; mixing these contexts is rejected.
#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum ValueRef {
    Input(usize),
    Output,
    Node(NodeId),
}

/// Typed, data-only proof obligations. No injected Lean text or trusted callback.
/// The supported prover currently handles tensor equality, nonnegativity and
/// pointwise ordering. Unsupported claims fail closed at proof generation/check.
#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum Predicate {
    Nonnegative(ValueRef),
    Equal(ValueRef, ValueRef),
    PointwiseLe(ValueRef, ValueRef),
}

impl Predicate {
    pub fn nonnegative(value: ValueRef) -> Self {
        Self::Nonnegative(value)
    }

    pub fn equal(left: ValueRef, right: ValueRef) -> Self {
        Self::Equal(left, right)
    }

    pub fn pointwise_le(lower: ValueRef, upper: ValueRef) -> Self {
        Self::PointwiseLe(lower, upper)
    }
}

/// A machine-checkable *structural* contract. It is NOT a Lean proof.
///
/// Output guarantees are accepted only if the graph's conservative inference
/// supports them. Source input domains remain caller-supplied assumptions.
#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct MathContract {
    pub requires: Vec<PortContract>,
    pub ensures: PortContract,
    pub claims: Vec<ContractClaim>,
}

impl MathContract {
    pub fn new(requires: Vec<PortContract>, ensures: PortContract) -> Self {
        Self {
            requires,
            ensures,
            claims: Vec::new(),
        }
    }

    /// The declared claim is checked in the Lean backend, not in this builder.
    pub fn with_claim(mut self, claim: ContractClaim) -> Self {
        self.claims.push(claim);
        self
    }

    pub fn nonnegative(self) -> Self {
        self.with_claim(ContractClaim::Nonnegative)
    }

    pub fn equals_input(self, port: usize) -> Self {
        self.with_claim(ContractClaim::EqualsInput(port))
    }

    /// Declare an independent ideal-Int relational contract.
    pub fn predicate(self, predicate: Predicate) -> Self {
        self.with_claim(ContractClaim::Predicate(predicate))
    }
}

/// The three semantic layers: ideal operator, FP32 target, and missing GPU lowering.
#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct OperationSemantics {
    pub ideal: Operation,
    pub fp32: FP32Policy,
    pub gpu: GpuSemantics,
}

/// Node identifiers are scoped to one graph, including transactional clones.
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Hash)]
pub struct NodeId {
    graph: u64,
    index: usize,
}

impl NodeId {
    pub fn index(self) -> usize {
        self.index
    }
}

/// Execution storage contract derived from Semantic IR. The first supported
/// profile is deliberately strict: every value owns contiguous row-major
/// storage except Reshape, which is a zero-copy contiguous alias.
#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum NodeStorage {
    OwnedContiguous { strides: Vec<usize> },
    Alias { source: NodeId, strides: Vec<usize> },
}

impl NodeStorage {
    pub fn strides(&self) -> &[usize] {
        match self {
            Self::OwnedContiguous { strides } | Self::Alias { strides, .. } => strides,
        }
    }

    pub const fn alias_source(&self) -> Option<NodeId> {
        match self {
            Self::OwnedContiguous { .. } => None,
            Self::Alias { source, .. } => Some(*source),
        }
    }

    pub const fn is_alias(&self) -> bool {
        matches!(self, Self::Alias { .. })
    }

    /// Stable text without graph identity; safe for canonical IR/DOT evidence.
    pub fn describe(&self) -> String {
        match self {
            Self::OwnedContiguous { strides } => {
                format!("owned_contiguous:strides={strides:?}")
            }
            Self::Alias { source, strides } => {
                format!("alias_node_{}:strides={strides:?}", source.index())
            }
        }
    }
}

/// Immutable public view of a validated symbolic operation.
#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct Node {
    pub id: NodeId,
    pub operation: Operation,
    pub inputs: Vec<NodeId>,
    pub shape: Shape,
    pub dtype: DType,
    pub domain: Domain,
    pub contract: MathContract,
    pub semantics: OperationSemantics,
}

/// A successful module application, with its declared checked interface.
#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct ModuleInvocation {
    pub name: &'static str,
    pub inputs: Vec<NodeId>,
    /// Half-open interval `[body_start, body_end)` owned by this invocation.
    /// It includes every node created by the body, even nodes created after the
    /// returned output. This is the single source of truth for module ownership.
    pub body_start: usize,
    pub body_end: usize,
    pub output: NodeId,
    pub contract: MathContract,
    /// Versioned semantic declaration, not a proof identifier by itself.
    pub semantic_version: &'static str,
}

impl ModuleInvocation {
    pub fn body_range(&self) -> Range<usize> {
        self.body_start..self.body_end
    }
}

/// Borrowed view over either module kind, in real application order.
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]
pub enum ModuleInstanceRef<'a> {
    Single(&'a ModuleInvocation),
    Multi(&'a MultiModuleInvocation),
}

impl<'a> ModuleInstanceRef<'a> {
    pub fn name(self) -> &'static str {
        match self {
            Self::Single(module) => module.name,
            Self::Multi(module) => module.name,
        }
    }

    pub fn semantic_version(self) -> &'static str {
        match self {
            Self::Single(module) => module.semantic_version,
            Self::Multi(module) => module.semantic_version,
        }
    }

    pub fn inputs(self) -> &'a [NodeId] {
        match self {
            Self::Single(module) => &module.inputs,
            Self::Multi(module) => &module.inputs,
        }
    }

    pub fn outputs(self) -> Vec<NodeId> {
        match self {
            Self::Single(module) => vec![module.output],
            Self::Multi(module) => module.outputs.clone(),
        }
    }

    pub fn contains_output(self, output: NodeId) -> bool {
        match self {
            Self::Single(module) => module.output == output,
            Self::Multi(module) => module.outputs.contains(&output),
        }
    }

    pub fn body_range(self) -> Range<usize> {
        match self {
            Self::Single(module) => module.body_range(),
            Self::Multi(module) => module.body_range(),
        }
    }
}

/// A user-defined, composable symbolic module.
///
/// The body builds graph nodes rather than executing arbitrary Rust code.
/// Contracts are validated structurally; mathematical claims create separate
/// proof obligations in the Lean backend.
pub trait NeuralModule {
    fn name(&self) -> &'static str;
    fn contract(&self) -> &MathContract;
    fn build(&self, graph: &mut NeuralGraph, inputs: &[NodeId]) -> Result<NodeId, NeuralError>;
    fn semantic_version(&self) -> &'static str {
        "unversioned"
    }
}

/// Named output contracts for a multi-output module.
#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct NamedPortContract {
    pub name: &'static str,
    pub port: PortContract,
    pub claims: Vec<ContractClaim>,
}

impl NamedPortContract {
    pub fn new(name: &'static str, port: PortContract) -> Self {
        Self {
            name,
            port,
            claims: Vec::new(),
        }
    }

    pub fn with_claim(mut self, claim: ContractClaim) -> Self {
        self.claims.push(claim);
        self
    }

    pub fn nonnegative(self) -> Self {
        self.with_claim(ContractClaim::Nonnegative)
    }

    pub fn equals_input(self, port: usize) -> Self {
        self.with_claim(ContractClaim::EqualsInput(port))
    }

    /// Declare an independent ideal-Int relational contract.
    pub fn predicate(self, predicate: Predicate) -> Self {
        self.with_claim(ContractClaim::Predicate(predicate))
    }
}

#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct MultiOutputContract {
    pub inputs: Vec<NamedPortContract>,
    pub outputs: Vec<NamedPortContract>,
}

impl MultiOutputContract {
    pub fn new(inputs: Vec<NamedPortContract>, outputs: Vec<NamedPortContract>) -> Self {
        Self { inputs, outputs }
    }
}

pub trait MultiOutputModule {
    fn name(&self) -> &'static str;
    fn contract(&self) -> &MultiOutputContract;
    fn build(&self, graph: &mut NeuralGraph, inputs: &[NodeId])
    -> Result<Vec<NodeId>, NeuralError>;
    fn semantic_version(&self) -> &'static str {
        "unversioned"
    }
}

#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct MultiModuleInvocation {
    pub name: &'static str,
    pub semantic_version: &'static str,
    pub inputs: Vec<NodeId>,
    pub body_start: usize,
    pub body_end: usize,
    pub outputs: Vec<NodeId>,
    pub contract: MultiOutputContract,
}

impl MultiModuleInvocation {
    pub fn body_range(&self) -> Range<usize> {
        self.body_start..self.body_end
    }

    /// Resolve an output by its declared stable port name, rather than relying
    /// on the caller to remember a positional result index.
    pub fn output_named(&self, name: &str) -> Option<NodeId> {
        self.contract
            .outputs
            .iter()
            .zip(&self.outputs)
            .find(|(port, _)| port.name == name)
            .map(|(_, &output)| output)
    }
}

/// A bounded, explicit state-transition chain. `states[0]` is the initial
/// value and `states[t + 1]` is the `next_state` returned at step `t`.
/// This represents finite unrolling, not inductive verification for all time.
#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct FixedScan {
    pub states: Vec<NodeId>,
    pub outputs: Vec<NodeId>,
    /// Indices of instantiated step modules in `NeuralGraph::multi_modules`.
    pub module_indices: Vec<usize>,
}

impl FixedScan {
    /// Select every state transition and readout for a single Lean program.
    /// Proof generation still requires a separate Lean checker invocation.
    pub fn proof_outputs(&self) -> Vec<NodeId> {
        self.states
            .iter()
            .skip(1)
            .chain(self.outputs.iter())
            .copied()
            .collect()
    }
}

#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
enum ModuleInstanceKey {
    Single(usize),
    Multi(usize),
}

/// Append-only Semantic Neural IR with graph-scoped edges and checked contracts.
#[derive(Clone, Debug)]
pub struct NeuralGraph {
    identity: u64,
    policy: FP32Policy,
    nodes: Vec<Node>,
    modules: Vec<ModuleInvocation>,
    multi_modules: Vec<MultiModuleInvocation>,
    module_order: Vec<ModuleInstanceKey>,
}

/// Drop-based append transaction: nested builders can fail or panic without
/// leaving partial nodes/module invocations. All graph mutations are append-only.
struct GraphAppendGuard<'a> {
    graph: &'a mut NeuralGraph,
    nodes: usize,
    modules: usize,
    multi_modules: usize,
    module_order: usize,
    committed: bool,
}

impl Drop for GraphAppendGuard<'_> {
    fn drop(&mut self) {
        if !self.committed {
            self.graph.nodes.truncate(self.nodes);
            self.graph.modules.truncate(self.modules);
            self.graph.multi_modules.truncate(self.multi_modules);
            self.graph.module_order.truncate(self.module_order);
        }
    }
}

impl NeuralGraph {
    fn transaction<T>(
        &mut self,
        build: impl FnOnce(&mut NeuralGraph) -> Result<T, NeuralError>,
    ) -> Result<T, NeuralError> {
        let mut guard = GraphAppendGuard {
            nodes: self.nodes.len(),
            modules: self.modules.len(),
            multi_modules: self.multi_modules.len(),
            module_order: self.module_order.len(),
            graph: self,
            committed: false,
        };
        let result = build(&mut *guard.graph);
        guard.committed = result.is_ok();
        result
    }

    pub fn new(policy: FP32Policy) -> Self {
        Self {
            identity: NEXT_GRAPH_ID.fetch_add(1, Ordering::Relaxed),
            policy,
            nodes: Vec::new(),
            modules: Vec::new(),
            multi_modules: Vec::new(),
            module_order: Vec::new(),
        }
    }

    pub fn policy(&self) -> FP32Policy {
        self.policy
    }

    pub fn nodes(&self) -> &[Node] {
        &self.nodes
    }

    pub fn modules(&self) -> &[ModuleInvocation] {
        &self.modules
    }

    pub fn multi_modules(&self) -> &[MultiModuleInvocation] {
        &self.multi_modules
    }

    /// Iterate all module invocations in the order in which they were applied.
    /// This is the canonical hierarchy order for architecture tooling.
    pub fn module_instances(&self) -> impl Iterator<Item = ModuleInstanceRef<'_>> {
        self.module_order.iter().map(|key| match *key {
            ModuleInstanceKey::Single(index) => ModuleInstanceRef::Single(&self.modules[index]),
            ModuleInstanceKey::Multi(index) => ModuleInstanceRef::Multi(&self.multi_modules[index]),
        })
    }

    /// Dependency closure of graph roots, including declared module inputs even
    /// when a module body does not read every port directly. Artifact writers
    /// and proof planning use this one definition of semantic reachability.
    pub fn dependency_scope(&self, roots: &[NodeId]) -> Result<BTreeSet<usize>, NeuralError> {
        // A module declares dependencies beyond its body edges: even an unused
        // port remains part of its interface. Index them once for this walk
        // instead of scanning every module once per reachable IR node.
        // Multiple invocations can name the same output: preserve every
        // declaration by accumulating rather than overwriting input lists.
        let mut module_inputs: BTreeMap<usize, Vec<NodeId>> = BTreeMap::new();
        for module in self.module_instances() {
            for output in module.outputs() {
                module_inputs
                    .entry(output.index())
                    .or_default()
                    .extend_from_slice(module.inputs());
            }
        }
        let mut used = BTreeSet::new();
        let mut pending = roots.to_vec();
        while let Some(id) = pending.pop() {
            let node = self.node(id)?;
            if !used.insert(id.index()) {
                continue;
            }
            pending.extend(node.inputs.iter().copied());
            if let Some(inputs) = module_inputs.get(&id.index()) {
                pending.extend(inputs.iter().copied());
            }
        }
        Ok(used)
    }

    pub fn node(&self, id: NodeId) -> Result<&Node, NeuralError> {
        if id.graph != self.identity {
            return Err(NeuralError::InvalidNode);
        }
        self.nodes.get(id.index).ok_or(NeuralError::InvalidNode)
    }

    /// Explicit contiguous storage/alias contract for this IR value.
    pub fn storage(&self, id: NodeId) -> Result<NodeStorage, NeuralError> {
        let node = self.node(id)?;
        let strides = node.shape.row_major_strides();
        Ok(match node.operation {
            Operation::Reshape(_) => NodeStorage::Alias {
                source: node.inputs[0],
                strides,
            },
            _ => NodeStorage::OwnedContiguous { strides },
        })
    }

    /// Resolve a zero-copy alias chain to the value that owns its allocation.
    pub fn storage_root(&self, mut id: NodeId) -> Result<NodeId, NeuralError> {
        loop {
            match self.storage(id)? {
                NodeStorage::OwnedContiguous { .. } => return Ok(id),
                NodeStorage::Alias { source, .. } => id = source,
            }
        }
    }

    pub fn aliases(&self, left: NodeId, right: NodeId) -> Result<bool, NeuralError> {
        Ok(self.storage_root(left)? == self.storage_root(right)?)
    }

    /// Declare a symbolic input and its caller-supplied domain assumption.
    /// The assumption must be checked for actual values before execution.
    pub fn input(&mut self, shape: Shape, domain: Domain) -> NodeId {
        let id = NodeId {
            graph: self.identity,
            index: self.nodes.len(),
        };
        self.nodes.push(Node {
            id,
            operation: Operation::Input,
            inputs: Vec::new(),
            shape: shape.clone(),
            dtype: DType::F32,
            domain,
            contract: MathContract::new(Vec::new(), PortContract::new(shape, domain)),
            semantics: OperationSemantics {
                ideal: Operation::Input,
                fp32: self.policy,
                gpu: GpuSemantics::NotLowered,
            },
        });
        id
    }

    /// Append an operation only after checking arity, shape, source and domain.
    pub fn apply(&mut self, op: Operation, inputs: &[NodeId]) -> Result<NodeId, NeuralError> {
        if matches!(op, Operation::Input) {
            return Err(NeuralError::InputCannotBeApplied);
        }
        if inputs.len() != op.arity() {
            return Err(NeuralError::WrongArity {
                operation: op.name(),
                expected: op.arity(),
                actual: inputs.len(),
            });
        }
        let source_nodes = inputs
            .iter()
            .map(|&id| self.node(id))
            .collect::<Result<Vec<_>, _>>()?;
        let shapes = source_nodes
            .iter()
            .map(|n| n.shape.clone())
            .collect::<Vec<_>>();
        let domains = source_nodes.iter().map(|n| n.domain).collect::<Vec<_>>();
        let dtypes = source_nodes.iter().map(|n| n.dtype).collect::<Vec<_>>();
        let shape = op.infer_shape(&shapes)?;
        let dtype = op.infer_dtype(&dtypes)?;
        if let Operation::Take { axis } = &op {
            let axis = *axis;
            let index_node = source_nodes[1];
            let upper_bound = match index_node.operation {
                Operation::ArgMax {
                    axis: source_axis, ..
                } => {
                    let argmax_input = self.node(index_node.inputs[0])?;
                    argmax_input.shape.dims()[source_axis]
                }
                _ => {
                    return Err(NeuralError::IndexRangeUnknown {
                        node: index_node.id.index(),
                    });
                }
            };
            let extent = source_nodes[0].shape.dims()[axis];
            if upper_bound > extent {
                return Err(NeuralError::IndexRangeExceedsAxis {
                    upper_bound,
                    axis,
                    extent,
                });
            }
        }
        let required = op.required_domain();
        for &actual in &domains {
            if !actual.satisfies(required) {
                return Err(NeuralError::DomainNotEstablished { required, actual });
            }
        }
        let contract = MathContract::new(
            shapes
                .into_iter()
                .zip(dtypes)
                .map(|(shape, dtype)| PortContract::typed(shape, dtype, required))
                .collect(),
            PortContract::typed(shape.clone(), dtype, op.infer_domain(&domains)),
        );
        let id = NodeId {
            graph: self.identity,
            index: self.nodes.len(),
        };
        self.nodes.push(Node {
            id,
            operation: op.clone(),
            inputs: inputs.to_vec(),
            shape,
            dtype,
            domain: contract.ensures.domain,
            contract,
            semantics: OperationSemantics {
                ideal: op,
                fp32: self.policy,
                gpu: GpuSemantics::NotLowered,
            },
        });
        Ok(id)
    }

    /// Sum one tensor axis in row-major order. Reductions are not implicitly
    /// reassociated: both the host reference and ideal Lean semantics fold left.
    pub fn reduce_sum(&mut self, input: NodeId, axis: usize) -> Result<NodeId, NeuralError> {
        self.apply(Operation::ReduceSum { axis }, &[input])
    }

    pub fn reduce_max(&mut self, input: NodeId, axis: usize) -> Result<NodeId, NeuralError> {
        self.apply(Operation::ReduceMax { axis }, &[input])
    }

    pub fn broadcast_to(&mut self, input: NodeId, shape: Shape) -> Result<NodeId, NeuralError> {
        self.apply(Operation::BroadcastTo(shape), &[input])
    }

    /// Elementwise subtraction defined as a versioned pointwise AST.
    pub fn sub(&mut self, a: NodeId, b: NodeId) -> Result<NodeId, NeuralError> {
        let spec = PointwiseSpec::new(
            "verineural.sub",
            "1",
            2,
            PointwiseExpr::input(0).sub(PointwiseExpr::input(1)),
        )?;
        spec.apply(self, &[a, b])
    }

    /// Elementwise division: IEEE f32 host reference, ideal-Int proof unsupported.
    pub fn div(&mut self, a: NodeId, b: NodeId) -> Result<NodeId, NeuralError> {
        let spec = PointwiseSpec::new(
            "verineural.div",
            "1",
            2,
            PointwiseExpr::input(0).div(PointwiseExpr::input(1)),
        )?;
        spec.apply(self, &[a, b])
    }

    /// Elementwise natural exponential: experimental GPU lowering, proof unsupported.
    pub fn exp(&mut self, input: NodeId) -> Result<NodeId, NeuralError> {
        let spec = PointwiseSpec::new("verineural.exp", "1", 1, PointwiseExpr::input(0).exp())?;
        spec.apply(self, &[input])
    }

    /// IEEE-style sqrt on any binary32 input, including NaN for negative inputs.
    /// Unlike the contract-restricted Sqrt node, this pointwise primitive
    /// accepts unrestricted inputs and is not a mathematical proof of positivity.
    pub fn sqrt_ieee(&mut self, input: NodeId) -> Result<NodeId, NeuralError> {
        let spec = PointwiseSpec::new("verineural.sqrt", "1", 1, PointwiseExpr::input(0).sqrt())?;
        spec.apply(self, &[input])
    }

    pub fn permute(&mut self, input: NodeId, axes: &[usize]) -> Result<NodeId, NeuralError> {
        self.apply(
            Operation::Permute {
                axes: axes.to_vec(),
            },
            &[input],
        )
    }

    pub fn reverse_axis(&mut self, input: NodeId, axis: usize) -> Result<NodeId, NeuralError> {
        self.apply(Operation::ReverseAxis { axis }, &[input])
    }

    /// Static contiguous slice of one axis. Bounds are part of Semantic IR,
    /// so host/proof/backends cannot silently disagree about the interval.
    pub fn slice_axis(
        &mut self,
        input: NodeId,
        axis: usize,
        start: usize,
        len: usize,
    ) -> Result<NodeId, NeuralError> {
        self.apply(Operation::SliceAxis { axis, start, len }, &[input])
    }

    /// Concatenate one or more tensors by lowering the public variadic API to
    /// the binary semantic primitive. This keeps the core operation minimal.
    pub fn concat(&mut self, axis: usize, inputs: &[NodeId]) -> Result<NodeId, NeuralError> {
        let (&first, rest) = inputs.split_first().ok_or(NeuralError::EmptyConcat)?;
        let first_node = self.node(first)?;
        if axis >= first_node.shape.rank() {
            return Err(NeuralError::InvalidAxis {
                axis,
                rank: first_node.shape.rank(),
            });
        }
        let mut current = first;
        for &next in rest {
            current = self.apply(Operation::Concat { axis }, &[current, next])?;
        }
        Ok(current)
    }

    pub fn argmax(
        &mut self,
        input: NodeId,
        axis: usize,
        tie_break: ArgMaxTieBreak,
    ) -> Result<NodeId, NeuralError> {
        self.apply(Operation::ArgMax { axis, tie_break }, &[input])
    }

    pub fn take(
        &mut self,
        data: NodeId,
        index: NodeId,
        axis: usize,
    ) -> Result<NodeId, NeuralError> {
        self.apply(Operation::Take { axis }, &[data, index])
    }

    pub fn add(&mut self, a: NodeId, b: NodeId) -> Result<NodeId, NeuralError> {
        self.apply(Operation::Add, &[a, b])
    }

    pub fn mul(&mut self, a: NodeId, b: NodeId) -> Result<NodeId, NeuralError> {
        self.apply(Operation::Mul, &[a, b])
    }

    pub fn matmul(&mut self, a: NodeId, b: NodeId) -> Result<NodeId, NeuralError> {
        self.apply(Operation::MatMul, &[a, b])
    }

    /// Add a length-N bias to each row of an MxN tensor (no arbitrary broadcast).
    pub fn bias_add(&mut self, matrix: NodeId, bias: NodeId) -> Result<NodeId, NeuralError> {
        self.apply(Operation::BiasAdd, &[matrix, bias])
    }

    pub fn relu(&mut self, a: NodeId) -> Result<NodeId, NeuralError> {
        self.apply(Operation::Relu, &[a])
    }

    /// Pointwise 0/1 mask for the strict positive branch (NaN takes false branch).
    pub fn positive_mask(&mut self, a: NodeId) -> Result<NodeId, NeuralError> {
        self.apply(Operation::PositiveMask, &[a])
    }

    /// Elementwise conditional selection, no implicit broadcast or arithmetic.
    pub fn select_positive(
        &mut self,
        mask: NodeId,
        yes: NodeId,
        no: NodeId,
    ) -> Result<NodeId, NeuralError> {
        self.apply(Operation::SelectPositive, &[mask, yes, no])
    }

    pub fn sqrt(&mut self, a: NodeId) -> Result<NodeId, NeuralError> {
        self.apply(Operation::Sqrt, &[a])
    }

    pub fn reshape(&mut self, a: NodeId, shape: Shape) -> Result<NodeId, NeuralError> {
        self.apply(Operation::Reshape(shape), &[a])
    }

    /// Check every edge crossing a module boundary, including nested invocations.
    /// An output must be owned by this invocation, not borrowed from its caller.
    fn validate_body(
        &self,
        body_start: usize,
        modules_start: usize,
        multi_start: usize,
        allowed: &[NodeId],
        outputs: &[NodeId],
        name: &'static str,
    ) -> Result<(), NeuralError> {
        if self.nodes.len() == body_start || outputs.is_empty() {
            return Err(NeuralError::ContractViolation {
                module: name,
                detail: "empty body or outputs",
            });
        }
        for &output in outputs {
            self.node(output)?;
            if output.index < body_start {
                return Err(NeuralError::ContractViolation {
                    module: name,
                    detail: "output not owned by module",
                });
            }
        }
        let authorized = |id: NodeId| id.index >= body_start || allowed.contains(&id);
        for node in &self.nodes[body_start..] {
            if matches!(node.operation, Operation::Input) {
                return Err(NeuralError::ContractViolation {
                    module: name,
                    detail: "module declared a hidden source input",
                });
            }
            if node.inputs.iter().any(|&id| !authorized(id)) {
                return Err(NeuralError::ContractViolation {
                    module: name,
                    detail: "undeclared external capture",
                });
            }
        }
        for nested in &self.modules[modules_start..] {
            if nested.inputs.iter().any(|&id| !authorized(id)) {
                return Err(NeuralError::ContractViolation {
                    module: name,
                    detail: "nested module captured undeclared input",
                });
            }
        }
        for nested in &self.multi_modules[multi_start..] {
            if nested.inputs.iter().any(|&id| !authorized(id)) {
                return Err(NeuralError::ContractViolation {
                    module: name,
                    detail: "nested multi-module captured undeclared input",
                });
            }
        }
        Ok(())
    }

    /// Compose an ad-hoc single-output module without defining a Rust type.
    /// Existing `NeuralModule` implementations delegate to this same path.
    pub fn compose<F>(
        &mut self,
        name: &'static str,
        semantic_version: &'static str,
        contract: &MathContract,
        inputs: &[NodeId],
        build: F,
    ) -> Result<NodeId, NeuralError>
    where
        F: FnOnce(&mut NeuralGraph, &[NodeId]) -> Result<NodeId, NeuralError>,
    {
        self.apply_module_with(name, semantic_version, contract, inputs, build)
    }

    /// Validate the interface, then append transactionally. Failed bodies (or
    /// caught panics) roll back all added nodes and nested module metadata.
    pub fn apply_module<M: NeuralModule>(
        &mut self,
        module: &M,
        inputs: &[NodeId],
    ) -> Result<NodeId, NeuralError> {
        self.apply_module_with(
            module.name(),
            module.semantic_version(),
            module.contract(),
            inputs,
            |graph, inputs| module.build(graph, inputs),
        )
    }

    fn apply_module_with<F>(
        &mut self,
        name: &'static str,
        semantic_version: &'static str,
        contract: &MathContract,
        inputs: &[NodeId],
        build: F,
    ) -> Result<NodeId, NeuralError>
    where
        F: FnOnce(&mut NeuralGraph, &[NodeId]) -> Result<NodeId, NeuralError>,
    {
        if inputs.len() != contract.requires.len() {
            return Err(NeuralError::ContractViolation {
                module: name,
                detail: "incorrect number of inputs",
            });
        }
        for (&id, required) in inputs.iter().zip(&contract.requires) {
            let actual = self.node(id)?;
            if actual.shape != required.shape {
                return Err(NeuralError::ShapeMismatch {
                    expected: required.shape.clone(),
                    actual: actual.shape.clone(),
                });
            }
            if actual.dtype != required.dtype {
                return Err(NeuralError::DTypeMismatch {
                    operation: "module_input",
                    expected: required.dtype,
                    actual: actual.dtype,
                });
            }
            if !actual.domain.satisfies(required.domain) {
                return Err(NeuralError::DomainNotEstablished {
                    required: required.domain,
                    actual: actual.domain,
                });
            }
        }

        let body_start = self.nodes.len();
        let module_start = self.modules.len();
        let multi_start = self.multi_modules.len();
        self.transaction(|candidate| {
            let output = build(candidate, inputs)?;
            candidate.validate_body(
                body_start,
                module_start,
                multi_start,
                inputs,
                &[output],
                name,
            )?;
            let actual = candidate.node(output)?;
            if actual.shape != contract.ensures.shape {
                return Err(NeuralError::ShapeMismatch {
                    expected: contract.ensures.shape.clone(),
                    actual: actual.shape.clone(),
                });
            }
            if actual.dtype != contract.ensures.dtype {
                return Err(NeuralError::DTypeMismatch {
                    operation: "module_output",
                    expected: contract.ensures.dtype,
                    actual: actual.dtype,
                });
            }
            if !actual.domain.satisfies(contract.ensures.domain) {
                return Err(NeuralError::DomainNotEstablished {
                    required: contract.ensures.domain,
                    actual: actual.domain,
                });
            }
            let body_end = candidate.nodes.len();
            let module_index = candidate.modules.len();
            candidate.modules.push(ModuleInvocation {
                name,
                inputs: inputs.to_vec(),
                body_start,
                body_end,
                output,
                contract: contract.clone(),
                semantic_version,
            });
            candidate
                .module_order
                .push(ModuleInstanceKey::Single(module_index));
            Ok(output)
        })
    }

    /// Structural composition without a caller-written duplicate MathContract.
    /// Only shapes and conservative domains are inferred, never mathematical
    /// claims or Lean certification. Failed bodies leave this graph unchanged.
    pub fn compose_inferred<F>(
        &mut self,
        name: &'static str,
        semantic_version: &'static str,
        inputs: &[NodeId],
        build: F,
    ) -> Result<NodeId, NeuralError>
    where
        F: FnOnce(&mut NeuralGraph, &[NodeId]) -> Result<NodeId, NeuralError>,
    {
        let requires = inputs
            .iter()
            .map(|&id| {
                let node = self.node(id)?;
                Ok(PortContract::typed(
                    node.shape.clone(),
                    node.dtype,
                    node.domain,
                ))
            })
            .collect::<Result<Vec<_>, NeuralError>>()?;
        let body_start = self.nodes.len();
        let module_start = self.modules.len();
        let multi_start = self.multi_modules.len();
        self.transaction(|candidate| {
            let output = build(candidate, inputs)?;
            candidate.validate_body(
                body_start,
                module_start,
                multi_start,
                inputs,
                &[output],
                name,
            )?;
            let result = candidate.node(output)?;
            let contract = MathContract::new(
                requires,
                PortContract::typed(result.shape.clone(), result.dtype, result.domain),
            );
            let module_index = candidate.modules.len();
            let body_end = candidate.nodes.len();
            candidate.modules.push(ModuleInvocation {
                name,
                inputs: inputs.to_vec(),
                body_start,
                body_end,
                output,
                contract,
                semantic_version,
            });
            candidate
                .module_order
                .push(ModuleInstanceKey::Single(module_index));
            Ok(output)
        })
    }

    /// Infer an atomic named multi-output block from its semantic IR.
    /// Input names and output names are part of the structural contract;
    /// mathematical postconditions still require explicit proof obligations.
    pub fn compose_multi_inferred<F>(
        &mut self,
        name: &'static str,
        semantic_version: &'static str,
        inputs: &[(&'static str, NodeId)],
        output_names: &[&'static str],
        build: F,
    ) -> Result<Vec<NodeId>, NeuralError>
    where
        F: FnOnce(&mut NeuralGraph, &[NodeId]) -> Result<Vec<NodeId>, NeuralError>,
    {
        if output_names.is_empty() {
            return Err(NeuralError::ContractViolation {
                module: name,
                detail: "multi-output block requires at least one output",
            });
        }
        for names in [
            inputs.iter().map(|(label, _)| *label).collect::<Vec<_>>(),
            output_names.to_vec(),
        ] {
            let mut seen = BTreeSet::new();
            if names
                .iter()
                .any(|label| label.is_empty() || !seen.insert(*label))
            {
                return Err(NeuralError::ContractViolation {
                    module: name,
                    detail: "empty or duplicate inferred multi-port name",
                });
            }
        }
        let input_ids: Vec<_> = inputs.iter().map(|(_, node)| *node).collect();
        let requires = inputs
            .iter()
            .map(|(label, node)| {
                let value = self.node(*node)?;
                Ok(NamedPortContract::new(
                    label,
                    PortContract::typed(value.shape.clone(), value.dtype, value.domain),
                ))
            })
            .collect::<Result<Vec<_>, NeuralError>>()?;
        let body_start = self.nodes.len();
        let module_start = self.modules.len();
        let multi_start = self.multi_modules.len();
        self.transaction(|candidate| {
            let outputs = build(candidate, &input_ids)?;
            if outputs.len() != output_names.len() {
                return Err(NeuralError::ContractViolation {
                    module: name,
                    detail: "incorrect inferred multi-output result count",
                });
            }
            candidate.validate_body(
                body_start,
                module_start,
                multi_start,
                &input_ids,
                &outputs,
                name,
            )?;
            if outputs
                .iter()
                .map(|id| id.index())
                .collect::<BTreeSet<_>>()
                .len()
                != outputs.len()
            {
                return Err(NeuralError::ContractViolation {
                    module: name,
                    detail: "duplicate inferred multi-output identity",
                });
            }
            let ensures = outputs
                .iter()
                .zip(output_names)
                .map(|(&id, &label)| {
                    let value = candidate.node(id)?;
                    Ok(NamedPortContract::new(
                        label,
                        PortContract::typed(value.shape.clone(), value.dtype, value.domain),
                    ))
                })
                .collect::<Result<Vec<_>, NeuralError>>()?;
            let module_index = candidate.multi_modules.len();
            candidate.multi_modules.push(MultiModuleInvocation {
                name,
                semantic_version,
                inputs: input_ids,
                body_start,
                body_end: candidate.nodes.len(),
                outputs: outputs.clone(),
                contract: MultiOutputContract::new(requires, ensures),
            });
            candidate
                .module_order
                .push(ModuleInstanceKey::Multi(module_index));
            Ok(outputs)
        })
    }

    /// Unroll a statically bounded state transition, without introducing a
    /// built-in recurrent architecture or an implicit GPU execution mode.
    /// The transition's interface must be exactly:
    /// inputs: `state`, `input`; outputs: `next_state`, `output`.
    /// Step instances use `apply_multi_module` with the same shape/domain
    /// checks and named proof obligations as any other consumer module.
    ///
    /// All steps are committed atomically, including when a later input
    /// violates its contract. The final state and every readout are explicit
    /// IR nodes usable by Lean generation and CUDA Graph lowering.
    pub fn scan_fixed<M: MultiOutputModule>(
        &mut self,
        transition: &M,
        initial_state: NodeId,
        inputs: &[NodeId],
    ) -> Result<FixedScan, NeuralError> {
        let contract = transition.contract();
        if contract.inputs.len() != 2
            || contract.outputs.len() != 2
            || contract.inputs[0].name != "state"
            || contract.inputs[1].name != "input"
            || contract.outputs[0].name != "next_state"
            || contract.outputs[1].name != "output"
        {
            return Err(NeuralError::ContractViolation {
                module: transition.name(),
                detail: "fixed scan requires state/input and next_state/output ports",
            });
        }
        if inputs.is_empty() {
            return Err(NeuralError::ContractViolation {
                module: transition.name(),
                detail: "fixed scan requires at least one step",
            });
        }
        if contract.inputs[0].port.shape != contract.outputs[0].port.shape
            || contract.inputs[0].port.dtype != contract.outputs[0].port.dtype
            || !contract.outputs[0]
                .port
                .domain
                .satisfies(contract.inputs[0].port.domain)
        {
            return Err(NeuralError::ContractViolation {
                module: transition.name(),
                detail: "next_state does not satisfy the next step's state port",
            });
        }
        self.node(initial_state)?;
        for &input in inputs {
            self.node(input)?;
        }
        self.transaction(|candidate| {
            let mut states = vec![initial_state];
            let mut outputs = Vec::with_capacity(inputs.len());
            let mut module_indices = Vec::with_capacity(inputs.len());
            for &input in inputs {
                let state = *states.last().expect("initialized with initial_state");
                let result = candidate.apply_multi_module(transition, &[state, input])?;
                module_indices.push(candidate.multi_modules.len() - 1);
                states.push(result[0]);
                outputs.push(result[1]);
            }
            Ok(FixedScan {
                states,
                outputs,
                module_indices,
            })
        })
    }

    /// Compose an ad-hoc multi-output module without defining a Rust type.
    pub fn compose_multi<F>(
        &mut self,
        name: &'static str,
        semantic_version: &'static str,
        contract: &MultiOutputContract,
        inputs: &[NodeId],
        build: F,
    ) -> Result<Vec<NodeId>, NeuralError>
    where
        F: FnOnce(&mut NeuralGraph, &[NodeId]) -> Result<Vec<NodeId>, NeuralError>,
    {
        self.apply_multi_module_with(name, semantic_version, contract, inputs, build)
    }

    /// Multi-output module invocation is atomic; each returned port has its own
    /// structural contract. Formal proof obligations remain per output.
    pub fn apply_multi_module<M: MultiOutputModule>(
        &mut self,
        module: &M,
        inputs: &[NodeId],
    ) -> Result<Vec<NodeId>, NeuralError> {
        self.apply_multi_module_with(
            module.name(),
            module.semantic_version(),
            module.contract(),
            inputs,
            |graph, inputs| module.build(graph, inputs),
        )
    }

    fn apply_multi_module_with<F>(
        &mut self,
        name: &'static str,
        semantic_version: &'static str,
        contract: &MultiOutputContract,
        inputs: &[NodeId],
        build: F,
    ) -> Result<Vec<NodeId>, NeuralError>
    where
        F: FnOnce(&mut NeuralGraph, &[NodeId]) -> Result<Vec<NodeId>, NeuralError>,
    {
        if inputs.len() != contract.inputs.len() || contract.outputs.is_empty() {
            return Err(NeuralError::ContractViolation {
                module: name,
                detail: "incorrect multi-output arity",
            });
        }
        for ports in [&contract.inputs, &contract.outputs] {
            let mut names = std::collections::BTreeSet::new();
            for port in ports {
                if port.name.is_empty() || !names.insert(port.name) {
                    return Err(NeuralError::ContractViolation {
                        module: name,
                        detail: "empty or duplicated named port",
                    });
                }
            }
        }
        if contract.inputs.iter().any(|port| !port.claims.is_empty()) {
            return Err(NeuralError::ContractViolation {
                module: name,
                detail: "input port claims are unsupported",
            });
        }
        for (&input, port) in inputs.iter().zip(&contract.inputs) {
            let node = self.node(input)?;
            if node.shape != port.port.shape {
                return Err(NeuralError::ShapeMismatch {
                    expected: port.port.shape.clone(),
                    actual: node.shape.clone(),
                });
            }
            if node.dtype != port.port.dtype {
                return Err(NeuralError::DTypeMismatch {
                    operation: "multi_module_input",
                    expected: port.port.dtype,
                    actual: node.dtype,
                });
            }
            if !node.domain.satisfies(port.port.domain) {
                return Err(NeuralError::DomainNotEstablished {
                    required: port.port.domain,
                    actual: node.domain,
                });
            }
        }
        let body_start = self.nodes.len();
        let module_start = self.modules.len();
        let multi_start = self.multi_modules.len();
        self.transaction(|candidate| {
            let outputs = build(candidate, inputs)?;
            if outputs.len() != contract.outputs.len() {
                return Err(NeuralError::ContractViolation {
                    module: name,
                    detail: "incorrect multi-output result count",
                });
            }
            candidate.validate_body(
                body_start,
                module_start,
                multi_start,
                inputs,
                &outputs,
                name,
            )?;
            if outputs
                .iter()
                .map(|id| id.index())
                .collect::<std::collections::BTreeSet<_>>()
                .len()
                != outputs.len()
            {
                return Err(NeuralError::ContractViolation {
                    module: name,
                    detail: "duplicate output identity",
                });
            }
            for (&id, port) in outputs.iter().zip(&contract.outputs) {
                let node = candidate.node(id)?;
                if node.shape != port.port.shape {
                    return Err(NeuralError::ShapeMismatch {
                        expected: port.port.shape.clone(),
                        actual: node.shape.clone(),
                    });
                }
                if node.dtype != port.port.dtype {
                    return Err(NeuralError::DTypeMismatch {
                        operation: "multi_module_output",
                        expected: port.port.dtype,
                        actual: node.dtype,
                    });
                }
                if !node.domain.satisfies(port.port.domain) {
                    return Err(NeuralError::DomainNotEstablished {
                        required: port.port.domain,
                        actual: node.domain,
                    });
                }
            }
            let module_index = candidate.multi_modules.len();
            candidate.multi_modules.push(MultiModuleInvocation {
                name,
                semantic_version,
                inputs: inputs.to_vec(),
                body_start,
                body_end: candidate.nodes.len(),
                outputs: outputs.clone(),
                contract: contract.clone(),
            });
            candidate
                .module_order
                .push(ModuleInstanceKey::Multi(module_index));
            Ok(outputs)
        })
    }
}

impl Default for NeuralGraph {
    fn default() -> Self {
        Self::new(FP32Policy::strict())
    }
}

#[cfg(test)]
mod graph_append_transaction_tests {
    use super::*;

    #[test]
    fn scope_indexes_all_module_outputs_and_unused_declared_ports() {
        let mut graph = NeuralGraph::default();
        let x = graph.input(Shape::new(vec![2]).unwrap(), Domain::Finite);
        let unused = graph.input(Shape::new(vec![2]).unwrap(), Domain::Finite);
        let unrelated = graph.input(Shape::new(vec![2]).unwrap(), Domain::Finite);
        let outputs = graph
            .compose_multi_inferred(
                "branch",
                "1",
                &[("x", x), ("unused", unused)],
                &["one", "two"],
                |g, values| {
                    let one = g.relu(values[0])?;
                    let two = g.mul(one, values[0])?;
                    Ok(vec![one, two])
                },
            )
            .unwrap();
        let outer = graph
            .compose_inferred("outer", "1", &[outputs[1]], |g, values| g.relu(values[0]))
            .unwrap();
        // The output of a declared module pulls *all* its named inputs,
        // even when its body doesn't use one of them.
        for &root in &[outputs[0], outputs[1], outer] {
            let scope = graph.dependency_scope(&[root]).unwrap();
            assert!(scope.contains(&x.index()));
            assert!(scope.contains(&unused.index()));
            assert!(!scope.contains(&unrelated.index()));
        }
        // Every selected root still validates its graph identity.
        let foreign = NeuralGraph::default().input(Shape::new(vec![2]).unwrap(), Domain::Finite);
        assert!(matches!(
            graph.dependency_scope(&[foreign]),
            Err(NeuralError::InvalidNode)
        ));
    }

    #[test]
    fn indexed_dependency_scope_matches_reference_for_nested_and_shared_blocks() {
        let mut graph = NeuralGraph::default();
        let a = graph.input(Shape::new(vec![2]).unwrap(), Domain::Finite);
        let b = graph.input(Shape::new(vec![2]).unwrap(), Domain::Finite);
        let mut head = a;
        for _ in 0..48 {
            let ports = graph
                .compose_multi_inferred(
                    "pair",
                    "1",
                    &[("head", head), ("extra", b)],
                    &["next", "diagnostic"],
                    |g, xs| {
                        let next = g.add(xs[0], xs[1])?;
                        let diag = g.relu(next)?;
                        Ok(vec![next, diag])
                    },
                )
                .unwrap();
            head = ports[0];
        }
        let roots = [head];
        let indexed = graph.dependency_scope(&roots).unwrap();
        let mut old = BTreeSet::new();
        let mut pending = roots.to_vec();
        while let Some(id) = pending.pop() {
            let node = graph.node(id).unwrap();
            if !old.insert(id.index()) {
                continue;
            }
            pending.extend(node.inputs.iter().copied());
            for module in graph.module_instances() {
                if module.contains_output(id) {
                    pending.extend(module.inputs().iter().copied());
                }
            }
        }
        assert_eq!(indexed, old);
        assert!(indexed.contains(&a.index()));
        assert!(indexed.contains(&b.index()));
    }

    #[test]
    fn failed_parent_rolls_back_successful_nested_multi_module() {
        let mut graph = NeuralGraph::default();
        let source = graph.input(Shape::new(vec![2]).unwrap(), Domain::Finite);
        let original_nodes = graph.nodes().len();
        let original_modules = graph.modules().len();
        let original_multi = graph.multi_modules().len();
        let original_order = graph.module_instances().count();
        let failure = graph.compose_inferred("parent", "1", &[source], |candidate, inputs| {
            let results = candidate.compose_multi_inferred(
                "child",
                "1",
                &[("value", inputs[0])],
                &["a", "b"],
                |nested, ports| {
                    let first = nested.relu(ports[0])?;
                    let second = nested.add(first, ports[0])?;
                    Ok(vec![first, second])
                },
            )?;
            let _ = candidate.mul(results[0], results[1])?;
            Err(NeuralError::InvalidNode)
        });
        assert!(matches!(failure, Err(NeuralError::InvalidNode)));
        assert_eq!(graph.nodes().len(), original_nodes);
        assert_eq!(graph.modules().len(), original_modules);
        assert_eq!(graph.multi_modules().len(), original_multi);
        assert_eq!(graph.module_instances().count(), original_order);
        // Failed transactions may reuse their former numeric positions.
        let next = graph.relu(source).unwrap();
        assert_eq!(next.index(), original_nodes);
    }

    #[test]
    fn caught_panic_rolls_back_all_appended_graph_data() {
        let mut graph = NeuralGraph::default();
        let source = graph.input(Shape::new(vec![2]).unwrap(), Domain::Finite);
        let old_len = graph.nodes().len();
        let panic = std::panic::catch_unwind(std::panic::AssertUnwindSafe(|| {
            let _ = graph.compose_inferred("panic", "1", &[source], |candidate, inputs| {
                let _ = candidate.relu(inputs[0])?;
                panic!("intentional append transaction rollback test");
            });
        }));
        assert!(panic.is_err());
        assert_eq!(graph.nodes().len(), old_len);
        assert!(graph.modules().is_empty());
        assert!(graph.multi_modules().is_empty());
        assert_eq!(graph.module_instances().count(), 0);
        assert!(graph.relu(source).is_ok());
    }
}

FILE	crates/verineural/src/lib.rs
//! VeriNeural: an importable Rust API and Semantic Neural IR.
//!
//! Stage 3 adds Lean 4 proof generation and checker integration for a bounded
//! ideal-integer fragment (Add, Mul, Relu, Reshape). Shape, pointwise semantics
//! and compositional nonnegativity are verified under explicit input hypotheses.
//! Stage 4 adds experimental LLVM NVPTX + CUDA Driver execution on NVIDIA GPUs.
//! Stage 5 emits an integrity-checked evidence bundle with separate assurance levels.
//! Stage 6 adds MatMul, row-wise bias and composable Dense/Residual FFN blocks.
//! Stage 7 begins controllable CUDA launches and experimental local Relu fusion,
//! with ideal-Int Lean rewrite lemmas, not certified FP32/PTX equivalence.
//! Stage 8 adds exact-integer range proofs plus concrete dyadic binary32
//! RNE traces with Lean-composed error bounds for Add/Mul/MatMul/BiasAdd/Relu/
//! Reshape, including explicit separate multiply/add MatMul reductions. Reusable
//! range/error contracts summarize arbitrary bounded dyadic inputs and module
//! boundaries. Generated whole-module theorems compose each supported
//! ModuleInvocation elementwise, including direct nested-module theorem reuse.
//! Architecture-level range theorems compose the reachable top-level module DAG,
//! including fork/fan-in boundaries, under the same formal RNE target relation.
//! Multi-output reusable proof definitions use one normalized right-nested
//! product for all output tensors and a single shared conjunction theorem,
//! with per-port, per-instance applications and independently checked premises.
//! This ideal-Int profile currently covers explicit Nonnegative claims only.
//!
//! An explicit global ideal-Int nonnegativity request groups compatible
//! top-level module invocations by normalized definition, proves each shared
//! definition once, checks concrete invocation premises separately, and builds
//! the architecture theorem from those applications. Nested module bodies are
//! normalized inside their enclosing definition in this profile; a general
//! typed theorem-dependency graph remains future work. This property is
//! separate from FP32/GPU guarantees.
//! Stage 8 ReLU threshold decisions use conditional per-node error margins;
//! uncertain pre-activations remain indeterminate.
//! Strict FP32 NVPTX lowering uses explicit rounded PTX operations and
//! rejects unsupported contraction at the emitted PTX level. The LLVM/PTX/GPU
//! machine correspondence remains trusted rather than formally certified.
//! Per-kernel translation plans fail closed on inconsistent LLVM/PTX lowering;
//! structural validation is distinct from semantic proof or JIT/SASS assurance.

