FILE	labs/coupled-field-0.1.0/README.md
# CoupledField 0.1.0

Independent Stage 9 VeriNeural consumer. It is not a built-in network,
training pipeline, or verified CUDA/SASS implementation.

## Model and API

The architecture is declared in src/lib.rs with the public ModelBuilder API:

- Three named nonnegative input fields: x, y, z, each [1,4].
- Two named nonnegative, shared parameter fields: p, q, each [4].
- Seven nested semantic modules (four Boundary responses, two Coupled units,
  one CoupledField) using graph operations mul, bias_add, add and relu.
- Three model outputs: final, left and right. They refer to existing graph
  nodes; output registration adds no computation. Only final is executed by
  the legacy end-to-end Stage 9 runner.
- One explicit relational proof obligation, coupled_branch_lower_bound,
  relating left and final. It is not inferred solely from ReLU of final.

The branch outputs are consumed by Model::plan for shared multi-output NVPTX
planning. The runnable GPU evidence path still exercises the single final
output with baseline/fused CUDA Graph, avoiding any silent expansion of the
execution guarantees.

## Local acceptance (Nix devShell, workspace root)

    git pull --ff-only
    task check
    task test
    task clippy
    task lab-stage9
    task verify-lab-stage9

Certification artifacts (generated Lean, DOT/PNG, LLVM/PTX, bit-level
inputs/outputs, manifests) are **not tracked in Git**. On a fresh checkout
run `task lab-stage9` before `task verify-lab-stage9`. This avoids
shipping stale evidence and dangling legacy `auto-build/` symlinks.
Published source files, tests and proof obligations remain versioned.

The lab runs the same independent checked i64 oracle for the concrete
[4,10,8,12] values, kernel-checks both architecture_global_nonnegative
and architecture_property_coupled_branch_lower_bound via Lean, checks
baseline/fused CUDA Graph results, validates LLVM/PTX translation evidence,
and writes an 18-file integrity manifest.

The structural contracts are now inferred instead of handwritten. Therefore
all earlier generated Semantic IR, DOT, PNG, Lean, PTX and SHA256SUMS files
must be rebuilt by task lab-stage9 and validated by task verify-lab-stage9.
Do not update the manifest or any proof artifact manually.

Lean establishes properties of the ideal integer semantics under declared
source assumptions. GPU bitwise agreement is a finite concrete probe.
CUDA JIT/SASS and general FP32 equivalence are not formally established.

FILE	labs/coupled-field-0.1.0/src/lib.rs
//! Independent Stage 9 research consumer: a coupled, two-level spatial field.
//! This is NOT a prescribed VeriNeural architecture, neural language model
//! or an implementation of training/state updates. It exercises nested module
//! boundaries, parameter sharing, fork/fan-in and a global ideal-Int theorem.

use std::error::Error;
use verineural::{
    ArchitectureMetadata, Domain, Model, ModelBuilder, ModelError, NeuralError, NeuralGraph,
    NodeId, Operation, Predicate, ProofGoal, ProofGoalKind, Shape, Tensor, ValueRef,
};

fn field() -> Shape {
    Shape::new(vec![1, 4]).expect("valid field shape")
}
fn channel() -> Shape {
    Shape::new(vec![4]).expect("valid channel shape")
}

/// Consumer-defined primitive: every GPU/Lean operation still comes from VeriNeural.
fn boundary_response(g: &mut NeuralGraph, inputs: &[NodeId]) -> Result<NodeId, NeuralError> {
    let product = g.mul(inputs[0], inputs[1])?;
    let biased = g.bias_add(product, inputs[2])?;
    g.relu(biased)
}

/// CoupledUnit(a,b,c,p,q) := Relu(Boundary(a,b,p) + Boundary(b,c,q)).
fn coupled_unit(g: &mut NeuralGraph, inputs: &[NodeId]) -> Result<NodeId, NeuralError> {
    let left = g.compose_inferred(
        "boundary_response",
        "1.0",
        &[inputs[0], inputs[1], inputs[3]],
        boundary_response,
    )?;
    let right = g.compose_inferred(
        "boundary_response",
        "1.0",
        &[inputs[1], inputs[2], inputs[4]],
        boundary_response,
    )?;
    let merged = g.add(left, right)?;
    g.relu(merged)
}

/// Rotate the fields; reuse the two shared parameter sources for both branches.
fn coupled_field(g: &mut NeuralGraph, inputs: &[NodeId]) -> Result<NodeId, NeuralError> {
    let left = g.compose_inferred("coupled_unit", "1.0", inputs, coupled_unit)?;
    let right = g.compose_inferred(
        "coupled_unit",
        "1.0",
        &[inputs[0], inputs[2], inputs[1], inputs[4], inputs[3]],
        coupled_unit,
    )?;
    let merged = g.add(left, right)?;
    g.relu(merged)
}

/// Named sources, outputs and independent Lean goals share one Semantic IR.
pub fn architecture() -> Result<Model, ModelError> {
    let mut m = ModelBuilder::new("coupled-field", "0.1.0");
    let x = m.input("x", [1, 4], Domain::NonNegativeFinite)?;
    let y = m.input("y", [1, 4], Domain::NonNegativeFinite)?;
    let z = m.input("z", [1, 4], Domain::NonNegativeFinite)?;
    let p = m.parameter("p", [4], Domain::NonNegativeFinite)?;
    let q = m.parameter("q", [4], Domain::NonNegativeFinite)?;
    let result = m.block("coupled_field", &[x, y, z, p, q], coupled_field)?;

    // Expose the two actual branches for multi-output planning, without
    // changing the existing single-root Stage 9 execution/evidence profile.
    let root = m.graph_mut().node(result)?;
    if !matches!(root.operation, Operation::Relu) {
        return Err(ModelError::Invalid("expected output ReLU".into()));
    }
    let merge_id = root.inputs[0];
    let merge = m.graph_mut().node(merge_id)?;
    if !matches!(merge.operation, Operation::Add) || merge.inputs.len() != 2 {
        return Err(ModelError::Invalid("expected two-branch Add".into()));
    }
    let left = merge.inputs[0];
    let right = merge.inputs[1];
    if !matches!(m.graph_mut().node(right)?.operation, Operation::Relu) {
        return Err(ModelError::Invalid("right branch must be a ReLU".into()));
    }
    m.output("final", result)?;
    m.output("left", left)?;
    m.output("right", right)?;
    m.proof_goal(ProofGoal {
        name: "coupled_branch_lower_bound".into(),
        output: result,
        kind: ProofGoalKind::Predicate(Predicate::pointwise_le(
            ValueRef::Node(left),
            ValueRef::Output,
        )),
    })?;
    m.finish()
}

/// Concrete parameters and values are tiny nonnegative integers and exactly
/// representable in binary32. All nonnegative facts used by Lean remain
/// explicit caller assumptions, verified for this particular input vector.
pub fn build() -> Result<Lab, Box<dyn Error>> {
    let model = architecture()?;
    let mut inputs = model.bind([
        ("x", Tensor::new(field(), vec![1., 2., 3., 4.])?),
        ("y", Tensor::new(field(), vec![2., 1., 0., 1.])?),
        ("z", Tensor::new(field(), vec![0., 1., 2., 1.])?),
        ("p", Tensor::new(channel(), vec![1., 0., 1., 0.])?),
        ("q", Tensor::new(channel(), vec![0., 2., 0., 1.])?),
    ])?;
    inputs.sort_by_key(|(id, _)| id.index());
    Ok(Lab { model, inputs })
}

pub struct Lab {
    pub model: Model,
    pub inputs: Vec<(NodeId, Tensor<f32>)>,
}

impl Lab {
    pub fn graph(&self) -> &NeuralGraph {
        self.model.graph()
    }

    pub fn output(&self) -> NodeId {
        self.model
            .output("final")
            .expect("architecture declares final")
    }

    pub fn source_nodes(&self) -> [NodeId; 5] {
        ["x", "y", "z", "p", "q"].map(|name| {
            self.model
                .source(name)
                .expect("architecture declares every source")
                .0
        })
    }

    pub fn metadata(&self) -> ArchitectureMetadata {
        self.model.metadata("architecture_global_nonnegative")
    }

    pub fn inputs_bits(&self) -> String {
        let roles = self.metadata().input_roles;
        self.inputs
            .iter()
            .map(|(id, t)| {
                format!(
                    "node={} role={} shape={:?} bits={}\n",
                    id.index(),
                    roles.get(&id.index()).expect("all source roles declared"),
                    t.shape().dims(),
                    t.values()
                        .iter()
                        .map(|x| format!("{:08x}", x.to_bits()))
                        .collect::<Vec<_>>()
                        .join(",")
                )
            })
            .collect()
    }
    pub fn parameters_bits(&self) -> String {
        let roles = self.metadata().input_roles;
        self.inputs
            .iter()
            .filter(|(id, _)| roles.get(&id.index()).is_some_and(|s| s == "parameter"))
            .map(|(id, t)| {
                format!(
                    "node={} bits={}\n",
                    id.index(),
                    t.values()
                        .iter()
                        .map(|x| format!("{:08x}", x.to_bits()))
                        .collect::<Vec<_>>()
                        .join(",")
                )
            })
            .collect()
    }
    /// Independent Int forward pass over all live nodes, with checked +/-2^24
    /// integer-exact intermediate bounds. Not host f32 math.
    pub fn exact_integer_output(&self) -> Result<Vec<i64>, Box<dyn Error>> {
        use verineural::Operation;
        let mut values: Vec<Vec<i64>> = Vec::new();
        for (idx, node) in self.graph().nodes().iter().enumerate() {
            let result = match &node.operation {
                Operation::Input => {
                    let t = &self
                        .inputs
                        .iter()
                        .find(|(id, _)| id.index() == idx)
                        .ok_or("source input missing")?
                        .1;
                    t.values()
                        .iter()
                        .map(|&v| {
                            if !v.is_finite() || v < 0.0 || v.fract() != 0.0 || v > 16_777_216.0 {
                                Err("nonexact or negative source input")
                            } else {
                                Ok(v as i64)
                            }
                        })
                        .collect::<Result<Vec<_>, _>>()?
                }
                Operation::Add => {
                    let a = &values[node.inputs[0].index()];
                    let b = &values[node.inputs[1].index()];
                    a.iter()
                        .zip(b)
                        .map(|(x, y)| x.checked_add(*y).ok_or("i64 add overflow"))
                        .collect::<Result<Vec<_>, _>>()?
                }
                Operation::Mul => {
                    let a = &values[node.inputs[0].index()];
                    let b = &values[node.inputs[1].index()];
                    a.iter()
                        .zip(b)
                        .map(|(x, y)| x.checked_mul(*y).ok_or("i64 mul overflow"))
                        .collect::<Result<Vec<_>, _>>()?
                }
                Operation::BiasAdd => {
                    let a = &values[node.inputs[0].index()];
                    let b = &values[node.inputs[1].index()];
                    a.iter()
                        .enumerate()
                        .map(|(i, x)| x.checked_add(b[i % b.len()]).ok_or("i64 bias add overflow"))
                        .collect::<Result<Vec<_>, _>>()?
                }
                Operation::Relu => values[node.inputs[0].index()]
                    .iter()
                    .map(|v| (*v).max(0))
                    .collect(),
                Operation::Reshape(_) => values[node.inputs[0].index()].clone(),
                _ => return Err("unsupported lab integer operation".into()),
            };
            if result.iter().any(|&x| x.unsigned_abs() > 16_777_216) {
                return Err("lab integer operation outside exact FP32 profile".into());
            }
            values.push(result);
        }
        let output = values[self.output().index()].clone();
        if output != [4, 10, 8, 12] {
            return Err("lab oracle regression".into());
        }
        Ok(output)
    }
}

#[cfg(test)]
mod tests {
    use super::*;
    use verineural::{GpuEngine, LeanProofEngine};

    #[test]
    fn nested_architecture_has_independent_global_property_and_exact_oracle() {
        let lab = build().unwrap();
        assert_eq!(lab.graph().modules().len(), 7);
        assert_eq!(lab.graph().nodes().len(), 23);
        assert_eq!(lab.source_nodes()[3], lab.model.source("p").unwrap().0);
        assert_eq!(lab.source_nodes()[4], lab.model.source("q").unwrap().0);
        assert_eq!(lab.model.outputs().len(), 3);
        let compiler = verineural::ArchitectureAutoCompiler::new(
            LeanProofEngine::default(),
            GpuEngine::default(),
        );
        let plan = lab
            .model
            .plan(&compiler, verineural::GpuRequirement::AllOutputs)
            .unwrap();
        assert_eq!(plan.outputs.len(), 3);
        assert!(plan.outputs.contains(&lab.output()));
        assert_eq!(plan.goals.len(), 1);
        assert_eq!(plan.goals[0].0, "coupled_branch_lower_bound");
        assert!(
            plan.goals[0]
                .1
                .source()
                .contains("theorem architecture_property_coupled_branch_lower_bound")
        );
        assert!(plan.shared_gpu.is_some());
        assert_eq!(lab.exact_integer_output().unwrap(), [4, 10, 8, 12]);
        let proof = LeanProofEngine::default()
            .generate_global_nonnegative(lab.graph(), lab.output(), &lab.source_nodes())
            .unwrap();
        assert!(
            proof
                .source()
                .contains("theorem architecture_global_nonnegative")
        );
        // Each of the five input lemmas must expose exactly one used
        // hypothesis, with the remaining positional binders explicitly unused.
        for source in 0..5 {
            let marker = format!("theorem node_{source}_nonnegative ");
            let declaration = proof
                .source()
                .split(&marker)
                .nth(1)
                .expect("source nonnegativity theorem")
                .split(" := by")
                .next()
                .expect("theorem declaration");
            for hypothesis in 0..5 {
                let binder = if source == hypothesis {
                    format!("(h_{hypothesis} :")
                } else {
                    format!("(_h_{hypothesis} :")
                };
                assert!(
                    declaration.contains(&binder),
                    "node {source} binder {hypothesis}"
                );
            }
        }
        assert!(
            !proof
                .source()
                .contains("set_option linter.unusedVariables false")
        );
        let gpu = GpuEngine::default()
            .compile(lab.graph(), lab.output())
            .unwrap();
        assert!(!gpu.translation_plan().unwrap().kernels.is_empty());
        let snapshot =
            verineural::snapshot_architecture(lab.graph(), lab.output(), &gpu, &lab.metadata())
                .unwrap();
        assert_eq!(snapshot.dot.matches("subgraph cluster_m").count(), 7);
        assert!(snapshot.dot.contains(r#"vn_role="parameter""#));
        // Module port metadata is stored once per normalized module scope.
        assert_eq!(
            snapshot.dot.matches("vn_input_ports=").count(),
            lab.graph().modules().len()
        );
        assert_eq!(
            snapshot.dot.matches("vn_output_ports=").count(),
            lab.graph().modules().len()
        );
        // The renderer should draw only real IR dependencies. Port identity
        // remains in the cluster label and the explicit typed port mappings.
        let real_edges: usize = lab
            .graph()
            .nodes()
            .iter()
            .map(|node| node.inputs.len())
            .sum();
        assert_eq!(snapshot.dot.matches(" -> ").count(), real_edges);
        assert_eq!(snapshot.dot.matches("vn_semantic_dst=").count(), real_edges);
        // The first boundary module declares x, y and shared parameter p.
        // Quoted names are escaped because this metadata lives inside DOT.
        assert!(snapshot.dot.contains(
            r#"vn_input_ports="[(\"input_0\", 0), (\"input_1\", 1), (\"input_2\", 3)]""#
        ));
        assert!(!snapshot.dot.contains("module_interface"));
        assert!(!snapshot.dot.contains("module_input_port"));
        assert!(
            snapshot
                .dot
                .contains(r#"vn_output_ports="[(\"output\", 7)]""#)
        );
        assert!(
            snapshot
                .dot
                .contains(r#"label="BOUNDARY RESPONSE  ·  m0\ninput_0:n0"#)
        );
        let has_edge = |source: &str, destination: &str| {
            let prefix = format!("{source} -> {destination} [");
            snapshot
                .dot
                .lines()
                .any(|line| line.trim_start().starts_with(&prefix))
        };
        assert!(has_edge("n0", "n5"));
        assert!(has_edge("n3", "n6"));
        assert!(!has_edge("n0", "m6_in0"));
        assert!(snapshot.dot.contains("vn_semantic_src=\"n0\""));
        assert!(snapshot.dot.contains("vn_visual_src=\"n0\""));
        assert!(!snapshot.dot.contains("rank=same;"));
        assert!(snapshot.dot.contains("fillcolor=\"#FFF1DB\""));
        assert!(snapshot.dot.contains(r#"style="rounded,filled""#));
        assert!(snapshot.dot.contains("dpi=180"));
        assert!(snapshot.dot.contains("splines=spline"));
        assert!(snapshot.dot.contains("concentrate=false"));
        assert!(snapshot.dot.contains("mclimit=4"));
        assert!(!snapshot.dot.contains("headport="));
        assert!(!snapshot.dot.contains("tailport="));
        assert!(snapshot.dot.contains("constraint=\"false\""));
        assert!(snapshot.dot.contains("constraint=\"true\""));
        assert!(snapshot.dot.contains("vn_ir_sha256="));
    }

    #[test]
    fn bad_inferred_component_rolls_back_and_preserves_sources() {
        let mut model = ModelBuilder::new("bad", "1");
        let x = model.input("x", [1, 3], Domain::NonNegativeFinite).unwrap();
        let y = model.input("y", [1, 4], Domain::NonNegativeFinite).unwrap();
        let z = model.input("z", [1, 4], Domain::NonNegativeFinite).unwrap();
        let p = model
            .parameter("p", [4], Domain::NonNegativeFinite)
            .unwrap();
        let q = model
            .parameter("q", [4], Domain::NonNegativeFinite)
            .unwrap();
        assert!(matches!(
            model.block("coupled_field", &[x, y, z, p, q], coupled_field),
            Err(ModelError::Neural(NeuralError::ShapeMismatch { .. }))
        ));
        assert_eq!(model.graph_mut().modules().len(), 0);
        assert_eq!(model.graph_mut().nodes().len(), 5);
    }

    #[test]
    fn changed_parameter_must_revalidate_its_contract() {
        let mut lab = build().unwrap();
        let id = lab.inputs[3].0;
        lab.inputs[3].1 = Tensor::new(channel(), vec![-1., 0., 1., 0.]).unwrap();
        assert!(
            lab.inputs[3]
                .1
                .validate_domain(lab.graph().node(id).unwrap().domain)
                .is_err()
        );
        assert!(lab.exact_integer_output().is_err());
    }
}

